 youths far more harshly than whites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The department said Friday that the juvenile justice system in St. Louis County, Mo., treats black youths far more harshly than whites.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice Department Investigation of St. Louis County Family Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Courts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Louis County (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-01T04:27:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/3ed9255d-3cb2-551a-9610-c6186c21112e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/3ed9255d-3cb2-551a-9610-c6186c21112e'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/01/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) BIRDMAN OR (THE UNEXPECTED VIRTUE OF IGNORANCE) (2014) Riggan Thomson (Michael Keaton, in an Oscar-nominated performance), a washed-up Hollywood superhero, floats down to earth to deliver himself from his past by staging a Broadway adaptation of a Raymond Carver short story. Then a pompous theater actor (Edward Norton) comes along and threatens to steal the show. Riggan’s fresh-from-rehab daughter (Emma Stone) has taken on the role of his assistant. Writing in The New York Times, A. O. Scott called this best-picture winner “a funny, frenetic, buoyant and rambunctiously showboating entertainment” in which the director Alejandro G. Iñárritu “himself rises high and then higher still.” Riggan, Mr. Scott added, “isn’t the only man on the move: So is Mr. Iñárritu, who has staged and shot the movie so that it looks like everything that happens, from airborne beginning to end, occurs during one transporting continuous take. The camera doesn’t just move with the story and characters, it also ebbs and flows like water, soars and swoops like a bird, its movement as fluid as a natural element, as animated as a living organism.” Mr. Iñárritu won the Oscar for best director, and Emmanuel Lubezki for cinematography.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-01T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/3173f96a-3c82-5f2a-826e-b8bdf320b364', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3173f96a-3c82-5f2a-826e-b8bdf320b364'}, {'abstract': 'Runggye Adak was jailed for eight years after calling for the spiritual leader’s return to Tibet in a speech at a major festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/world/asia/tibetan-who-called-for-dalai-lamas-return-is-said-to-be-freed-from-chinese-prison.html', 'snippet': 'Runggye Adak was jailed for eight years after calling for the spiritual leader’s return to Tibet in a speech at a major festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — A Tibetan man who was imprisoned for eight years after calling for the Dalai Lama’s return to Tibet at a popular festival has been released, according to overseas Tibet advocacy groups.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tibetan Who Called for Dalai Lama’s Return Is Said to Be Freed From Chinese Prison', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tibetan Man Is Said to Be Freed From Chinese Prison ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wong, Edward (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalai Lama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tenzin Delek Rinpoche (1950-2015)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-01T05:07:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74b110a2-9ebe-577e-945b-9532edb3ad72', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74b110a2-9ebe-577e-945b-9532edb3ad72'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, August 1, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/01/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, August 1, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“But maybe everything that dies someday comes back. Maybe Asbury Park is back?”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_