rd', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3BOX/3BOX-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3BOX/3BOX-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'R-Rated Comedies, ‘Vacation’ Among Them, Continue to Struggle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'R-Rated Comedies Lag in Sales ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Parental Guidance)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Vacation (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-02T21:06:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3c1e193-4cbf-5330-9dc6-d2713e8ad968', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3c1e193-4cbf-5330-9dc6-d2713e8ad968'}, {'abstract': 'Her performance comes from the incisiveness, colorings and inflections of her singing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/03/arts/music/review-cecilia-bartoli-has-dramatic-depth-as-norma-at-salzburg-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Her performance comes from the incisiveness, colorings and inflections of her singing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALZBURG, Austria — During the mid-1990s, when Cecilia Bartoli was known for scintillating performances of roles like Rossini’s Cenerentola (Cinderella), the suggestion that this light-voiced mezzo-soprano might take on the daunting title role of Bellini’s “Norma” someday would have seemed absurd. Maria Callas had defined the role for late 20th-century audiences as a supreme test for a fiercely intense, formidable soprano. Some powerhouse mezzo-sopranos, like Shirley Verrett and Grace Bumbry, had made the leap. But a perky Cinderella singing Norma? No way.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3NORMA/3NORMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3NORMA/3NORMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3NORMA/3NORMA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3NORMA/3NORMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3NORMA/3NORMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3NORMA/3NORMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3NORMA/3NORMA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Cecilia Bartoli Has Dramatic Depth as ‘Norma’ at Salzburg Festival', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking Command of a Daunting Role', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salzburg Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leiser, Moshe (1956- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caurier, Patrice (1954- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Antonini, Giovanni (1965- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orchestra la Scintilla', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coro Della Radiotelevisione Svizzera', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salzburg (Austria)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartoli, Cecilia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Norma (Opera)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-02T21:09:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4261602b-67d8-53f1-a09e-9f45aa77ad26', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4261602b-67d8-53f1-a09e-9f45aa77ad26'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Oberlin’s show at Stage 72 at the Triad celebrates Mr. Costello’s work as a cryptic genre unto itself, a code to be cracked or not.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/03/arts/music/review-karen-oberlins-his-aim-is-true-a-tribute-to-elvis-costello.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Oberlin’s show at Stage 72 at the Triad celebrates Mr. Costello’s work as a cryptic genre unto itself, a code to be cracked or not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Karen Oberlin’s extensively researched, beautifully executed tribute to the music of Elvis Costello answers a question that has been gnawing at me for years: Why have so few of Mr. Costello’s songs achieved the status of modern standards? For all this time, I had assumed that his raw, unwelcoming voice, with its strangulated diction, was the reason. Surely, a better-equipped singer could untangle his knotty lyrics and sharpen the melodic profiles of songs that Mr. Costello presented as impassioned downbeat mystery stories.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3OBERLIN/3OBERLIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3OBERLIN/3OBERLIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3OBERLIN/3OBERLIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3OBERLIN/3OBERLIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1287, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3OBERLIN/3OBERLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3OBERLIN/3OBERLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/arts/3OBERLIN/3OBERLIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'heigh