rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a411f8be-c6d2-5341-bf52-83f43e503126', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a411f8be-c6d2-5341-bf52-83f43e503126'}, {'abstract': 'This week the Athens Stock Exchange reopens, several of Europe’s biggest banks will report their first-half results, and Tesla Motors will announce its second-quarter earnings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/03/business/greeces-market-reopens-european-banks-report-results-and-tesla-announces-earnings.html', 'snippet': 'This week the Athens Stock Exchange reopens, several of Europe’s biggest banks will report their first-half results, and Tesla Motors will announce its second-quarter earnings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Athens Stock Exchange reopened on Monday after a five-week closure that followed a decision by the Greek authorities to shut Greek banks and impose capital controls. The banks reopened two weeks ago, though restrictions on cash transactions remain in place to avert a run on the banks’ deposits. To prevent capital flight, a mass sell-off of holdings and a market crash, there is a cap on stock fluctuations and restrictions on local traders, though foreign investors will face no constraints when stock trading resumes. The reopening of Greece’s market comes as government officials and representatives of the country’s international creditors enter a second week of difficult negotiations on a multibillion-euro bailout, Greece’s third in five years. —Niki Kitsantonis', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/03/business/03Ahead/03Ahead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 848, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/03/business/03Ahead/03Ahead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 848}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 