64f8fc05286'}, {'abstract': 'On St. Lawrence Island, a former military listening post in the Bering Sea, native residents believe pollution has contributed to their poor health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/us/native-alaskans-study-and-clean-up-a-legacy-of-pollution.html', 'snippet': 'On St. Lawrence Island, a former military listening post in the Bering Sea, native residents believe pollution has contributed to their poor health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LAWRENCE ISLAND, Alaska — America’s Far North cherishes its image of wild purity in a landscape so vast it can sometimes seem barely touched by people. But the roughly 600 military installations across Alaska — some dating from World War II, others built during the Cold War — tell a different story, in polluted sites that were never fully cleaned up, and in the related health problems that have lingered and festered.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleaning Up a Legacy of Pollution on an Alaskan Island', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cleaning Up a Legacy of Pollution on an Alaskan Island ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Lawrence Island (Alaska)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PCB (Polychlorinated Biphenyls)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-03T09:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person