 executive of Gravity Payments, a credit card processing company, decided to raise the salary of his lowest paid workers to $70,000. Almost overnight, he represented a swashbuckling blow against income inequality. He also drew no small amount of criticism.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If You Were the Boss, Would You Raise the Minimum Salary to $70,000?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Price, Daniel J (1984- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gravity Payments Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-03T18:46:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9b9eab3-436b-5883-b1a9-89d95803e623', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9b9eab3-436b-5883-b1a9-89d95803e623'}, {'abstract': 'Smokeless tobacco, a staple of players for more than a century, will be banned from San Francisco’s AT&T Park at the beginning of next year, and more venues are likely to follow suit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/sports/baseball/a-baseball-habit-begins-to-feel-the-pinch.html', 'snippet': 'Smokeless tobacco, a staple of players for more than a century, will be banned from San Francisco’s AT&T Park at the beginning of next year, and more venues are likely to follow suit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Most days he is at work at AT&T Park here, Giants pitcher Madison Bumga