seeks to spotlight the use of handcuffs to restrain young children who act out in school.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The American Civil Liberties Union, seeking to spotlight the use of handcuffs to restrain young children who act out in school, filed a federal lawsuit in Covington, Ky., on Monday alleging that a school resource officer there shackled an 8-year-old boy and a 9-year-old girl, both with disabilities, causing the children “pain, fear and emotional trauma.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.C.L.U. Sues Over Handcuffing of Boy, 8, and Girl, 9, in Kentucky School', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A.C.L.U. Sues Over Handcuffing of Boy, 8, and Girl, 9, in Kentucky School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stolberg, Sheryl Gay (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T00:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d28d779-edc4-5c4f-946f-579732721be2', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d28d779-edc4-5c4f-946f-579732721be2'}, {'abstract': 'Obama is sending a signal that low-carbon energy will be profitable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/opinion/a-climate-plan-businesses-can-like.html', 'snippet': 'Obama is sending a signal that low-carbon energy will be profitable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH the release of President Obama’s Clean Power Plan, a flood of legal challenges will begin. Already, opponents have denounced the new rule limiting carbon pollution as unconstitutional. Behind the rattling sabers, however, there’s a quieter story worth noticing. Many big players in the electric power industry will gain more with the rule in place than if the courts strike it down.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Climate Plan Businesses Can Like', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Climate Plan Businesses Can Like', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeman, Jody', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Konschnik, Kate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'p