en jeopardize his tenure as the state’s top lawyer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04texas-sub/04texas-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 383, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04texas-sub/04texas-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 383, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04texas-sub/04texas-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04texas-sub/04texas-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04texas-sub/04texas-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Securities Fraud Charges Bring Texas Attorney General, Ken Paxton, to County Jail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Securities Fraud Charges Bring Texas Attorney General to County Jail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Manny (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paxton, Ken', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attorneys General', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T00:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c31cd391-6968-56d4-9ee5-a2879c104e5c', 'word_count': 1193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c31cd391-6968-56d4-9ee5-a2879c104e5c'}, {'abstract': 'The Treasury Department’s Office of Foreign Assets Control said seven commercial ships had been blocked by its action, cutting off a potential fuel source to Assad’s military.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/world/middleeast/syria-us-sets-new-sanctions.html', 'snippet': 'The Treasury Department’s Office of Foreign Assets Control said seven commercial ships had been blocked by its action, cutting off a potential fuel source to Assad’s military.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States sought to broaden its economic pressure on Syria’s government on Monday, imposing sanctions on a far-flung network of seven overseas companies and four individuals for actions to evade American and European Union restrictions on fuel imports. The Treasury Department’s Office of Foreign Assets Control, which oversees enforcement of American sanctions, said seven commercial ships owned or controlled by one of the newly penalized companies had been blocked by its action, cutting off a potential source of fuel to President Bashar al-Assad’s military. The affected companies operated in Syria, the United Arab Emirates, Turkey, Lebanon, Panama, St. Kitts and Nevis and the Marshall Islands, the Treasury said in a statement, asserting that “many of these entities are front companies that the government of Syria and its supporters have used in an attempt to evade U.S. and E.U. sanctions.” Any sanctioned individuals and entities risk seizure of assets under American jurisdiction, and are barred from commercial dealings with the United States.  ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria: U.S. Sets New Sanctions', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Syria: U.S. Sets New Sanctions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Foreign Assets Control (United States Treasury)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T00:44:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5d725d4-a208-5d45-a471-83c986cd7613', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5d725d4-a208-5d45-a471-83c986cd7613'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Marotta, who once played football professionally and signed with an M.L.B. team, created a coffee maker that knocked the percolator from its perch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/business/vincent-marotta-sr-a-creator-of-mr-coffee-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Marotta, who once played football professionally and signed with an M.L.B. team, created a coffee maker that knocked the percolator from its perch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vincent Marotta Sr., who as a creator of the Mr. Coffee machine helped send the percolator the way of the one-horse shay, died on Saturday at his home in Pepper Pike, Ohio. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/business/04marotta-1-obit/04marotta-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/04/business/04marotta-1-obit/04marotta-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/business/04marotta-1-obit/04marotta-1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/business/04marotta-1-obit/04marotta-1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1175, 'width': 881, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/business/04marotta-1-obit/04marotta-1-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/04/business/04marotta-1-obit/04marotta-1-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/business/04marotta-1-obit/04marotta-1-obit-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vincent Marotta Sr., a Crea