oices for his bars, from Clyde Common in Downtown Portland to his latest venture, the Up & Up, on New York’s Macdougal Street. “This stuff” is Piacentini’s shorthand for the goods he found easily accessible back in Europe that he wants to bring stateside: everything from William Morris wallpapers and Italian amari to Scandinavian aquavit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04brennivin-nichols-1/04brennivin-nichols-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04brennivin-nichols-1/04brennivin-nichols-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04brennivin-nichols-1/04brennivin-nichols-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04brennivin-nichols-1/04brennivin-nichols-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04brennivin-nichols-1/04brennivin-nichols-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04brennivin-nichols-1/04brennivin-nichols-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04brennivin-nichols-1/04brennivin-nichols-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Refreshing Cocktail Recipe, Featuring Iceland’s Newest Export', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Nichols', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nichols', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e5e9118-9e64-55ac-9b40-aa0dc78962c5', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e5e9118-9e64-55ac-9b40-aa0dc78962c5'}, {'abstract': "Evangelia Koutsovoulou created Daphnis and Chloe, a store under the Acropolis, to source and celebrate her home country's thyme flowers, bay leaves and more.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/t-magazine/daphnis-chloe-greek-herbs.html', 'snippet': "Evangelia Koutsovoulou created Daphnis and Chloe, a store under the Acropolis, to source and celebrate her home country's thyme flowers, bay leaves and more.", 'lead_paragraph': 'Among a generation of young Greeks scattered around the more prosperous cities of Europe, Evangelia Koutsovoulou is an anomaly: an émigré who last year returned to Athens with opportunity on her mind. The sage- and mint-perfumed islands of her Mediterranean homeland are rich in herbs, unchanged and mostly uncultivated since ancient times with a world of unique flavors not found elsewhere, even in her adopted country of Italy. “Greek herbs were something very special but no one else had paid any attention to them,” says the former journalist, who opened her tiny headquarters below the Acropolis in the midst of the country’s economic crisis and created Daphnis and Chloe, a brand of wild-bred culinary herbs named after a second-century Greek tale of predestined love.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04symonds-herbs2/04symonds-herbs2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04symonds-herbs2/04symonds-herbs2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04symonds-herbs2/04symonds-herbs2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04symonds-herbs2/04symonds-herbs2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04symonds-herbs2/04symonds-herbs2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04symonds-herbs2/04symonds-herbs2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04symonds-herbs2/04symonds-herbs2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One-Thing Shops: Herbs in Athens', 'kicker': 'One Thing Shops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ancient Greek Herbs, Foraged for the Modern Chef', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Herbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocat