ons', 'value': 'Warner Music Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birthdays', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Jennifer (Filmmaker)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T14:16:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a30b94f9-0048-577c-b1c1-af7278a1c983', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a30b94f9-0048-577c-b1c1-af7278a1c983'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: U.S. peace mission fails in Haiti in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/1915-peace-mission-fails-in-haiti/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: U.S. peace mission fails in Haiti in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — A special cablegram to the Herald from Port-au-Prince says the mission of the Peace Committee has completely failed. The Cape army refused to fight. Governor Blot and his staff secretly fled during the night aboard a Haitian gunboat, while the population shouted ‘‘Vive Bobo.’’ The garrison of 1,500 was disarmed. Later the American warships Eagle and Nashville landed 250 sailors. Bobo’s army then tried to force the city gates despite the interdiction of the United States naval commanders. The Eagle then shelled the army. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 5, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Peace Mission Fails in Haiti', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War and Revolution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Woodrow', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T14:22:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27e7d585-78c4-5f53-b0fd-1b8ba0410f2d', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27e7d585-78c4-5f53-b0fd-1b8ba0410f2d'}, {'abstract': 'Donald Trump has a weapon against his Republican rivals should they attack him in a debate. He can recount how many of them graciously accepted his money in the past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/08/04/donald-trump-debate-weapon-checks-written-to-his-rivals/', 'snippet': 'Donald Trump has a weapon against his Republican rivals should they attack him in a debate. He can recount how many of them graciously accepted his money in the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Favors are not free in business or politics and Donald J. Trump will have his ledger ready if the insults start flying his way at Thursday’s debate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/politics/04firstdraft-trump2/04firstdraft-trump2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/04/us/politics/04firstdraft-trump2/04firstdraft-trump2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':