, 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f5a56de4-0195-5901-84c7-1a24959b3bcf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f5a56de4-0195-5901-84c7-1a24959b3bcf'}, {'abstract': 'A decade later, the city is arguably a better place to eat than it was before the storm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/dining/new-orleans-restaurants-post-hurricane-katrina.html', 'snippet': 'A decade later, the city is arguably a better place to eat than it was before the storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — On a brutally humid day almost 10 years ago, Donald Link was a sweaty, desperate man in a respirator mask lugging a rotting pig’s head to the curb.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Orleans Restaurant Bounce, After Katrina', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Culinary Feat for New Orleans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Severson, Kim (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Katrina (2005)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Link, Donald', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Besh, John (1968- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T16:21:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37691f67-b7a9-5df0-a8d0-b67a67349272', 'word_count': 1719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37691f67-b7a9-5df0-a8d0-b67a67349272'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Greek lawmakers take part in a vote of confidence in the government in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/1965-greek-lawmakers-vote/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Greek lawmakers take part in a vote of confidence in the government in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Parliament met for a showdown vote on the nation’s political crisis tonight [Aug. 4], with observers giving the three- week-old government only a slim chance of success. Shouts and interruptions rang out across the assembly as soon as debate got under way. A vote of confidence in the administration of Premier George Athanasiades-Novas was expected to be held early tomorrow morning. In the lobbies, the predominant opinion was that Mr. Athanasiades-Novas has little chance of mustering a majority of the 300 deputies. At least 143 deputies belonging to the Center Union party are pledged to support former Premier George Papandreou. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, August 5, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Greek Lawmakers Vote', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Papandreou, George A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T16:32:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95552cfc-47af-594d-a841-96c3941c5ab2', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95552cfc-47af-594d-a841-96c3941c5ab2'}, {'abstract': 'It seems like the Republican presidential candidate was just flailing around for attention.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/lindsey-graham-hillary-clinton-monica-lewinsky-a-case-study-in-desperation/', 'snippet': 'It seems like the Republican presidential candidate was just flailing around for attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You would think that a struggling (to be charitable) presidential candidate would think about his words on a day when it had just been revealed by the Washington Post that his much bragged-on record in the military reserve was wildly overblown. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lindsey Graham, Hillary Clinton, Monica Lewinsky: A Case Study in Desperation', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Lindsey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewinsky, Monica S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T16:34:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/495d94de-9391-50ae-9147-f5abc48813b3', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/495d94de-9391-50ae-9147-f5abc48813b3'}, {'abstract': 'The New Yorker article comes nearly a year after Mr. Wilson, a white former police officer, fatally shot Michael Brown, an unarmed black teenager, in Ferguson, Mo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/us/new-yorker-ferguson-darren-wilson-michael-brown.html', 'snippet': 'The New Yorker article comes nearly a year after Mr. Wilson, a white former police officer, fatally shot Michael Brown, an unarmed black teenager, in Ferguson, Mo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Darren Wilson, the police officer who fatally shot an unarmed black teenager almost a year ago, now lives on a dead-end street on the outskirts of St. Louis. His name is not on the deed of the house. He wears a hat and sunglasses when he goes outside to greet a reporter, having synced his phone with a security system to tip him off to his visitor’s arrival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/us/05WILSONWEB/05WILSONWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/05/us/05WILSONWEB/05WILSONWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/us/05WILSONWEB/05WILSONWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/us/05WILSONWEB/05WILSONWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/us/05WILSONWEB/05WILSONWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width':