t': 'Looking at how many times a candidate’s Twitter handle or name has been mentioned on the social platform over the past 30 days, Twitter has come up with a top 10 list of their own for the Republican field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/08/04/the-twitter-primary-who-makes-the-top-10/', 'snippet': 'Looking at how many times a candidate’s Twitter handle or name has been mentioned on the social platform over the past 30 days, Twitter has come up with a top 10 list of their own for the Republican field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Fox News determines exactly who will make the cut for the first Republican presidential debate on Thursday, the data team at Twitter has compiled a similar list. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04firstdraft-twitter/04firstdraft-twitter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04firstdraft-twitter/04firstdraft-twitter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04firstdraft-twitter/04firstdraft-twitter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04firstdraft-twitter/04firstdraft-twitter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04firstdraft-twitter/04firstdraft-twitter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04firstdraft-twitter/04firstdraft-twitter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/us/04firstdraft-twitter/04firstdraft-twitter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Twitter Primary: Who Makes the Top 10', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T20:02:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1772e25-1371-50a6-9a1d-e508e95700ae', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1772e25-1371-50a6-9a1d-e508e95700ae'}, {'abstract': 'A handful of new serums and oils promise to protect locks from sun damage.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/hair-protection-sun/', 'snippet': 'A handful of new serums and oils promise to protect locks from sun damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the summer, protecting one’s hair from the sun isn’t always a top priority, with so much attention and energy paid to safeguarding the skin. But as anyone who’s seen blond turn to brass knows, the sun can do long-lasting damage to one’s locks. Luckily, there are a handful of products on the market to protect against it: Last summer, the Stockholm-based brand Sachajuan launched a leave-in serum that protects the hair from ultraviolet rays; earlier this year, the French colorist Christophe Robin released a treatment (with SPF 6) infused with lavender and plant oils to strengthen it before sun exposure. Elsewhere, Phyto introduced five\xa0oils in a single bottle as an after-sun mist to renew hair fibers and Davines relaunched its SU line in a four-product range, all with antioxidant and anti-inflammatory benefits. Even the 58-year-old hair-care company René Furterer added three new products to its already-established sun protection line, Soleil. But our favorite of the bunch is a sun-specific hair-repair shampoo, formulated with jojoba wax, that prevents strands from dehydration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04sun-mosci/04sun-mosci-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04sun-mosci/04sun-mosci-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04sun-mosci/04sun-mosci-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04sun-mosci/04sun-mosci-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04sun-mosci/04sun-mosci-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04sun-mosci/04sun-mosci-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/t-magazine/04sun-mosci/04sun-mosci-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hair Protection From the Sun, One Spritz (or Pump) at a Time', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sun', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ultraviolet Light', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T20:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Renata Mosci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Renata', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mosci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00a4f174-84d4-5360-89ac-80a3a54b7aab', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00a4f174-84d4-5360-89ac-80a3a54b7aab'}, {'abstract': 'Do Americans who are upset about Cecil even realize how terrifying animals can be?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/opinion/in-zimbabwe-we-dont-cry-for-lions.html', 'snippet': 'Do Americans who are upset about Cecil even realize how te