ng like an unblemished, shiny, just-picked zucchini, whatever the size (well, perhaps not those great, great big ones).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zucchini Two Ways', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zucchini', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-04T21:08:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3914af00-f0ad-529f-9d07-59590fb53433', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3914af00-f0ad-529f-9d07-59590fb53433'}, {'abstract': 'Indian-spiced corn soup and corn-jalapeño muffins go beyond corn on the cob.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/08/05/dining/corn.html', 'snippet': 'Indian-spiced corn soup and corn-jalapeño muffins go beyond corn on the cob.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Indian-spiced corn soup and corn-jalapeño muffins go beyond corn on the cob.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/dining/CORN-slide-S6G3/CORN-slide-S6G3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/05/dining/CORN-slide-S6G3/CORN-slide-S6G3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/dining/CORN-slide-S6G3/CORN-slide-S