” in text messages and emails between two lawyers, a federal judge scrapped a proposed $75 million settlement between American Express and a group of retailers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It sounded like an innocuous message: “Amex negotiation has gotten crazy,” Gary Friedman, representing merchants in a lawsuit against American Express, said in a text message to his friend and fellow lawyer Keila Ravelo two years ago. “Gmailed u the issue.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Rejects Settlement in American Express Case ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Rejects Settlement in American Express Case ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MasterCard Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Visa Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T00:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66c0ac13-6309-5da8-b648-3895f63bbf91', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66c0ac13-6309-5da8-b648-3895f63bbf91'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary General Ban Ki-moon beseeched donors on Tuesday to fill an emergency $100 million gap in funding for the agency that aids five million Palestinian refugees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/world/middleeast/un-chief-appeals-for-more-aid-to-support-palestinian-refugees.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary General Ban Ki-moon beseeched donors on Tuesday to fill an emergency $100 million gap in funding for the agency that aids five million Palestinian refugees.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Secretary General Ban Ki-moon of the United Nations beseeched donors on Tuesday to fill an emergency $100 million gap in funding for the agency that aids five million Palestinian refugees in the Middle East. In a statement, Mr. Ban said the shortfall confronting the United Nations Relief and Works Agency was unprecedented and risked disrupting the education of a half-million children. Many United Nations agencies are under severe financial pressure because of emergency efforts to help people displaced by the conflicts in Syria, Iraq and Yemen. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Chief Appeals for More Aid to Support Palestinian Refugees', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; U.N. Chief Appeals for More Aid to Support Palestinian Refugees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Relief and Works Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T01:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbddd5b6-4e49-55ad-b185-30229089d106', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbddd5b6-4e49-55ad-b185-30229089d106'}, {'abstract': 'The aid agencies, including the W.H.O., need $60.9 million to operate their health care centers in Iraq but have received only $5.1 million from donors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/world/middleeast/iraq-funding-shortfall-deprives-uprooted-iraqis-of-health-services.html', 'snippet': 'The aid agencies, including the W.H.O., need $60.9 million to operate their health care centers in Iraq but have received only $5.1 million from donors.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Faced with a shortage of funds, international aid agencies have been forced to suspend 84 percent of their health programs in 10 Iraqi provinces, depriving almost three million people of basic medical care, World Health Organization officials said Tuesday. The aid agencies, including the W.H.O., need $60.9 million to operate their health care centers in Iraq but have received only $5.1 million from donors. More than 184 centers serving refugees and other people displaced by violence in Iraq have suspended their operations, the W.H.O. said. The centers were the only health care providers in many parts of Iraq. “This is a country ravaged by conflict,” said Dr. Syed Jaffar Hussain, the W.H.O. representative in Iraq. “Not only do we have innocent civilians being caught in the violence, with so many people fleeing the fighting and living in temporary housing, people are at much higher risk from communicable diseases. Unless additional funding is received, millions more will be deprived of health services they urgently need.” The W.H.O. said it was appealing to international donors and seeking alternative sources of funding. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Funding Shortfall Deprives Uprooted Iraqis of Health Services', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Iraq: Funding Shortfall Deprives Uprooted Iraqis of Health Services', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jawoshy, Omar Al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T01:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Omar Al-Jawoshy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Omar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Al-Jawoshy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1882bd83-3ec1-5338-bbe5-64b3396d6dd6', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1882bd83-3ec1-5338-bbe5-64b3396d6dd6'}, {'abstract': 'At least 17 states will temporarily exempt state sales tax (and, in some cases, local sales taxes) for shoppers buying school supplies, clothing and other school needs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/business/catch-a-back-to-school-spending-break-with-sales-tax-holidays.html', 'snippet': 'At least 17 states will temporarily exempt state sales tax (and, in some cases, local sales taxes) for shoppers buying school supplies, clothing and other school needs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'August is time for back-to-school shopping — and, in many states, that means so-called sales-tax holidays as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catch a Back-to-School Spending Break With Sales-Tax Holidays', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T01:13:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'tit