eball Advanced Media will pay the National Hockey League $100 million annually starting next year to operate the NHL.com website, and the NHL Network will also distribute out-of-market games online through NHL GameCenter Live and through television providers on NHL Center Ice.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'M.L.B. Advanced Media Joins With N.H.L. in Unusual Intersport Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sports Briefing | Sports Media; Major League Dealings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandomir, Richard (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NHL Network', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T01:41:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2fa031c-6fd6-5ceb-964a-7c4aa3bff5ee', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2fa031c-6fd6-5ceb-964a-7c4aa3bff5ee'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday, Joel Fowler, who was found guilty of murder in 2009, became the latest person to have a conviction overturned since Kenneth P. Thompson became the borough’s district attorney in 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/nyregion/another-exoneration-in-brooklyn-brings-total-since-last-year-to-14.html', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, Joel Fowler, who was found guilty of murder in 2009, became the latest person to have a conviction overturned since Kenneth P. Thompson became the borough’s district attorney in 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joel Fowler wore his green, prison-issued clothes for the last time on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Exoneration in Brooklyn Brings Total Since Last Year to 14', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exoneration in Brooklyn Is 14th of District Attorney&#8217;s Term', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Colleen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Kenneth P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hynes, Charles J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Witnesses', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T01:49:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colleen Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colleen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df241f13-6cad-56a1-9c51-ddda9ec0203f', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df241f13-6cad-56a1-9c51-ddda9ec0203f'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick Berry comes up with some interesting alibis. Sorry, I mean clues.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/04/fruits-at-an-oasis/', 'snippet': 'Patrick Berry comes up with some interesting alibis. Sorry, I mean clues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY PUZZLE — If you’ve been reading Wordplay for a while, you will know that I firmly believe that the themes in some of the crosswords published here are subliminal messages from the constructors or, if they’ve been doing this for many years, an occasional cry for help. Today, we have a call for help from Patrick Berry, who has apparently landed himself in prison.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fruit at an Oasis', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T02:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48452589-5f1b-518d-890d-e5e32188b497', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48452589-5f1b-518d-890d-e5e32188b497'}, {'abstract': 'The county sheriff in Covington on Tuesday defended a school resource officer who was shown on a video restraining an 8-year-old boy with handcuffs last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/us/kentucky-sheriff-defends-officer-shown-handcuffing-child-in-video.html', 'snippet': 'The county sheriff in Covington on Tuesday defended a school resource officer who was shown on a video restraining an 8-year-old boy with handcuffs last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The county sheriff in Covington on Tuesday defended a school resource officer who was shown on a video restraining an 8-year-old boy with handcuffs last year, saying the officer had acted appropriately while responding to a request from school officials to “de-escalate and defuse a threat to others.” The handcuffing is the subject of a federal lawsuit filed Monday by the American Civil Liberties Union against the Kenton County sheriff’s office, Sheriff Charles L. Korzenborn and the resource officer, Deputy Kevin Sumner; a video shows the boy, who has attention hyperactivity deficit disorder and had been acting out in school, crying as Deputy Sumner holds his arms behind his back and places handcuffs on his biceps. In a statement, Sheriff Korzenborn said the deputy “did what he is sworn to do and in conformity with all constitutional and law enforcement standards.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kentucky: Sheriff Defends Officer Shown Handcuffing Child in Video', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kentucky: Sheriff Defends Officer Shown Handcuffing Child in Video', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stolberg, Sheryl Gay (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sumner, Kevin R (1970- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Covington (Ky)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T02:01:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_