{'abstract': 'The final score notwithstanding, it was not as comfortable an evening as it might have been for the Yankees, who blew the game open with a nine-run seventh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/sports/baseball/mccann-and-teixeira-help-yankees-unleash-floodgates-against-red-sox.html', 'snippet': 'The final score notwithstanding, it was not as comfortable an evening as it might have been for the Yankees, who blew the game open with a nine-run seventh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The way the Yankees are swinging the bats, pounding pitchers and racking up runs, as they did again Tuesday night in a 13-3 win over the Boston Red Sox, they do more than overwhelm opponents.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/05/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/05/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/05/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees’ Surging Offense Makes Up for Imperfections in Rout of Red Sox', 'kicker': 'Yankees 13, Red Sox 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surging Offense Makes Up for the Imperfections in a Shellacking of Boston ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCann, Brian (1984- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teixeira, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Betances, Dellin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Justin (1987- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T03:04:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb24e618-c25f-5679-83c8-ef635c653573', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb24e618-c25f-5679-83c8-ef635c653573'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cheuse, a late-blooming author, assimilated his wide range of experiences to give authentic first-person voices to his characters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/books/alan-cheuse-author-and-npr-book-critic-dies-at-75.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cheuse, a late-blooming author, assimilated his wide range of experiences to give authentic first-person voices to his characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alan Cheuse, a late-blooming author who published his first short story just before his 40th birthday and went on to write two dozen books, but who became even better known as a longtime book critic for NPR, died on July 31 in San Jose, Calif. He was 75.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/arts/04cheuse-obit-web/04cheuse-obit-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/04/arts/04cheuse-obit-web/04cheuse-obit-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 832}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/arts/04cheuse-obit-web/04cheuse-obit-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/arts/04cheuse-obit-web/04cheuse-obit-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1913, 'width': 1379, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/arts/04cheuse-obit-web/04cheuse-obit-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/04/arts/04cheuse-obit-web/04cheuse-obit-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/04/arts/04cheuse-obit-web/04cheuse-obit-web-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alan Cheuse, Late-Blooming Author and NPR Book Critic, Dies at 75', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alan Cheuse, 75, an Author Hungry for Experiences', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheuse, Alan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T03:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/803c644b-898c-5c38-8212-ec32e82564d4', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/803c644b-898c-5c38-8212-ec32e82564d4'}, {'abstract': 'Crispy canard and crisp rieslings convene.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/t-magazine/byob-peking-duck-feast.html', 'snippet': 'Crispy canard and crisp rieslings convene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Thursday, Chinatown blazed in a noontime swelter as some of the city’s top sommeliers filed into the Peking Duck House on Mott Street. Each had a thing or two tucked under his or her arm — bottles of wine from their personal collections. Michael Madrigale, Bar Boulud’s head sommelier, entered with a 2007 Albert Boxler Riesling Grand Cru Brand ($50). Ashley Santoro, the wine director at Narcissa, came with a 1974 Francesco Rinaldi & Figli Barolo from Piedmont, Italy (about $115 retail). Patrick Cappiello was waiting for the sommeliers — eight, in all — with a magnum of Savart Premier Cru L’Accomplie Brut Champagne ($80). As the wine director for Rebelle and Pearl & Ash, sister restaurants on Bowery, Cappiello convenes these impromptu lunches about once a month, whenever the time allows. There are only two rules: Bring an intriguing bottle of wine; and keep it to around $100 each.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A B.Y.O.B. Peking Duck Feast With Some of New York’s Top Sommeliers', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edna Ishayik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ishayik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d66019c-aa1e-52a8-a621-a3db47ae408e', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d66019c-aa1e-52a8-a621-a3db47ae408e'}, {'abstract': 'The company, which specializes in communications for emergency workers, has taken a $1 billion investment from the private equity firm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/business/motorola-solutions-chooses-silver-lake-to-help-fund-transition-away-from-radios.html', 'snippet': 'The company, which specializes in communications for emergency workers, has taken a $1 billion investment from the private equity firm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Motorola Solutions has been the target of several prominent investors over the years, notably the activists Carl C. Icahn and ValueAct Capital.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Motorola Solutions Chooses Silver Lake to Help Fund Transition A