i': 'nyt://article/1165a770-54fa-50ce-962f-a740d7cca3d2'}, {'abstract': 'A Berkeley zoologist writes, “Neither tourism nor hunting returns enough money to local people to make up for the depredations of wildlife.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/opinion/the-tragedies-in-the-story-of-cecil-the-lion.html', 'snippet': 'A Berkeley zoologist writes, “Neither tourism nor hunting returns enough money to local people to make up for the depredations of wildlife.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tragedies in the Story of Cecil the Lion', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Tragedies in the Story of Cecil the Lion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T07:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d4e58c6-1b78-55da-9301-a2a2640fb471', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d4e58c6-1b78-55da-9301-a2a2640fb471'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration should accept a judge’s order by doing the right thing: end the detainment of hundreds of immigrant women and children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/opinion/a-judges-rebuke-of-immigration-detention.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration should accept a judge’s order by doing the right thing: end the detainment of hundreds of immigrant women and children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Children do not belong in prison. The mass detention of families offends American values, a lesson this country learned long ago at Manzanar, Tule Lake, Heart Mountain and the other Japanese-American internment camps of World War II.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Judge’s Rebuke of Immigration Detention', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rebuke of Immigration Detention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gee, Dolly M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T07:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/16a3596a-3113-576c-817b-0e3b02dbab50', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16a3596a-3113-576c-817b-0e3b02dbab50'}, {'abstract': 'I’d certainly pay a nickel for the candidates’ thoughts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/opinion/thomas-friedman-my-question-for-the-republican-presidential-debate.html', 'snippet': 'I’d certainly pay a nickel for the candidates’ thoughts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If I got to ask one question of the presidential aspirants at Thursday’s Fox Republican debate, it would be this: “As part of a 1982 transportation bill, President Ronald Reagan agreed to boost the then 4-cent-a-gallon gasoline tax to 9 cents, saying, ‘When we first built our highways, we paid for them with a gas tax,’ adding, ‘It was a fair concept then, and it is today.’ Do you believe Reagan was right then, and would you agree to raise the gasoline tax by 5 cents a gallon today so we can pay for our highway bill, which is now stalled in Congress over funding?”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Question for the Republican Presidential Debate', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My G.O.P. Debate Question  ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gasoline Tax (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Thomas L (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Highway Trust Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T07:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/32b65e7c-b586-52e2-ad31-6b9b26698c3a', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32b65e7c-b586-52e2-ad31-6b9b26698c3a'}, {'abstract': 'The promise of integration vs. the reality of segregation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/opinion/where-should-a-poor-family-live.html', 'snippet': 'The promise of integration vs. the reality of segregation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If its goal is to move up the ladder, where should a poor family live? Should federal dollars go toward affordable housing within high-poverty neighborhoods, or should subsidies be used to move residents of impoverished communities into more upscale – and more resistant — sections of cities and suburbs with better schools and job opportunities?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/edsall-circular/edsall-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {