rren Wilson, shot an unarmed black teenager, Michael Brown, on a street in that suburb of St. Louis. One year later, the word “Ferguson” has become indelibly linked to the charged conversation about racial justice in the United States. Like many Americans, I followed the case and ensuing protests, absorbing a barrage of commentary from news sources and my social networks. And yet as the months wore on, and the officer was not indicted, I realized that I (perhaps like many others), was never clear on the details: What exactly happened in Ferguson the day Mr. Brown was shot?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Verbatim: The Ferguson Case’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Darren (1986- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T08:14:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brett Weiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a49d9b3a-177b-5055-91cd-f7cfe7c0d442', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a49d9b3a-177b-5055-91cd-f7cfe7c0d442'}, {'abstract': 'This short video juxtaposes the reenacted testimony of two key witnesses in the shooting of the unarmed black teenager Michael Brown by a police officer in Ferguson, M