: 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'The Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By QUYNHANH DO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quynhanh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8330d50f-3a24-5407-add1-a25bd301926e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/8330d50f-3a24-5407-add1-a25bd301926e'}, {'abstract': 'The Ethicists debate whether it is a violation of generosity to profit from a friend’s giveaways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/09/magazine/is-it-wrong-if-a-friend-sells-my-hand-me-downs.html', 'snippet': 'The Ethicists debate whether it is a violation of generosity to profit from a friend’s giveaways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have two small children and am frequently divesting our household of toys, clothes and other child supplies. I sell the larger items, but I typically give the smaller items away to a neighborhood parent or leave them in a box in front of my house to be taken for free. A friend on my block recently indicated that she takes much of what we leave out, and I’ve since offered her first pick before leaving the remaining items outside. I was happy to do so, as she has two children a bit younger than mine, and I considered it a worthwhile gesture to share what we no longer need with her, despite the fact that she is of similar economic status and likely doesn’t need our castoffs. She recently held a stoop sale, and I recognized a very large number of the items that were formerly ours on display for sale. Am I wrong to see this as somehow inappropriate? I recognize that a gift means I’m not free to question what the receiver does with it, but this has changed the way I feel about her and the prospect of putting out other items in the future. Am I wrong to feel that she should have passed on these items to others? NAME WITHHELD, BROOKLYN', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/magazine/09ethicists/09mag-09ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/09/magazine/09ethicists/09mag-09ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/magazine/09ethicists/09mag-09ethicists-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/magazine/09ethicists/09mag-09ethicists-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 1367, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/magazine/09ethicists/09mag-09ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/09/magazine/09ethicists/09mag-09ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/magazine/09ethicists/09mag-09ethicists-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Wrong If a Friend Sells My Hand-Me-Downs?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicists', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is It Wrong If a Friend Sells My Hand-Me-Downs?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoshino, Kenji', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicists, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony (Per)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah, Amy Bloom and Kenji Yoshino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Kenji', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yoshino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0248477d-cc36-5dc0-8088-3dd8b1949daa', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0248477d-cc36-5dc0-8088-3dd8b1949daa'}, {'abstract': 'Amid the accusations of Deflategate, his image has been tarnished. But how much will it really matter?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/fashion/assessing-tom-bradys-stock-in-the-fashion-world.html', 'snippet': 'Amid the accusations of Deflategate, his image has been tarnished. But how much will it really matter?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If we accept as a given in the fashion/celebrity complex that public figures sell clothes (and cars and cookies) — that their carefully constructed image transfers itself to the stuff that surrounds them, along the way suggesting that if we get that stuff, too, we might be more like them — does it then follow that the obverse is true? That the tarnishing of public figures tarnishes that which is associated with them, too?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/fashion/06UNBUTTONED/06UNBUTTONED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/06/fashion/06UNBUTTONED/06UNBUTTONED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/fashion/06UNBUTTONED/06UNBUTTONED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/fashion/06UNBUTTONED/06UNBUTTONED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/fashion/06UNBUTTONED/06UNBUTTONED-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/06/fashion/06UNBUTTONED/06UNBUTTONED-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None