t': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5063ce1a-7794-51db-8e66-1059562686d1'}, {'abstract': 'The marketing push with Halo 5 is a reminder that we’ve entered a brave new world, one in which, when the first Halo arrived 14 years ago, was barely a figment of our imagination.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/daily-report-e-sports-continues-to-reshape-gaming-landscape/', 'snippet': 'The marketing push with Halo 5 is a reminder that we’ve entered a brave new world, one in which, when the first Halo arrived 14 years ago, was barely a figment of our imagination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Video games used to be such a simple business. You bought a console (say, an Xbox), you bought a game at your local big-box retailer ($46 for Halo: Combat Evolved at Wal-Mart), and you went on your merry way — spending hundreds of hours glued to a TV screen, blasting away at the bad guys.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: E-Sports Continues to Reshape Gaming Landscape', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T13:33:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Plambeck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Plambeck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24213e3a-3484-54d1-8bce-aa6cb93ac794', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24213e3a-3484-54d1-8bce-aa6cb93ac794'}, {'abstract': 'Neiman Marcus files for I.P.O. | Shire Rebuffed by Baxalta | A Sydney Exchange Woos Chinese Listings', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/morning-agenda-puerto-ricos-next-debt-problem/', 'snippet': 'Neiman Marcus files for I.P.O. | Shire Rebuffed by Baxalta | A Sydney Exchange Woos Chinese Listings', 'lead_paragraph': 'PUERTO RICO’S NEXT DEBT PROBLEM | The Puerto Rican government quietly disclosed on Monday afternoon that it had stopped making contributions of $92 million a month into a fund used to make payments on $13 billion in bond debt, Mary Williams Walsh writes in DealBook. A small payment from the fund is due on Sept. 1 and unlike the bond payments that went into default on Monday, these are general obligation bonds. Puerto Rico had issued such bonds over the years to raise money for government projects, with a guarantee in the island’s constitution that the bonds would be paid. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Puerto Rico’s Next Debt Problem', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PUERTO RICO', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayes, Tom', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soros, George', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ares Management L.L.C.', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baxalta Inc.', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canada Pension Plan Investment Board', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Scotland PLC', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shire PLC', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Societe Generale', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Chartered Bank PLC', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Specialty Lending Inc.', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS AG', 'rank': 23, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 24, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 25, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T13:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amie Tsang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tsang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb89cddb-c9e6-5c44-806f-8ec017292180', 'word_count': 2074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb89cddb-c9e6-5c44-806f-8ec017292180'}, {'abstract': 'Why a popular argument for funding the nation’s largest abortion purveyor doesn’t hold up.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/there-is-no-pro-life-case-for-planned-parenthood/', 'snippet': 'Why a popular argument for funding the nation’s largest abortion purveyor doesn’t hold up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m hoping to do something broader about the abortion issue in this space soon, given the prominence\xa0that the debate over Planned Parenthood funding\xa0has suddenly assumed.\xa0But for this week a\xa0word (well, a few words) on the argument in this Dana Milbank column, which was also basically the argument in this earlier Milbank column, which is also roughly the argument in this Ruth Marcus column, which is also the argument in this Damon Linker column,\xa0which is also a case that Slate’s Will Saletan has made repeatedly in the past, which … well, you get the idea. The claim they’re all making, in different ways,\xa0is that even though Planned Parenthood performs hundreds of thousands of abortions every year (while lobbying constantly against any restriction on the practice), to oppose channeling public dollars to its family planning operations is to be objectively pro-abortion, because those operations objectively prevent many more abortions still.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There is No Pro-Life Case For Planned Parenthood', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Education', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Linker, Damon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcus, Ruth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Milbank, Dana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guttmacher Institute', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T13:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c02b2321-d6d0-50b8-b2d0-92afde39a585', 'word_count': 1913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c02b2321-d6d0-50b8-b2d0-92afde39a585'}, {'abstract': 'Some countries’ demands for the erasure of search engine results on privacy grounds could soon affect even information available in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/technology/personaltech/right-to-be-forgotten-online-is-poised-to-spread.html', 'snippet': 'Some countries’ demands for the erasure of search engine results on privacy grounds could soon affect even information available in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a year ago, in a decision that stunned many American Internet companies, Europe’s highest court ruled that search engines were required to grant an unusual right — the “right to be forgotten.” Privacy advocates cheered the decision by the European Court of Justice, which seemed to offer citizens some recourse to what had become a growing menace of modern life: The Internet never forgets, and, in its robotic zeal to collect and organize every scrap of data about everyone, it was beginning to wreak havoc on personal privacy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/business/06state/06state-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/06/business/06state/06state-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/business/06state/06state-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non