s.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/1890-push-for-president-to-resign/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Argentina’s president is pressured to resign in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AYRES, Aug. 5 — Having failed to obtain a single Opposition Minister, President Celman has offered the city all kinds of privileges, including practical autonomy. The populace, sullen and menacing, refuse everything except the President’s resignation. The officers of the regiments that recently fought on opposite sides have fraternized and declare that in future the troops will not fight against each other. The naval opposition officers have been quietly permitted to resume their commands in the fleet. The situation here is unprecedented and almost incredible. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 6, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06-celman/06iht-oldaug06-celman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06-celman/06iht-oldaug06-celman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 758}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06-celman/06iht-oldaug06-celman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06-celman/06iht-oldaug06-celman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06-celman/06iht-oldaug06-celman-thumbStandard.jpg', '