03'}, {'abstract': 'It would be far better for a woman to replace Andrew Jackson than Alexander Hamilton.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/a-woman-on-the-10-or-the-20-bill/', 'snippet': 'It would be far better for a woman to replace Andrew Jackson than Alexander Hamilton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new poll out on Wednesday shows that 27 percent of Americans would like to see Eleanor Roosevelt on the $10 bill and about 17 percent want Harriet Tubman. Sacagawea came in third with 13 percent and Susan B. Anthony and Amelia Earhart each had 11 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Woman on the $10 or the $20 Bill?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'US Dollar (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T21:14:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3e31f7d-5e48-5d5e-9c63-02b8d79ccb8a', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3e31f7d-5e48-5d5e-9c63-02b8d79ccb8a'}, {'abstract': 'Adults are impermanently inking up in style with help from companies like Tattly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/fashion/temporary-tattoos-now-for-grown-ups-too.html', 'snippet': 'Adults are impermanently inking up in style with help from companies like Tattly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a Friday night cocktail party early this year at the auction house Christie’s, some 400 prospective buyers in the