ies” and a sensual duet, “Stay.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/arts/dance/review-joshua-beamish-takes-on-challenges-within-couples-in-4-takes.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer presented four works, including the highly involved ensemble piece “Surface Properties” and a sensual duet, “Stay.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do major ballet companies commission new works by committee, or does it just seem that way? Depending on the year, certain choreographers — lately Liam Scarlett and Justin Peck\xa0— are suddenly everywhere. But what about all the others plugging away? The Joyce Theater plays host to several in its two-week Ballet Festival, which began Tuesday with Joshua Beamish’s MOVE: the company.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BEAMISH1/06BEAMISH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BEAMISH1/06BEAMISH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BEAMISH1/06BEAMISH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BEAMISH1/06BEAMISH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1237, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BEAMISH1/06BEAMISH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BEAMISH1/06BEAMISH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BEAMISH1/06BEAMISH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Joshua Beamish Takes On Challenges Within Couples, in 4 Takes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Challenges Within Couples, in 4 Takes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beamish, Joshua', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dibble, Matthew', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MOVE: the company (Dance Co)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebastian, Jose (Dancer)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T22:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e1731f-ef6f-525e-8437-4b0127b78a20', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e1731f-ef6f-525e-8437-4b0127b78a20'}, {'abstract': 'Danny Bacher, with a lineup of seasoned traditional jazzmen, conflated the music of three Louises — Armstrong, Jordan and Prima — at the Metropolitan Room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/arts/music/review-swing-that-music-effortless-fun-in-a-tribute-to-jazz-forerunners.html', 'snippet': 'Danny Bacher, with a lineup of seasoned traditional jazzmen, conflated the music of three Louises — Armstrong, Jordan and Prima — at the Metropolitan Room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The secret of serious fun is not to take it too seriously, especially if it involves playing jazz. That attitude is something that the easygoing singer and saxophonist Danny Bacher, who appeared with a small swing band at the Metropolitan Room on Tuesday evening, knows in his bones. It is about making hot music but staying cool, about cutting up while maintaining effortless self-control, about having a blast with friends. And at his performance of “Swing That Music,” a homage to the era of jumpin’ jive with a dollop of Dixieland, Mr. Bacher conflated the music of three Louises — Armstrong, Jordan and Prima — in a concert revealing him to be a prodigiously talented musical preservationist.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BACHER/06BACHER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BACHER/06BACHER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BACHER/06BACHER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BACHER/06BACHER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BACHER/06BACHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/06BACHER/06BACHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thu