 creating shorts and features that use hand-drawn animation to explore adult themes, like\xa0 relationships and sexuality. That was the case with his recent film “Cheatin’ ” which looked at difficulties in a relationship with a fever-dream kind of style. He has also collaborated with recording artists including Kanye West on music videos and has drawn some of the opening couch gags for “Simpsons” episodes. His contributions to anthology projects included a segment in the film “The ABCs of Death 2″ and “The Animation Show,” a compilation\xa0 put together by Don Hertzfeldt and Mike Judge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Plympton Lends His Animation Skills to ‘Kahlil Gibran’s The Prophet’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plympton, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-05T23:24:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c06135e9-bdb3-58f6-a4ff-f9c3a21d278a', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c06135e9-bdb3-58f6-a4ff-f9c3a21d278a'}, {'abstract': 'Beyond the glistening muscles and dramatic poses, Brian Finke wanted to get at the spirit and personalities of competitive bodybuilders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/08/05/blogs/photographs-most-muscular.html', 'snippet': 'Beyond the glistening muscles and dramatic poses, Brian Finke wanted to get at the spirit and personalities of competitive bodybuilders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beyond the glistening muscles and dramatic poses, Brian Finke wanted to get at the spirit and personalities of competitive bo