ion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9036c3d-ab5c-5161-b086-55339beb8081', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9036c3d-ab5c-5161-b086-55339beb8081'}, {'abstract': 'Officials on Wednesday voted against funding health centers operated by Planned Parenthood of Northern New England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/us/new-hampshire-a-vote-against-planned-parenthood.html', 'snippet': 'Officials on Wednesday voted against funding health centers operated by Planned Parenthood of Northern New England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Officials \xa0on Wednesday\xa0voted against funding \xa0health centers operated by Planned Parenthood of Northern New England. New Hampshire’s Executive Council voted, 3 to 2, to reject contracts that would have provided the organization’s centers in the state with about $638,000 over two years, roughly one-third of the public funding for the centers, which is primarily federal.\xa0 Planned Parenthood, whose centers \xa0provides reproductive health services that sometimes include abortion, has been under fire after an abortion opponent released undercover videos showing its officials discussing fees for fetal tissue donation. Lawmakers elsewhere have also called for funding cuts.\xa0On Monday, Gov. Bobby Jindal of Louisiana announced that his state would terminate its Medicaid contract with the organization.\xa0On Wednesday, the councilors in New Hampshire approved contracts for three other reproductive health service providers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Hampshire: A Vote Against Planned Parenthood ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Hampshire: A Vote Against Planned Parenthood ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-06T00:26:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2bf6261-4ab2-5e4e-a659-642f1ec5c343', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2bf6261-4ab2-5e4e-a659-642f1ec5c343'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Goldstein was a high-stakes New York real estate lawyer who transformed himself into a tenacious advocate for recovering art stolen from Holocaust victims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/nyregion/charles-goldstein-dies-at-78-sought-return-of-art-looted-by-nazis.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Goldstein was a high-stakes New York real estate lawyer who transformed himself into a tenacious advocate for recovering art stolen from Holocaust victims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charles Goldstein, a high-stakes New York real estate lawyer who transformed himself into a tenacious advocate for recovering art looted from Holocaust victims, died on July 30 in Manhattan. He was 78.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/nyregion/09goldstein-obit/09goldstein-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/09/nyregion/09goldstein-obit/09goldstein-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 832}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type