g been a prized delicacy at Chinese banquets, the mark of a special occasion. And no variety of sea cucumber is more valued, or costlier, than the exceedingly rare albino. Just a few years ago, five white sea cucumbers sold at auction in the city of Jinan for 160,000 renminbi, or nearly $26,000 at today’s exchange rate. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06SINO-SEA/06SINO-SEA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 258, 'width': 363, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06SINO-SEA/06SINO-SEA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 258, 'width': 363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06SINO-SEA/06SINO-SEA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06SINO-SEA/06SINO-SEA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/blogs/06SINO-SEA/06SINO-SEA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Albino Sea Cucumbers, a Delicacy, Could Become a Lot Less Rare', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Albinism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yang Hongsheng', 'rank': 7, 'major'