perous couple and their ominous new acquaintance takes several turns even after abandoning its formulaic premise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even if “The Gift,” the Australian director Joel Edgerton’s creepy stalker thriller, didn’t make a dramatic U-turn at around the halfway point, it would still rank as a superior specimen. This movie doesn’t foam at the mouth like “Fatal Attraction.” No bunnies are boiled. But fish are poisoned, a family dog goes missing and the soundtrack is tricked out with the sudden jolts dear to the genre. Any revenge is more pitiable than cathartic. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/gift-image/gift-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/gift-image/gift-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/gift-image/gift-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/gift-image/gift-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1423, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/gift-image/gift-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/gift-image/gift-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/arts/gift-image/gift-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘The Gift,’ a Stalker Thriller That Isn’t What It Seems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Happy Couple, a Newcomer and the Coldness in a Husband&#8217;s Smile ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edgerton, Joel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bateman, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Rebecca', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'THE GIFT (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-06T12:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc7389b1-d2b8-5702-9dfa-f83801014b8e', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc7389b1-d2b8-5702-9dfa-f83801014b8e'}, {'abstract': 'Katmai National Park is visited by thousands of bears near its campground every summer, so visitors must follow the rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/09/travel/alaska-brown-bears-katmai-national-park.html', 'snippet': 'Katmai National Park is visited by thousands of bears near its campground every summer, so visitors must follow the rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katmai National Park sprawls over four million acres in southern Alaska. So why does its only established campground allow for just 60 people per night — a limit that leads to an online booking fray every January? The answer is also one of the park’s main draws, and its primary claim to national fame: bears. Lots of them — about 2,200 at the National Park Service’s last count, with 60 or so regulars that hang around Brooks Camp every summer. In theory, you can camp elsewhere in Katmai, but the campground has an electric fence and constant activity, making it an unlikely place to find a bear too close to your tent for sleeping comfort.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Katmai National Park in Alaska, Bears Rule', 'kicker': 'Explorer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hosts Are Wild, So Keep Your Distance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schnuer, Jenna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camps and Camping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Katmai National Park', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bears', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-06T12:09:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Schnuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schnuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5e12694-69d3-502c-8813-555a1366fcab', 'word_count': 2014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5e12694-69d3-502c-8813-555a1366fcab'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: President Johnson signed the Voting Rights Act into law in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/1965-voting-rights-act-passed/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: President Johnson signed the Voting Rights Act into law in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Johnson today [Aug. 6] signed into law federal voting rights legislation which he said will ‘‘fuse and blend … the Negro story and the American story.’’ He said his administration will move immediately to enforce it in the Deep South. After his address, Mr. Johnson walked to the ornate ‘‘President’s Room’’ in the Senate, where 104 years ago Abraham Lincoln signed a law freeing slaves impressed into war service by the Confederacy. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, August 7, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/blogs/07iht-oldaug07-voting/07iht-oldaug07-voting-articleLarge.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/07/blogs/07iht-oldaug07-voting/07iht-oldaug07-voting-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/blogs/07iht-oldaug07-voting/07iht-oldaug07-voting-jumbo.png', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/blogs/07iht-oldaug07-voting/07iht-oldaug07-voting-superJumbo.png', 'height': 850, 'width': 1275, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/blogs/07iht-oldaug07-voting/07iht-oldaug07-voting-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/07/b