uld recall involving a suspect so young.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detroit Boy, 11, Charged With Manslaughter in Shooting of 3-Year-Old', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '11-Year-Old Held in Detroit in Fatal Shooting of Boy, 3', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Elijah (d 2015)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-06T15:26:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af93acec-9780-56c5-bf07-427cadeba0fc', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af93acec-9780-56c5-bf07-427cadeba0fc'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Westminster discusses Noel Coward’s trip to America in wartime.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/1940-ministers-ponder-actors-trip/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Westminster discusses Noel Coward’s trip to America in wartime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Parliament today [Aug. 6] buckled down to discussing Noel Coward and Miss Gracie Fields and how they got away to America. Coward, actor and all-round entertainer, was the subject of a question put by a Conservative. On what mission, he asked, was Mr. Coward engaged by his majesty’s government? Harold Nicolson, Parliamentary Secretary to the Ministry of Information, replied that Coward had gone with the approval of Prime Minister Winston Churchill. Another member said feeling was rising that ‘‘if a man has a certain amount of publicity value and money he can get out of this country when the country is going through a period of great stress and anxiety?’’ — New York Herald Tribune, August 7, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Ministers Ponder Actor’s Trip', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Churchill, Winston Leonard Spencer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coward, Noel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-06T15:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/795a1cda-c20b-5dce-8eed-268246ee5b1c', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/795a1cda-c20b-5dce-8eed-268246ee5b1c'}, {'abstract': 'The first BRIC JazzFest is scheduled for Oct. 11-16.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/brooklyn-getting-a-new-jazz-festival-at-bric-house/', 'snippet': 'The first BRIC JazzFest is scheduled for Oct. 11-16.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new jazz festival will take root in downtown Brooklyn this fall. The first BRIC JazzFest will take place Oct. 11 to 16 at BRIC House, the recently renovated contemporary arts center in Fort Gre