e designer Adi Gil recently spent a week in the desert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Israel-born designer Adi Gil remembers family trips to South Sinai in the ’70s, before Egypt secured the area. Recently, she’s started spending time there again — though the present-day peninsula bears little resemblance to the crowded South Sinai from her childhood photo albums. Still, it remains “beautiful and surreal,” says Gil, one-third of the brand Three as Four. “It all depends on how you look at it — and who is looking at it. When it comes to the Middle East, sometimes I feel that the media likes to magnify the negative. We know there are issues in North Sinai. But next door there is beauty, and no one is talking about that.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In South Sinai With One-third of Three as Four', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinai Peninsula (Egypt)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-06T18:40:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aff4d25b-62aa-5ab3-ba5f-3597e10962cb', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aff4d25b-62aa-5ab3-ba5f-3597e10962cb'