h Deadline Deals, Blue Jays Load Up on Optimism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jays Acquire Optimism in Flurry of Transactions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trades (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tulowitzki, Troy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Price, David Taylor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawkins, Latroy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-06T19:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2de3e9c4-c185-53e0-9adf-899093a512f2', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2de3e9c4-c185-53e0-9adf-899093a512f2'}, {'abstract': 'The hip-hop musical about the nation’s founding fathers is scheduled to open on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/creator-and-fans-hit-it-lucky-with-hamilton/', 'snippet': 'The hip-hop musical about the nation’s founding fathers is scheduled to open on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three hours before the\xa05 p.m. Broadway opening night of his hip-hop\xa0musical “Hamilton,” Lin-Manuel Miranda paid emotional tribute to the biography, and the life, that inspired his work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Creator and Fans Hit It Lucky With ‘Hamilton’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chernow, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miranda, Lin-Manuel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seller, Jeffrey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-06T19:56:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Paulson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paulson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27522bcc-ebc5-51f2-ab7d-23699257d164', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27522bcc-ebc5-51f2-ab7d-23699257d164'}, {'abstract': 'The West London district has a new set of townhouses turned hotel suites.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/06/laslett-hotel-notting-hill/', 'snippet': 'The West London district has a new set of townhouses turned hotel suites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The West London district of Notting Hill famously attracts visitors to its pastel-colored rows of houses, sprawling Portobello Road Antiques Market and Europe’s biggest street festival — and yet has always, until now, lacked sumptuous places to stay. On the south side of the secluded Pembridge Gardens, just seconds from Notting Hill Gate station (and a mere 15-minute hop to the hubbub of Soho), a row of five stucco Victorian mansions have recently been transformed into what is now the Laslett hotel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/06/t-magazine/06llaslett-farrell/06llaslett-farrell-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'w