t at least its storytelling is fairly coherent, and its gleaming dream world of snow and ice is one of the most visually captivating environments to be found in a Disney animated film,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times about this blockbuster, inspired by Hans Christian Andersen’s “The Snow Queen.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b53d3adb-1763-55ac-a10a-4b6cdbabbfdf', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b53d3adb-1763-55ac-a10a-4b6cdbabbfdf'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, August 7, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/07/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, August 7, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Is this going to be a tearing apart, or a pivot point of people trying to understand each other, trying to live together?”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T05:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': ''