ssues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HANOI, Vietnam — Secretary of State John Kerry told a group of Vietnamese officials and business leaders on Friday that improvements in human rights here would lead to deeper ties.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Tells Vietnam That U.S. Ties Will Deepen if Human Rights Are Protected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Briefing | Asia; Vietnam: Progress on Human Rights Will Deepen Ties With U.S., Kerry Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T07:53:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb0dcffd-6fff-54c0-bf83-27f04f10d936', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb0dcffd-6fff-54c0-bf83-27f04f10d936'}, {'abstract': 'At least three waves of attacks left hundreds wounded: First a truck bomb, then group attacks on the police academy and, later, a police headquarters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/08/world/asia/suicide-truck-bombing-in-kabul-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'At least three waves of attacks left hundreds wounded: First a truck bomb, then group attacks on the police academy and, later, a police headquarters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A barrage of deadly suicide attacks killed at least 65 people and wounded hundreds more in Kabul on Friday, ending a two-month lull in major terrorist strikes in the capital, according to Afghan officials. It was the deadliest day in Kabul so far this year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waves of Suicide Attacks Shake Kabul on Its Deadliest Day of 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Waves of Suicide Attacks Shake Kabul on Its Deadliest Day of 2015', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakib, Ahmad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haqqani Network', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T08:19:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ahmad Shakib and Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ahmad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shakib', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://ar