ates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — A Chinese lawyer who defied the authorities by speaking publicly about being tortured in police custody and who had become a vocal critic of a continuing government crackdown on human rights lawyers has been detained by the police, his wife said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Detains Lawyer Who Accused Police of Torture, His Wife Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Heping (1971- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T11:25:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21b1e16b-8c21-5036-a06d-509d9c7d273d', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21b1e16b-8c21-5036-a06d-509d9c7d273d'}, {'abstract': 'Last week, the Catholic diocese of Wenzhou released a letter signed by its bishop and 26 priests on the government’s taking down of crosses at churches.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/07/a-call-to-cry-out-against-cross-removals-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Last week, the Catholic diocese of Wenzhou released a letter signed by its bishop and 26 priests on the government’s taking down of crosses at churches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past year and a half, the government of Zhejiang Province has forcibly removed hundreds of crosses from churches, part of a campaign by the local authorities to lower the profile of Christianity in a region where it has made deep inroads. The campaign has long met with protests by parishioners, but now it is also being denounced by government-approved Christian organizations. In early July, official Protestant and Catholic associations issued open letters questioning the campaign’s legality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/world/07sino-letter02/07sino-letter02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/07/world/07sino-letter02/07sino-letter02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/world/07sino-letter02/07sino-letter02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/world/07sino-letter02/07sino-letter02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/world/07sino-letter02/07sino-letter02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/07/world/07sino-letter02/07sino-letter02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/world/07sino-letter02/07sino-letter02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150