n the small screen in 1960, there’s been little doubt that while it’s the substance of presidential debates that matters most, image and appearance can play a potentially significant role in swaying voter opinion (consciously or not). As a result, different schools of thoughts have developed on the best approach to the situation. The two most popular were on view last night, and like the candidates themselves, proved to have varying degrees of success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Presidential Debate Fashions: Windows Into a Candidacy', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits (Apparel)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lynn University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T11:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5885d2f4-8d29-5644-b823-a9219ad98ae8', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5885d2f4-8d29-5644-b823-a9219ad98ae8'}, {'abstract': 'Donald J. Trump said that he owed it to his supporters to keep open the possibility of running as an independent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/08/