3c636c6'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s folk revival in pictures and interviews.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/09/books/review/folk-city-new-york-and-the-american-folk-music-revival.html', 'snippet': 'New York City’s folk revival in pictures and interviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How New York City and specifically Greenwich Village came to be at the epicenter of an American folk music revival between 1950 and 1965 is the subject of Stephen Petrus and Ronald D. Cohen’s “Folk City.” This handsome book, which includes rarely seen photographs, reminiscences of participants and a lively narrative, adds depth to an exhibition of the same name on view at the Museum of the City of New York until January. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09radosh/09radosh-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09radosh/09radosh-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 469}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09radosh/09radosh-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09radosh/09radosh-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1602, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09radosh/09radosh-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09r