, 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylvia Brownrigg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylvia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brownrigg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/95fa9e1b-6b34-5726-8a60-d87e43701a9b', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95fa9e1b-6b34-5726-8a60-d87e43701a9b'}, {'abstract': 'In Gabriel Urza’s debut novel, characters’ memories are prompted by the Madrid train bombing of 2004.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/09/books/review/all-that-followed-by-gabriel-urza.html', 'snippet': 'In Gabriel Urza’s debut novel, characters’ memories are prompted by the Madrid train bombing of 2004.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stories are shape-shifters in “All That Followed,” Gabriel Urza’s strange and ambitious debut novel. Set in Spain’s Basque Country, the book revolves around the assassination of Councilman José Antonio Torres, as recounted by three characters: Mariana, his dubiously grieving widow; the American teacher Joni Garrett, who came to Muriga in 1951 and wound up staying for his entire life; and Iker Abarzuza, serving time for murder in an island prison, where he listens to the cries of shorebirds and receives the occasional letter from Mariana.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09dubois/09dubois-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09dubois/09dubois-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09dubois/09dubois-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09dubois/09dubois-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1526, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09dubois/09dubois-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09dubois/09dubois-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/09/books/review/09dubois/09dubois-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘All That Followed,’ by\xa0Gabriel Urza', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Basque Connection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'duBois, Jennifer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urza, Gabriel (1978- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'All That Followed (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T13:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Dubois', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dubois', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f042c5bc-dd33-5f80-a35b-212c125761d7', 'word_count': 1365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f042c5bc-dd33-5f80-