and engaging in a systemic review.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/08/world/europe/in-britain-edward-heath-case-intensifies-debate-over-validity-of-sex-abuse-claims.html', 'snippet': 'After some notable previous revelations proved true, Britain is now taking each new case seriously and engaging in a systemic review.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Accusations of child sexual abuse against some prominent figures of Britain’s recent past have proved true. Allegations of similar wrongdoing by others, dating back decades, surface regularly now in the hothouse British press, as does talk of cover-ups by some of the nation’s most powerful institutions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Britain, Edward Heath Case Intensifies Debate Over Validity of Sex Abuse Claims', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shock in Britain as More Abuse Claims Emerge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heath, Edward', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brittan, Leon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savile, Jimmy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Rolf', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T17:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a08a902-265f-5ecb-a048-2993a735a7a3', 'word_count': 1632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a08a902-265f-5ecb-a048-2993a735a7a3'}, {'abstract': 'The Gregory Brothers present a musical mash-up video of the first Republican presidential debate of 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/07/opinion/we-need-brain-songify-the-gop-debate.html', 'snippet': 'The Gregory Brothers present a musical mash-up video of the first Republican presidential debate of 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we hunkered down at Gregory Brothers headquarters in Brooklyn to songify the first debate of the 2016 election season, word broke that the Fox News team, inspired by their broadcast from Quicken Loans Arena, was considering using the Cleveland Cavaliers’ N.B.A. shot-clock buzzer to alert candidates that their allotted time was up. We were crestfallen when, at the first such transgression, we instead heard a polite “ding.” The Cavaliers’ claxon would have been perfect for a debate field so large it could have filled two basketball teams, qualifying in number if not by height.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Need Brain: Songify the G.O.P. Debate’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘We Need Brain: Songify the G.O.P. Debate’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T17:05:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Gregory Brothers', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Gregory Brothers'}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dd626b8-3156-5d84-8508-d5a636a86f0a', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dd626b8-3156-5d84-8508-d5a636a86f0a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Hammond, 19, was shot by an officer in Seneca, S.C., but the episode initially escaped much of the national attention to race and police behavior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/08/us/questions-arise-after-police-kill-a-white-teenager-zachary-hammond.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hammond, 19, was shot by an officer in Seneca, S.C., but the episode initially escaped much of the national attention to race and police behavior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zachary Hammond, a white teenager, pulled up to a drive-through window last week at a Hardee’s restaurant in Seneca, S.C. A sting operation was underway, with police officers suspecting a possible drug deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/08/us/08zachary_watch/08zachary_watch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/08/us/08zachary_watch/08zachary_watch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/08/us/08zachary_watch/08zachary_watch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/08/us/08zachary_watch/08zachary_watch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1097, 'width': 1645, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/08/us/08zachary_watch/08zachary_watch-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbSta