aragraph': 'CENTENNIAL, Colo. — In a decision that surprised many in this community, a jury sentenced James E. Holmes on Friday to life in prison with no chance of parole, rejecting the death penalty for the man who carried out a 2012 shooting rampage that killed 12 people in a Colorado movie theater.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Sentence for James Holmes, Aurora Theater Gunman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater Gunman Is Spared Death in Aurora Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Healy, Jack (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora, Colo, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, James Eagan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-07T20:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47bb726c-c32b-55a7-bbd9-2556ebe8ef9c', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47bb726c-c32b-55a7-bbd9-2556ebe8ef9c'}, {'abstract': 'A federal appeals panel rejected an argument by the groups affiliated with the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of New York that an opt-out form imposed a “substantial burden” on their religious freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/08/nyregion/court-says-4-catholic-nonprofits-must-allow-workers-access-to-contraception.html', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals panel rejected an argument by the groups affiliat