rson': [{'firstname': 'Libby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/beaf5aff-9171-5f9f-82b1-c8565368bbce', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/beaf5aff-9171-5f9f-82b1-c8565368bbce'}, {'abstract': 'All hail Egbert.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/09/knitting-history-trivial/', 'snippet': 'All hail Egbert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Brad DeLong, a great history of socks. But somehow it misses the economic geography story, where there once was a great hosiery center in Cohoes, near Albany, thanks to one Egbert Egberts, who invented the first power knitting frame. In England the comparable complex was in Nottingham. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knitting History (Trivial)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-09T16:33:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4db7bbd-94b2-5d3e-85b0-3d0cb4e3859d', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4db7bbd-94b2-5d3e-85b0-3d0cb4e3859d'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/09/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7 P.M. (Travel) AMERICA. THE BEAUTIFUL. Robert Redford narrates this exploration of some of the country’s most breathtaking landscapes in advance of the National Park Service’s centennial celebration in 2016. The journey begins in California, as the pilots Chris Bolfing and John Heiney, above, hang glide through Yosemite; the arborist Chad Brey climbs 200 feet into the branches in Redwoods National Park; and the marine biologist Alana Osaki dives into kelp that can grow 90 feet tall in the Channel Islands. At 7:30, the series moves to Utah, where the adventurers Faith Dickey and Andy Lewis slack-line in Mineral Canyon, and Heidi Redd herds cattle in Indian Creek Canyon. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-09T17:17:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd949e58-40f9-5088-b9da-6428edd8dcc0', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd949e58-40f9-5088-b9da-6428edd8dcc0'}, {'abstract': 'In phone interviews with four Sunday programs, Donald J. Trump suggested that he had been singled out for attacks by the hosts of Thursday’s Republican presidential debate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/10/us/politics/trump-remains-defiant-on-news-programs-amid-gop-backlash.html', 'snippet': 'In phone interviews with four Sunday programs, Donald J. Trump suggested that he had been singled out for attacks by the hosts of Thursday’s Republican presidential debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A defiant Donald J. Trump suggested on Sunday that he had been singled out for attacks by the hosts of last week’s widely watched Republican presidential 