e-in-presidential-primaries.html', 'snippet': 'The vote is widely seen as a referendum on President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner’s governing Front for Victory, which has been in power for 12 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Argentines voted to select presidential nominees on Sunday in a primary election that will gauge the nation’s desire for change after 12 years of the current president’s governing party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentines Vote in Presidential Primary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentines Vote in Presidential Primary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scioli, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macri, Mauricio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Front for Victory (Argentina)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-10T00:27:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Gilbert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilbert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0887f75-e152-5313-857e-637d7d6b554c', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0887f75-e152-5313-857e-637d7d6b554c'}, {'abstract': 'This week analysts expect modest results from four department stores, a quarterly earnings report from Alibaba and retails sales for July.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/10/business/department-store-earnings-alibabas-results-and-july-retail-sales.html', 'snippet': 'This week analysts expect modest results from four department stores, a quarterly earnings report from Alibaba and retails sales for July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Labor will hold four days of public hearings this week to discuss its proposed rule that would require a broader group of financial professionals to put their clients’ interests ahead of their own when handling the clients’ retirement money. The hearings will be held from Monday through Thursday. The White House has estimated that the lack of consumer protection costs investors as much as $17 billion annually, or 1 percent of their assets, and perhaps more. But the rule has faced strong and well-funded opponents in the financial services industry. Those stakeholders, along with consumer advocates including AARP, will have the opportunity to make their arguments to regulators this week. —Tara Siegel Bernard', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/business/10ahead1/10ahead1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/10/business/10ahead1/10ahead1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/business/10ahead1/10ahead1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/business/10ahead1/10ahead1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail