,” about the sole survivor of a massacre that destroyed the rest of the pride. The lineup continues with “Big Cat Diary,” which tracks lions, cheetahs and leopards roaming the Masai Mara National Reserve in Kenya, at 7; “Into the Lion’s Den,” which follows Dave Salmoni, a large-predator expert, into lion territory as he tries to prove that the creatures are more likely to accept people than attack them, at 10; “Into the Pride,” in which Mr. Salmoni works to save rogue lions from elimination, at noon; and “A Lion Called Christian,” about the story behind the Internet phenomenon depicting the emotional reunion between two men and their 300-pound captive lion a year after it was released into the wild, at 5 p.m. Nat Geo Wild also commemorates big-cat conservation from noon through 8 p.m.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-10T04:11:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1e57c26-c26c-5d5b-9dbb-adaeb76419b2', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1e57c26-c26c-5d5b-9dbb-adaeb76419b2'}, {'abstract': 'Jason and Justin Sablich, who provide fantasy football analysis for The New York Times, pick their 10 favorite quarterbacks for 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/08/10/sports/football/top-10-fantasy-football-quarterbacks.html', 'snippet': 'Jason and Justin S