first post in an occasional series about new ventures to support Times journalism as print revenue declines.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/10/as-print-fades-part-1-live-journalism-at-the-times/', 'snippet': 'The first post in an occasional series about new ventures to support Times journalism as print revenue declines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its announcement last week that one million digital-only subscribers now pay for its journalism, The Times hit a major milestone, and one worth celebrating. Just a few years back, as various pay wall efforts were tried and put on the shelf, that eye-popping number was close to unimaginable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Print Fades, Part 1: ‘Live Journalism’ at The Times', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-10T12:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dfa78b9-dce6-50ba-a17c-52e8c285f3ac', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dfa78b9-dce6-50ba-a17c-52e8c285f3ac'}, {'abstract': 'Residents of Durango, Colo., are fuming over an E.P.A. mistake that sent three million gallons of mine waste into the town’s cultural soul, the Animas River.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/us/durango-colorado-mine-spill-environmental-protection-agency.html', 'snippet': 'Residents of Durango, Colo., are fuming over an E.P.A. mistake that sent three million gallons of mine waste into the town’s cultural soul, the Animas River.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURANGO, Colo. — The Animas River is the cultural soul of this patch of southwestern Colorado, a sort of moving Main Street that hosts multiple floating parades a year and is typically bustling with rafters and kayakers. Schoolchildren study the river. Sweethearts marry on its banks. Its former name, given by Spaniards, is el Río de las Ánimas, the River of Souls.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/11/us/11DURANGO1/11DURANGO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/11/us/11DURANGO1/11DURANGO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/11/us/11DURANGO1/11DURANGO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/11/us/11DURANGO1/11DURANGO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1331, 'width': 1998, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/11/us/11DURANGO1/11DURANGO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/11/us/11DURANGO1/11DURANGO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/11/us/11DURANGO1/11DURANGO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Environmental Agency Uncorks Its Own Toxic Water Spill at Colorado Mine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Environmental Agency Uncorks Its Own Toxic Spill ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Durango (Colo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Animas River (Colo-NM)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kinross Gold Corporation', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sunnyside Gold Corp', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-10T12:04:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Turkewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turkewitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da09bce8-dd7d-5ffa-9804-5f8372924750', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da09bce8-dd7d-5ffa-9804-5f8372924750'}, {'abstract': 'What happened to the Chicago School?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/10/trash-talk-and-the-macroeconomic-divide/', 'snippet': 'What happened to the Chicago School?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Romer continues to maintain that Chicago’s inward turn, the rejection of all salt-water macroeconomics that left it so hapless in the face of the Great Recession, was a defensive reaction to the sarcasm of Robert Solow. Brad DeLong points out that Solow was, as it turns out, right. Beyond that, as Brad notes and Paul actually acknowledges, what was actually going on at MIT was nothing like the implacable opposition of Chicago fantasies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trash Talk and the Macroeconomic Divide', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-10T12:05:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a72e9745-3985-5049-a6f1-71f4ce3f2d7a', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a72e9745-3985-5049-a6f1-71f4ce3f2d7a'}, {'abstract': 'The deal for Therakos, a maker of immunotherapy drugs, is expected to broaden Mallinckrodt’s offerings and to expand its business in hospitals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/business/dealbook/mallinckrodt-to-acquire-therakos-for-1-33-billion.html', 'snippet': 'The deal for Therakos, a maker of immunotherapy drugs, is expected to broaden Mallinckrodt’s offerings and to expand its business in hospitals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Mallinckrodt Pharmaceuticals, a maker of drugs and medical devices, said on Monday that it had agreed to buy Therakos from the American private equity firm Gores Group for about $1.33 billion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mallinckrodt\xa0Pharmaceu