ttan, Brooklyn and Queens offices, even though they were not open for the full day. At the Brooklyn bureau, on the second floor of Borough Hall, ten policemen were needed to keep a long line of applicants in order. Julius J. Brosen, chief clerk, said: ‘‘This is the biggest day we’ve had this year.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, August 11, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Rush to Marry Ahead of Draft', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-10T16:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1718717a-f792-5d72-b0df-a8c5f0df01a5', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1718717a-f792-5d72-b0df-a8c5f0df01a5'}, {'abstract': 'NBC, which has used English soccer to define its NBCSN cable network, made a deal worth about $1 billion, basically double the annual cost of NBC’s current contract.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/sports/soccer/nbc-retains-rights-to-premier-league-in-six-year-deal.html', 'snippet': 'NBC, which has used English soccer to define its NBCSN cable network, made a deal worth about $1 billion, basically double the annual cost of NBC’s current contract.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years of success broadcasting England’s Premier 