7-a209fdadf160'}, {'abstract': 'Geoffrey Kent’s book takes readers to Kenya, Antarctica and beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/10/safari-geoffrey-kent-memoir/', 'snippet': 'Geoffrey Kent’s book takes readers to Kenya, Antarctica and beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Geoffrey Kent, the founder and CEO of the luxury travel company Abercrombie & Kent, is adding, coincidentally albeit poignantly, to the discussion about big-game hunting. The Kenya-raised Kent led his inaugural safari in 1962 under the slogan “hunt with a camera, not with a gun,” and expanded his program over the years, even attracting a post-Liz-Taylor-breakup Richard Burton. In “Safari: A Memoir of a Worldwide Travel Pioneer” ($35, Harper Collins), out tomorrow, Kent recounts these anecdotes and more from places as far-flung as the North Pole and the Galápagos Islands. “I wanted this book to inspire people to travel,” he says. “You can find out more about yourself and find out more about others.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/t-magazine/10beddie-safari/10beddie-safari-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/10/t-magazine/10beddie-safari/10beddie-safari-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/t-magazine/10beddie-safari/10beddie-safari-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/t-magazine/10beddie-safari/10beddie-safari-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail'