ppet': 'Jonathan Ollivier, who starred in works choreographed by Matthew Bourne, was killed when a car struck his motorcyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Jonathan Ollivier, a British dancer who played a starring role in Matthew Bourne’s work, died here on Sunday after a car struck his motorcycle. He was 38. Mr. Ollivier, who had been performing the leading role in Mr. Bourne’s “The Car Man” at Sadler’s Wells, was on his way to the theater, where he was set to appear that night in the company’s final performance of the season. The BBC reported that paramedics and an air ambulance tried to save Mr. Ollivier’s life but pronounced him dead at the scene shortly before midday. It also reported that the driver of the vehicle that collided with Mr. Ollivier had been arrested.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jonathan Ollivier, Dancer Featured in Matthew Bourne’s Work, Dies in Crash', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Dancer Dies in Accident', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bourne, Matthew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ollivier, Jonathan (1977-2015)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-10T18:43:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a25e392a-1eb4-5867-b249-ad889cb15a42', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a25e392a-1eb4-5867-b249-ad889cb15a42'}, {'abstract': 'The police described the raid on Sunday in the Sundarban mangrove forest as the beginning of a larger crackdown on 