merican-west-ends-in-tragedy.html', 'snippet': 'David and Ornella Steiner were found dead in a New Mexico desert last week. Their 9-year-old son survived, likely because they sacrificed water to save him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The family from France was so enthralled by their last visit to the American West that they started planning another almost immediately. On Facebook, they posted pictures of the vast blue skies, the rugged ocher canyons and the endless strips of asphalt that had captivated them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A French Couple’s Love for the American West Ends in Tragedy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hikes and Hiking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'White Sands National Monument (NM)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steiner, David (d 2015)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steiner, Ornella (d 2015)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T01:47:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aurelien Breeden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aurelien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Breeden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c8a7b24-e351-53a5-bf87-5a9db8344094', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c8a7b24-e351-53a5-bf87-5a9db8344094'}, {'abstract': 'With wordplay and references to the Google parody from the HBO series “Silicon Valley,” the company formerly known as Google Inc. captured the imagination and curiosity of the Internet with its reorganization on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/10/alphabet-wordplay-a-hooli-easter-egg-and-more-on-googles-name-change/', 'snippet': 'With wordplay and references to the Google parody from the HBO series “Silicon Valley,” the company formerly known as Google Inc. captured the imagination and curiosity of the Internet with its reorganization on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, Google announced that it was changing the name of the company to Alphabet, creating a structure that would encompass multiple parts. The search engine division will be separate from some of the more futuristic parts of the company, such as an anti-aging biotech firm and the lab that builds self-driving cars. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/technology/10bits-alphabet2/10bits-alphabet2-articleLarge.png', 'height': 638, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/10/technology/10bits-alphabet2/10bits-alphabet2-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 638}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/technology/10bits-alphabet2/10bits-alphabet2-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 964, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/technology/10bits-alphabet2/10bits-alphabet2-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1411, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/technology/10bits-alphabet2/10bits-alphabet2-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': '