 Obama administration, citing the potential for economic and political harm to the Palestinian Authority and the broader peace process, asked a judge on Monday to “carefully consider” the size of the bond he requires for the authority to appeal a huge damages award for its role in six terrorist attacks in Israel that killed and injured Americans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Requests Lower Bond for Palestinian Appeal of Terror Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Requests Lower Bond for Appeal of Terror Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestine Liberation Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T04:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e7df4e6-568d-5988-a2a8-5757949224b1', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e7df4e6-568d-5988-a2a8-5757949224b1'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, August 11, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-tuesday-august-11-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, August 11, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There’s always a sense things can boil over, but there’s a sense of maturity here.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, August 11, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T04:39:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e86df4b-3e1d-5b33-9280-ae8d4d524298', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e86df4b-3e1d-5b33-9280-ae8d4d524298'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:05 P.M. (Encore) BUTCH CASSIDY AND THE SUNDANCE KID (1969) Does it get any prettier than this? Robert Redford and Paul Newman (above right, with Mr. Redford) star as the famous Wild West outlaws on the lam (destination: Bolivia), with Katharine Ross as the woman who sets their hearts aflutter. The soundtrack to their lives: Burt Bacharach’s Oscar-winning score, featuring “Raindrops Keep Fallin’ on My Head,” which won for best original song, written with Hal David. Much of the movie “is very funny in a strictly contemporary way — the last exuberant word on movies about the men of the mythic American West who have outlived their day,” Vincent Canby wrote in The New York Times. And while there are “some bothersome technical things about the movie (the camera is all zoom, zoom, zoom),” he added, “the overall production is very handsome, and the performances fine, especially Newman, Redford and Miss Ross, who must be broadly funny and straight, almost simultaneously. They succeed even if the movie does not.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/ada0dadc-d821-5a84-a317-2a7c9c6eb9d7', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ada0dadc-d821-5a84-a317-2a7c9c6eb9d7'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Tuesday, August 11, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/pageoneplus/corrections-august-11-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Tuesday, August 11, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: August 11, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T06:22:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b2c0538-bf8f-593e-bcb9-7c9c455fa096', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b2c0538-bf8f-593e-bcb9-7c9c455fa096'}, {'abstract': 'Harry Gruyaert’s father made film. He makes pictures. His credo: “I just physically jump into a situation and react to it, and see how things are working out.”', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/born-to-make-photos/', 'snippet': 'Harry Gruyaert’s father made film. He makes pictures. His credo: “I just physically jump into a situation and react to it, and see how things are working out.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harry Gruyaert, the Belgian photographer and member of Magnum, has been taking pictures for a long time. Long enough to have been friends — and colleagues — with Henri Cartier-Bresson, with whom he shared a philosophy of photography.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Born to Make Photos', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gruyaert, Harry (1941- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T07:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Blaustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blaustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7da2ab41-ca3d-5710-b48c-a318a07612fd', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7da2ab41-ca3d-5710-b48c-a318a07612fd'}, {'abstract': 'Test your knowledge of academic skills by playing our crossword.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/student-crossword-academic-skills/', 'snippet': 'Test your knowledge of academic skills by playing our crossword.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your knowledge of academic skills by playing our crossword (PDF). You can find the answers here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', '