 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9d09fe8-f940-5c91-8230-f7a374a12ad3', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9d09fe8-f940-5c91-8230-f7a374a12ad3'}, {'abstract': 'With a new rezoning plan, Mayor Bill de Blasio hopes to spur the creation of permanent affordable housing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/opinion/mayor-de-blasios-plan-for-affordable-housing.html', 'snippet': 'With a new rezoning plan, Mayor Bill de Blasio hopes to spur the creation of permanent affordable housing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio has unveiled another part of his ambitious plan to save New York City — a proposal to use land-use regulations to spur the creation of large amounts of permanently affordable housing. He wants to use a tactic called mandatory inclusionary zoning  in which as neighborhoods or specific parcels are rezoned, developers who want to build there would have to set aside at least 25 to 30 percent of new apartments for people of low and moderate incomes. They could not opt out, and the affordability would be permanent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/11/opinion/11Edit3-Web/11Edit3-Web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/11/opinion/11Edit3-Web/11Edit3-Web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/11/opinion/11Edit3-Web/11Edit3-Web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/11/opinion/11Edit3-Web/11Edit3-Web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 