': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democrats Sever Ties to Founders of Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jefferson, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d51706d-8432-5a33-8b4c-f6694db9f719', 'word_count': 1283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d51706d-8432-5a33-8b4c-f6694db9f719'}, {'abstract': 'Fans of music from Nigeria and Ghana discuss their personal style as they enter the Apollo Theater in Harlem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/fashion/hiplife-ghanaian-nigerian-style-at-the-apollo.html', 'snippet': 'Fans of music from Nigeria and Ghana discuss their personal style as they enter the Apollo Theater in Harlem.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What can you say? It’s Africa time!” the legendary music promoter Sparkie Martin remarked on Saturday evening, as he surveyed a modest crowd lining up outside the Apollo Theater for an evening of Ghanaian and Nigerian acts sharing the bill with the hiplife superstar Sarkodie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hiplife at the Apollo', 'kicker': 'Life as a Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APOLLO THEATER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ghana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eb6b11d-fc07-5b48-8a70-cf4b4b992961', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eb6b11d-fc07-5b48-8a70-cf4b4b992961'}, {'abstract': 'Nowhere is this city’s shift from drug capital to forward-looking metropolis more apparent than the chic El Poblado neighborhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/fashion/medelln-colombia-fashion.html', 'snippet': 'Nowhere is this city’s shift from drug capital to forward-looking metropolis more apparent than the chic El Poblado neighborhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Colombian city of Medellín has gone through a drastic transformation from drug capital to forward-looking metropolis. This is especially true of the chic El Poblado neighborhood, where the streets are crowded with designer boutiques, cafes and restaurants with ample outdoor seating — because, well, there’s no reason to sit inside. Locals are extremely proud of the neighborhood’s progress in bringing global style to Colombia while maintaining local flair. The city’s perennially comfortable weather and luscious natural habitat have a decided influence on the way people dress, from airy fabrics to colorful prints. “The way people dress in this part of Colombia is all about layers,” said Amelia Ochoa, who was recently spotted in the neighborhood. This interview has been edited and condensed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Remade Medellín, Colombia, Shows Off Its Style', 'kicker': 'Intersection', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Medellin (Colombia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oresti Tsonopoulos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oresti', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tsonopoulos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f956a78c-29cd-5d88-8902-b3d89e780d5e', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f956a78c-29cd-5d88-8902-b3d89e780d5e'}, {'abstract': 'Elisa and Amelia Ochoa, twins and founders of the website Sisterly Style, discuss fashion in Medellín’s Poblado neighborhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/fashion/100000003842989/intersection-medelln-colombia-fashion.html', 'snippet': 'Elisa and Amelia Ochoa, twins and founders of the website Sisterly Style, discuss fashion in Medellín’s Poblado neighborhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elisa and Amelia Ochoa, twins and founders of the website Sisterly Style, discuss fashion in Medellín’s Poblado neighborhood.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/07/multimedia/intersection-medellin/intersection-medellin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 