rge': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16liberland1/16liberland1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16liberland1/16liberland1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16liberland1/16liberland1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16liberland1/16liberland1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16liberland1/16liberland1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16liberland1/16liberland1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Welcome to Liberland, the World’s Newest Country (Maybe)', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Founder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jedlicka, Vit (1983- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis-Kraus, Gideon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Croatia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gideon Lewis-Kraus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gideon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis-Kraus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e34d7b1-d3e1-5220-b412-23aa91d779ec', 'word_count': 8747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e34d7b1-d3e1-5220-b412-23aa91d779ec'}, {'abstract': 'Like most things that were once cool because they positioned themselves against the mainstream, the rebel musician has been thoroughly co-opted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/magazine/how-rock-star-became-a-business-buzzword.html', 'snippet': 'Like most things that were once cool because they positioned themselves against the mainstream, the rebel musician has been thoroughly co-opted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once, a long time ago, a rock star was a free-spirited, convention-flouting artist/rebel/hero/Dionysian fertility god who fronted a world-famous band, sold millions of records and headlined stadium concerts where people were trampled in frenzies of cultlike fervor. Someone who smashed guitars, trashed hotel rooms, developed Byzantine drug problems and tried to mask evidence of his infidelity with the strategically applied scent of breakfast burritos. Despite what his ‘‘Behind the Music’’ episode would invariably reveal, a ‘‘rock star’’ — or the Platonic ideal of a rock star — was not just a powder keg of charisma and unresolved childhood issues, but a revolutionary driven by a need to assert the primacy of the self in an increasingly alienating commercial world.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16firstwords/16mag-16firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/