', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d48a3c8d-a670-59ed-82f5-f664f6f3058d', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d48a3c8d-a670-59ed-82f5-f664f6f3058d'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A meteor shower lights up the sky over Paris in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/1890-sky-streaked-with-meteors/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A meteor shower lights up the sky over Paris in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rain of meteors that streaked the sky with hundreds of fiery trails kept thousands of Parisians on the rooftops last night. It was a strange and fascinating sight. The absence of moonlight lent greater brilliancy to the huge bodies as they flashed through the starry sky and vanished. Many persons had provided themselves with telescopes after reading that the August shower of the Perseid group could be seen, but no lens, however powerful, could add to the silent grandeur of what could be seen with the naked eye.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, August 12, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-meteor/12iht-oldaug12-meteor-jumbo.png', 'height': 439, 'width': 373, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-meteor/12iht-oldaug12-meteor-superJumbo.png', 'height': 439, 'width': 373, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-meteor/12iht-oldaug12-meteor-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStand