fficial system.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Route to Conversion Challenges Israel’s Ultra-Orthodox Establishment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Route to Conversion Challenges Israel&#8217;s Ultra-Orthodox Establishment ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rabbis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T13:04:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfb74d98-a3b9-5be4-ab41-d5f56d5ff69c', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfb74d98-a3b9-5be4-ab41-d5f56d5ff69c'}, {'abstract': 'Google is adopting the Berkshire Hathaway model. The core Internet services of the company will still be called Google. And Twitter still hasn’t named a new chief executive, though the acting boss sure is acting like someone who plans to stick around.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/daily-report-google-remakes-itself-as-alphabet/', 'snippet': 'Google is adopting the Berkshire Hathaway model. The core Internet services of the company will still be called Google. And Twitter still hasn’t named a new chief executive, though the acting boss sure is acting like someone who plans to stick aro...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a major reinvention of one of the world’s most influential technology companies, Google announced Monday evening that it is reorganizing itself in the Berkshire Hathaway model. The n