tle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0d8c093-6ad1-501c-b2ca-8540b6c3e735', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0d8c093-6ad1-501c-b2ca-8540b6c3e735'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Britain fights off a Nazi attack on its coast in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/1940-british-fight-off-400-raiders/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Britain fights off a Nazi attack on its coast in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Out of a cloud-checked Sabbath sky over the English Channel, 400 Nazi warplanes struck yesterday at the British south coast naval bases of Portland and Weymouth, at balloon defense on the southeast coast in Kent and at a convoy. Two hundred German craft attacked Portland and Weymouth at one time. At 11:30 p.m., the Air Ministry said reports received up to 9 p.m. showed that sixty enemy planes had been shot down, five of them by anti-aircraft fire. The Ministry also raised the total of British losses from its first report of nineteen fighter planes lost to twenty-six, but said the pilots of two were saved.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, August 12, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-channeljets/12iht-oldaug12-channeljets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-channeljets/12iht-oldaug12-channeljets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-channeljets/12iht-oldaug12-channeljets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 571, 'width': 793, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_