-5c3c-8a83-b808cae87ec3'}, {'abstract': 'The Monocle Meter gets a workout from stories some saw as disgusting, but many readers talked about.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/from-underarm-hair-to-summer-turtlenecks-styles-trends-are-hot/', 'snippet': 'The Monocle Meter gets a workout from stories some saw as disgusting, but many readers talked about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the end of last year, I published a list of what I would like to see happen at The Times in 2015. Because I was having a little fun with the listicle format, which seems to require an odd, preferably prime, number in its title, I called it “17 Hopes and Dreams for The Times in the New Year.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Underarm Hair to Summer Turtlenecks, Styles Trends Are Hot', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T17:34:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2b588fa-fe6b-5c52-ba49-4995d9865cb7', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2b588fa-fe6b-5c52-ba49-4995d9865cb7'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Meyers is the first of his broadcast network peers to dispense with the stand-up comedy monologue, substituting instead a format that more closely resembles “Weekend Update” on “Saturday Night Live.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/12/arts/television/seth-meyers-decides-to-take-a-seat-to-deliver-his-late-night-monologue.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Meyers is the first of his broadcast network peers to dispense with the stand-up comedy monologue, substituting instead a format that more closely resembles “Weekend Update” on “Saturday Night Live.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When audience members at Monday’s broadcast of “Late Night” finished applauding and took their seats, the host Seth Meyers did something unusual: He sat down, too. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/arts/meyers/meyers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/12/arts/meyers/meyers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/arts/meyers/meyers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/arts/meyers/meyers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/arts/meyers/meyers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/12/arts/meyers/meyers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/arts/meyers/meyers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seth Meyers Decides to Take a Seat to Deliver His ‘Late Night’ Monologue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Comedy, but No Longer Stand-Up ', 'name': None,