m/2015/08/12/world/middleeast/palestinian-prisoners-case-tests-israeli-force-feeding-law.html', 'snippet': 'Mohammad Allan, who is on a hunger strike to protest his indefinite incarceration, could become the first Palestinian prisoner forced to stay alive under the law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASHKELON, Israel — The first Palestinian prisoner who could be forced to stay alive under a new Israeli law lies shackled to a hospital bed, vomiting bile and blood after 57 days of drinking only water to protest his indefinite incarceration without charges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/world/12Hungerstrike-web/12Hungerstrike-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/12/world/12Hungerstrike-web/12Hungerstrike-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/world/12Hungerstrike-web/12Hungerstrike-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/world/12Hungerstrike-web/12Hungerstrike-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/world/12Hungerstrike-web/12Hungerstrike-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/12/world/12Hungerstrike-web/12Hungerstrike-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/world/12Hungerstrike-web/12Hungerstrike-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Prisoner’s Case Tests Israeli Force-Feeding Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allan, Mohammad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T17:51:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diaa Hadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diaa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e90a8235-1250-5f18-98eb-277ee12245fa', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e90a8235-1250-5f18-98eb-277ee12245fa'}, {'abstract': 'Who won the competition among nations? The one percent.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/competitiveness-and-class-warfare/', 'snippet': 'Who won the competition among nations? The one percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For reasons not entirely clear to me, recently I found myself thinking about Lester Thurow’s Head to Head: The Coming Economic Battle Among Japan, Europe, and America. For those too young, or who don’t remember, Thurow’s book was a monster best-seller in the early 1990s; it resonated with many people who feared that America was losing its economic edge, that Japan was an unstoppable juggernaut, and so on. And it also played into the general notion of global economics as a struggle for competitive advantage, which is a perennial popular favorite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Competitiveness and Class Warfare', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T17:53:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/088d5a01-8c5f-5a5e-8ce6-f41adb048dc3', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/088d5a01-8c5f-5a5e-8ce6-f41adb048dc3'}, {'abstract': 'A rooftop enclave notable for its inventive drinks at One Fulton Square; whole-animal cooking in Bedford-Stuyvesant; and changes at Aldea and Kappo Masa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/12/dining/leaf-bar-and-lounge-joins-the-asian-rush-in-flushing.html', 'snippet': 'A rooftop enclave notable for its inventive drinks at One Fulton Square; whole-animal cooking in Bedford-Stuyvesant; and changes at Aldea and Kappo Masa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leaf Bar and Lounge Flushing, Queens, is already chockablock with Asian restaurants and bars, but this new rooftop enclave is notable for its inventive drinks, like a chrysanthemum old-fashioned. Leaf Bar and Lounge, which opens Wednesday, is on top of a Hyatt hotel at One Fulton Square. It is the latest in the growing collection of Asian restaurants in this new multistory complex. The bar offers a menu of small plates like pork-belly buns, yellowtail collar, dumplings and popcorn chicken. The chef is Henry Lin, a Taiwan native. Already open at One Fulton Square are the Coop, a bar and restaurant specializing in Korean fried chicken; Good Harvest, a branch of a big hot-pot chain in China; Rong Restaurant, for Chinese regional cuisine; and Iki, a Japanese restaurant with a variety of dishes and wagashi sweets: One Fulton Square, 39-16 Prince Street, (Roosevelt Avenue), Flushing, Queens, onefultonsquareflushing.com. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/dining/12OFF/12OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/12/dining/12OFF/12OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/dining/12OFF/12OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/dining/12OFF/12OFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/dining/12OFF/12OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/12/dining/12OFF/12OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/12/dining/12OFF/12OFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaf Bar and Lounge Joins the Asian Rush in Flushing', 'kicker': 'Off the Menu', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject'