'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4ea751e8-a159-5fba-840e-bcc936b6dd1b'}, {'abstract': 'A fortuneteller convicted in 2013 of swindling two women out of tens of thousands of dollars had appealed in part based on a possible mishandling of the notes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/12/nyregion/jury-notes-found-from-psychics-trial-may-weaken-her-appeal.html', 'snippet': 'A fortuneteller convicted in 2013 of swindling two women out of tens of thousands of dollars had appealed in part based on a possible mishandling of the notes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A mystery over two jury notes sent during a 2013 larceny trial of a Manhattan psychic has been resolved, dampening the hopes of the psychic, who has appealed her conviction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mystery Over Jury Notes in Manhattan Psychic’s Trial Is Solved', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, Sylvia E (1973- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychics and Psychic Phenomena', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fortune Telling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T20:26:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ec61737-d41d-553d-a7cb-21297e329cba', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ec61737-d41d-553d-a7cb-21297e329cba'}, {'abstract': 'While keeping a teenage driver on a family policy can increase premiums significantly, there are ways to reduce the cost.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/12/business/buying-car-insurance-for-teenagers-can-be-a-balancing-act.html', 'snippet': 'While keeping a teenage driver on a family policy can increase premiums significantly, there are ways to reduce the cost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adding a teenager to a family’s auto insurance policy is a sure way to raise the premiums, but it’s usually less expensive than buying a separate policy, according to new research.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buying Car Insurance for Teenagers Can Be a Balancing Act', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Insurance Institute for Highway Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'insuranceQuotes.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-11T20:27:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9a362da-2ea6-57ca-aa82-50948dd02573', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9a362da-2ea6-57ca-aa82-50948dd02573'}, {'abstract': 'The John W. Kluge Prize for Achievement in the Study of Humanity, recognizing work in disciplines not covered by the Nobel prizes, is awarded by the Library of Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/philosophers-jrgen-habermas-and-charles-taylor-to-share-1-5-million-prize/', 'snippet': 'The John W. Kluge Prize for Achievement in the Study of Humanity, recognizing work in disciplines not covered by the Nobel prizes, is awarded by the Library of Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The German philosopher Jürgen Habermas and the Canadian philosopher Charles Taylor will share this year’s $1.5 million John W. Kluge Prize for Achievement in the Study of Humanity. The prize, inaugurated in 2003 and awarded by the Library of Congress, is intended to recognize work in disciplines not covered by the Nobel prizes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/11HABERMAS/11HABERMAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/11HABERMAS/11HABERMAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/11HABERMAS/11HABERMAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/11HABERMAS/11HABERMAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/11HABERMAS/11HABERMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/11HABERMAS/11HABERMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank':