5906758', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/6298f691-eb8c-5d34-b7d1-ff3e65906758'}, {'abstract': 'Margot Perron and Mike Feller, paired for a summer as park rangers 32 years ago, did not stop their strolls together in the woods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/13/nyregion/many-long-walks-in-prospect-park-on-duty-then-a-kiss.html', 'snippet': 'Margot Perron and Mike Feller, paired for a summer as park rangers 32 years ago, did not stop their strolls together in the woods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lowly black walnut nearly ended their romance before it began.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Long Walks in Prospect Park, on Duty, Then a Kiss', 'kicker': 'Summer Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long Walks in the Park, While on Duty, Lead to a Kiss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu, Winnie (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feller, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-12T14:30:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcbcd627-52a4-5c12-aa0d-a365a547eda0', 'word_count': 1511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcbcd627-52a4-5c12-aa0d-a365a547eda0'}, {'abstract': 'Two novels reveal Haruki Murakami’s early interest in pop culture and slippery temporal realms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/books/review/haruki-murakami-wind-pinball-review.html', 'snippet': 'Two novels reveal Haruki Murakami’s early interest in pop culture and slippery temporal realms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than anyone, Haruki Murakami invented 21st-century fiction, which says as much about the 21st century as it does about Murakami. He is the novelist of our mash-up epoch and the subversive who, by intent or not, lit the fuse to whatever “canon” of the previous century anybody still takes seriously. Unless some aging secret master clandestinely labors away at the center of the Tokyo labyrinth, Murakami is the first major Japanese author born in the radioactive white light of the modern age that commenced in the zero-years of 1945, with nuclear decimation by the United States, and, even more traumatically, 1946, with the emperor’s admission to the Japanese public that he wasn’t divine.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16ERICKSON/16ERICKSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16ERICKSON/16ERICKSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16ERICKSON/16ERICKSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16ERICKSON/16ERICKSON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16ERICKSON/16ERICKSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16ERICKSON/16ERICKSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16ERICKSON/16ERICKSON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Haruki Murakami’s ‘Wind/Pinball’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Set Him Spinning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murakami, Haruki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goossen, Ted (Translator)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Wind/Pinball (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-12T14:31:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Erickson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erickson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e60689ae-8133-53be-9a48-a941d8c75849', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e60689ae-8133-53be-9a48-a941d8c75849'}, {'abstract': 'Lucia Berlin’s unadorned stories feature hard-pressed women and figures on the fringe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/books/review/a-manual-for-cleaning-women-by-lucia-berlin.html', 'snippet': 'Lucia Berlin’s unadorned stories feature hard-pressed women and figures on the fringe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some short story writers — \xadChekhov, Alice Munro, William Trevor — sidle up and tap you gently on the shoulder: Come, they murmur, sit down, listen to what I have to say. Lucia Berlin spins you around, knocks you down and grinds your face into the dirt. You will listen to me if I have to force you, her stories growl. But why would you make me do that, darlin’?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16FRANKLIN/0816-BKS-Franklin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16FRANKLIN/0816-BKS-Franklin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 526}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16FRANKLIN/0816-BKS-Franklin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 897, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16FRANKLIN/0816-BKS-Franklin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1795, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16FRANKLIN/0816-BKS-Franklin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16FRANKLIN/0816-BKS-Franklin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16FRANKLIN/0816-BKS-Franklin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘A Manual for Cleaning Women,’ by Lucia Berlin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marginal Gaze ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Ruth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlin, Lucia (1936-2004)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Manual for Cleaning Women (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-12T14:33:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth Franklin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Franklin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a894c81-41f9-5c37-ada8-bb2b7a852815', 'word_count': 1374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a894c81-41f9-5c37-ada8-bb2b7a852815'}, {'abstract': 'Francis’ identification with the poor derives from very distinctively Argentine forms of populism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/13/opinion/uki-goni-peronist-roots-of-pope-francis-politics.html', 'snippet': 'Francis’ identification with the poor derives from very distinctively Argentine forms of populism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — “I wish to join my voice to yours in calling for land, lodging and labor for all our brothers and sisters. I said it and I repeat it: These are sacred rights. It is important, it is well worth fighting for them.” The combative-sounding message of Pope Francis last month on his South American tour resonated deeply in a region where poverty continues to be the most pressing concern.', 'sou