orted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/521109ce-ff60-5b45-a5b4-b92ac002fb22', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/521109ce-ff60-5b45-a5b4-b92ac002fb22'}, {'abstract': 'A Doctors Without Borders spokeswoman said about 1,000 refugees on the island of Kos had been locked inside the stadium for 24 hours and had no food and very little water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/13/world/europe/greece-syria-iraq-migrants-locked-stadium-on-kos.html', 'snippet': 'A Doctors Without Borders spokeswoman said about 1,000 refugees on the island of Kos had been locked inside the stadium for 24 hours and had no food and very little water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — About a thousand refugees have been locked in a stadium on the Greek island of Kos overnight without food and with very little water, as Greek authorities struggle to contain the rising tide of migrants from war-torn countries, a spokeswoman for Doctors Without Borders said Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/world/KOS/KOS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/13/world/KOS/KOS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/world/KOS/KOS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/world/KOS/KOS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/world/KOS/KOS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/13/world/KOS/KOS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/world/KOS/KOS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Rounds Up Migrants on Kos, Locking Them in Stadium Overnight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece Gathers Hundreds of Migrants, Locking Them in Stadium Overnight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kos (Greece)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-12T15:07:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9cf7db9-db50-588f-bdfc-15ce7035fc14', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9cf7db9-db50-588f-bdfc-15ce7035fc14'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: President Johnson says the U.S. is present “to help” in Vietnam in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/12/1965-johnson-on-u-s-vietnam-role/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: President Johnson says the U.S. is present “to help” in Vietnam in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Johnson said today that the United States would not be making sacrifices in South Vietnam ‘‘if its help were not wanted and requested.’’ Mr. Johnson’s remarks, at the swearing in of Henry Cabot Lodge as U.S. ambassador to South Vietnam, were significant in light of reports that Mr. Lodge had told the Senate Foreign Relations Committee July 27 that the United States would keep its forces in South Vietnam even if the Saigon government asked them to leave. Spokesmen insisted yesterday that these reports were inaccurate. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, August 13, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen/13iht-oldaug13-wisemen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Johnson on U.S. Vietnam Role', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-12T15:16:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18204474-fb9a-5f26-b921-631362360d50', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18204474-fb9a-5f26-b921-631362360d50'}, {'abstract': 'A response (the first of two) to Katha Pollitt’s questions for the pro-life movement.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/12/pro-choice-questions-pro-life-answers/', 'snippet': 'A response (the first of two) to Katha Pollitt’s questions for the pro-life movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I turned a little bit\xa0intemperate in arguing about abortion with members of the conflicted center-left. Now I’m going to try to be a little calmer in pursuing a conversation with the not-at-all-conflicted pro-abortion left, by answering some of the questions\xa0that Katha Pollitt posed to her pro-life opponents last fall. I wanted to write a response at the time (she wrote up some of the answers she did receive\xa0here), but it slipped by the wayside; now that we’re in the throes of the\xa0ongoing Planned Parenthood controversy, it seems like an appropriate time to take her challenge\xa0up. So here are the first four of Pollitt’s (meaty) questions, in italics, with my (prolix) responses following; I’ll try to handle the remaining five by this time next week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pro-Choice Questions, Pro-Life Answers', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Education', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McArdle, Megan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollitt, Katha', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ponnuru, Ramesh', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations'