nd Ms. Lauryn Hill; progressive-pop virtuosity from the bassist Thundercat; enigmatic rapping from Danny Brown; metallic and noisy heaviness from Suicidal Tendencies and Death Grips; futuristic folk from Raury; traditional or mainstream blues and rock from Gary Clark Jr. and Lenny Kravitz.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE4/16GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE4/16GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE4/16GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE4/16GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE4/16GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE4/16GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE4/16GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Afropunk Festival in Brooklyn Explores All the Angles', 'kicker': 'Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Covering All the Angles ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Lauryn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Grace', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kravitz, Lenny', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-12T15:50:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc25fe2e-3222-5549-9d4e-3654428a7412', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc25fe2e-3222-5549-9d4e-3654428a7412'}, {'abstract': 'This darkly inventive chamber opera features the soprano Hila Plitmann and the mezzo Susan Bickley taking on a host of characters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/arts/music/george-benjamin-reimagines-the-pied-piper-in-into-the-little-hill.html', 'snippet': 'This darkly inventive chamber opera features the soprano Hila Plitmann and the mezzo Susan Bickley taking on a host of characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Benjamin’s brilliant opera “Written on Skin” was rightly heralded as the highlight of this summer’s Mostly Mozart Festival. If you weren’t able to snag a ticket, try Sunday’s performance of Mr. Benjamin’s “Into the Little Hill.” This 40-minute chamber opera is a darkly inventive reimagining of the tale of the Pied Piper of Hamelin as a political allegory, with a text by Martin Crimp, the poet behind the astonishingly original libretto to “Written on Skin.” The soprano Hila Plitmann and the mezzo Susan Bickley take on a host of characters, and many of the 15 musicians from the International Contemporary Ensemble multitask, too — watch for unusual instruments including bass flute, cimbalom, banjo and basset-horns.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE7/16GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 898, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE7/16GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 898}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE7/16GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 685, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE7/16GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1369, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE7/16GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE7/16GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE7/16GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'George Benjamin Reimagines the Pied Piper in ‘Into the Little Hill’', 'kicker': 'Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pied Piper&#8217;s Political Pull ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'