”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/movies/bigger-is-brighter-at-the-museum-of-the-moving-image.html', 'snippet': 'This week alone includes “Lawrence of Arabia” and the greatest New York musical, “West Side Story.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Table the tablet, shut down the smartphone. From outdoor movies to Imax blockbusters, summer seems built for living large. In that seasonal spirit, the Museum of the Moving Image’s intermittent series “See It Big!” has scheduled a program through Aug. 30 of features shot using 70-millimeter film for images that are brighter and sound that is richer than 35 millimeter can hope to provide. This week alone includes David Lean’s classic “Lawrence of Arabia” and the greatest New York musical, Jerome Robbins and Robert Wise’s “West Side Story.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE6SUB/16GUIDE6SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE6SUB/16GUIDE6SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE6SUB/16GUIDE6SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE6SUB/16GUIDE6SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1263, 'width': 1844, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE6SUB/16GUIDE6SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE6SUB/16GUIDE6SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE6SUB/16GUIDE6SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bigger Is Brighter at the Museum of the Moving Image', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Bigger Is Brighter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of the Moving Image', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-12T15:56:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aecc296b-92e7-5946-a8c2-58dcf0c463b6', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aecc296b-92e7-5946-a8c2-58dcf0c463b6'}, {'abstract': 'The playwright’s new work at the Signature Theater examines the late-in-life introspection of a wealthy widow determined to give away all her worldly possessions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/theater/ar-gurneys-love-money-wealth-a-widow-and-complications.html', 'snippet': 'The playwright’s new work at the Signature Theater examines the late-in-life introspection of a wealthy widow determined to give away all her worldly possessions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The playwright A. R. Gurney may have mused about retirement in the past, but he isn’t going anywhere. In his mid-80s, Mr. Gurney, the longtime chronicler of the white Anglo-Saxon Protestant experience, seems to have a play opening every week. Last season brought a revival of “Love Letters” on Broadway and two productions at the Signature Theater. A revival of his popular comedy “Sylvia” comes to Broadway in September. And his new “Love & Money,” now in previews for an Aug. 24 opening at the Signature, examines the late-in-life introspection of a wealthy widow named Cornelia Cunningham (played by Maureen Anderman) determined to give away all her worldly possessions. The plan of Ms. Cunningham, who is white, hits a snag when an African-American man (Gabriel Brown) arrives at her home saying that he is the child of her dead daughter, putting into question issues of inheritance. (Pershing Square Signature Theater, 212-244-7529, signaturetheatre.org.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE5/16GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE5/16GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE5/16GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE5/16GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE5/16GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16GUIDE5/16GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', '