mpetition in the world economic market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Donald J. Trump announced his run for president in June, much of the focus was on his explosive comments about Mexican immigrants. But he also had another target: China, which he mentioned at least a dozen times, saying, “They’re killing us” economically and that “China comes over and they dump all their stuff” on American markets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump Takes On China After Devaluation', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-12T16:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaffea6e-3625-56e2-821c-142a0dd4ef92', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaffea6e-3625-56e2-821c-142a0dd4ef92'}, {'abstract': 'A lover of dance tells why he’ll always remember the infinite variety of a mezzo-soprano’s 1970s opera performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/13/arts/music/janet-bakers-voice-a-singular-instrument-lingers-like-no-other.html', 'snippet': 'A lover of dance tells why he’ll always remember the infinite variety of a mezzo-soprano’s 1970s opera performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dance was not the first love of my life among the arts. Growing up in the English countryside, I lived for hours on end in books and beside the gramophone; the first performing art to obsess me was opera. When I first attended opera, at 17, it immediately proved addictive.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/arts/10MACAULY/10MACAULY-articleLarge-v4.gif', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/10/arts/10MACAULY/10MACAULY-articleLarge-v4.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/arts/10MACAULY/10MACAULY-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/arts/10MACAULY/10MACAULY-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/arts/10MACAULY/10MACAULY-thumbStandard-v4.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/10/arts/10MACAULY/10MACAULY-thumbStandard-v4.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/10/arts/10MACAULY/10MACAULY-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Janet Baker’s Voice, a Singular Instrument, Lingers Like No Other', 'kicker': 'Virgin Eyes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Voice Heard Repeatedly, Lingering Like No Other', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macaulay, Alastair (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Janet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'La Clemenza di Tito (Opera)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-12T16:53:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/731749f0-c4c7-5280-a3d2-a076c9bb8f80', 'word_count': 1334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/731749f0-c4c7-5280-a3d2-a076c9bb8f80'}, {'abstract': 'Noah Baumbach and Greta Gerwig talk about some of the films that helped inspire their latest collaboration, “Mistress America.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/movies/for-mistress-america-noah-baumbach-and-greta-gerwig-serve-screwball-with-a-whiff-of-menace.html', 'snippet': 'Noah Baumbach and Greta Gerwig talk about some of the films that helped inspire their latest collaboration, “Mistress America.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Both of Noah Baumbach’s parents reviewed movies when he was growing up in Brooklyn — his father, Jonathan Baumbach, for Partisan Review, and his mother, Georgia Brown, for The Village Voice. So it may not be a surprise that Mr. Baumbach, 45, became a writer-director whose films often pay homage to screen influences like Woody Allen and Hal Ashby.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16MISTRESS1/16MISTRESS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16MISTRESS1/16MISTRESS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16MISTRESS1/16MISTRESS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16MISTRESS1/16MISTRESS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16MISTRESS1/16MISTRESS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16MISTRESS1/16MISTRESS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16MISTRESS1/16MISTRESS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For ‘Mistress America,’ Noah Baumbach and Greta Gerwig Serve Screwball With a Whiff of Menace', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Screwball With a Whiff of Menace ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baumbach, Noah', 'rank': 3, 'major