ce-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Matthew Neenan’s two-act ballet, about a 1938 airmail flight and its crash, with scenes set in Auckland, New Zealand, and in Pago Pago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A plane crash may seem like unusual fodder for a story ballet, though the longer you spend with Matthew Neenan’s “Sunset, o639 Hours,” the more related ballet and aviation appear to be: twin forms of flight and propulsion through space. This two-act work for Philadelphia’s terrific BalletX, presented as part of the Joyce Theater’s Ballet Festival on Tuesday, revolves around the American pilot Edwin Musick, who in 1938 manned the first airmail flight from New Zealand to Hawaii. The Samoan Clipper, as his aircraft was known, went down on its return trip, just off the Samoan coast.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/arts/13balletx/13balletx-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/13/arts/13balletx/13balletx-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/arts/13balletx/13balletx-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/arts/13balletx/13balletx-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1287, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/arts/13balletx/13balletx-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/13/arts/13balle