erson': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7cdb4b6-3715-5ba7-a8ae-167809bc5da0', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7cdb4b6-3715-5ba7-a8ae-167809bc5da0'}, {'abstract': 'When Yana Paskova visited Cuba, her eyes — and heart — were attuned to details that summoned her childhood in Communist Bulgaria.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/13/cuba-reliving-memories-of-communism/', 'snippet': 'When Yana Paskova visited Cuba, her eyes — and heart — were attuned to details that summoned her childhood in Communist Bulgaria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most Americans who visit Cuba recall having a time machine moment: their grandfather’s Chevy, showgirls at the Tropicana, or the absent reach of email. My version of time travel included a Lada and a red scarf — two symbols of my childhood in Bulgaria, a Communist nation that turned to democracy after the fall of the Berlin Wall in 1989.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuba: Reliving Memories of Communism', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitalism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Communism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ladies in White (Cuba)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bulgaria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eastern Europe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date':