 'lead_paragraph': '“Straight Outta Compton,” an exultant rap-to-riches story about the group N.W.A., opens with a blast of action-film braggadocio. It’s night sometime in 1986, and the group’s future headliner and fly in the ointment, Eazy-E (Jason Mitchell), is taking care of shady business. With the camera dogging his steps so closely that you half expect him to shout “Heel,” he hotfoots it into a cramped, bleak house that has been prepped for maximum horror-film suggestiveness, with lighting as dark as a dungeon, a Welcome Wagon of tough-guy scowls and a she-devil who’s soon holding a shotgun next to a bare leg, her gat and her gam each loaded and lethal.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/world/14straight-web/14straight-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/world/14straight-web/14straight-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/world/14straight-web/14straight-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/world/14straight-web/14straight-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/world/14straight-web/14straight-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/14/world/14straight-web/14straight-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/world/14straight-web/14straight-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Straight Outta Compton,’ Upstarts Who Became the Establishment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Upstarts to Establishment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dargis, Manohla (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, F Gary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Jackson, O'Shea Jr", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawkins, Corey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, Jason', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Straight Outta Compton (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5a38d8e-8e62-5dd0-93f5-b4a1268c8dce', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5a38d8e-8e62-5dd0-93f5-b4a1268c8dce'}, {'abstract': 'In summer, when room rates are lower and tables accessible, hiking trails through forests and flower-filled meadows beckon, and enticing meals are never far away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/travel/italy-dolomites-hiking-trekking-camping.html', 'snippet': 'In summer, when room rates are lower and tables accessible, hiking trails through forests and flower-filled meadows beckon, and enticing meals are never far away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most sensible approach to the Alpine geological wonderland known as the Dolomites is also the most evocative one. Here’s how it’s done: After the three-hour drive from Venice Marco Polo Airport toward Austria, pull off the autostrada into the inviting city of Bolzano.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16DOLOMITES/16DOLOMITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16DOLOMITES/16DOLOMITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16DOLOMITES/16DOLOMITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16DOLOMITES/16DOLOMITES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16DOLOMITES/16DOLOMITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16DOLOMITES/16DOLOMITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16DOLOMITES/16DOLOMITES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Italy, Hiking and Haute Cuisine in the Dolomites', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Heart of the Dolomites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Draper, Robert (1959- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hikes and Hiking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Draper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1d4c510-1767-53ec-ae97-e6a33f94c654', 'word_count': 3003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1d4c510-1767-53ec-ae97-e6a33f94c654'}, {'abstract': 'Before we say categorically that there is a moral imperative to destroy groups like ISIS, we must consider the moral cost.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/13/in-the-age-of-isis-can-we-still-have-just-wars/', 'snippet': 'Before we say categorically that there is a moral imperative to destroy groups like ISIS, we must consider the moral cost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This interview, the seventh in a series on political topics, discusses philosophical issues concerning the morality of war. My interviewee is Cecile Fabre, professor of political philosophy at the University of Oxford. She is the author of “Cosmopolitan War.” — Gary Gutting', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-thestone/opinionator-pog-thestone-articleLarge.png', 'height