': '1940: Britain May Lift Blockade', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoover, Herbert Clark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T13:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9db7a31-db8d-5ff8-b53c-167c7de9d9f1', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9db7a31-db8d-5ff8-b53c-167c7de9d9f1'}, {'abstract': 'Home-grown or appropriating American elements, hip-hop is emerging in a music scene dominated by glossy K-pop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/arts/music/getting-rowdy-keith-ape-and-real-rap-in-korea.html', 'snippet': 'Home-grown or appropriating American elements, hip-hop is emerging in a music scene dominated by glossy K-pop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time the South Korean rapper Keith Ape made it to the nightclub S.O.B.’s in April for his first New York show, just three months had passed since the release of “It G Ma,” his breakout single.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/arts/16APE1/16APE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legac