ed novellas, in a new collection titled “Fortune Smiles.” Its author is Adam Johnson, who won the 2013 Pulitzer Prize for his novel about North Korea, “The Orphan Master’s Son.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16GROFF/16GROFF-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16GROFF/16GROFF-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 322}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16GROFF/16GROFF-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16GROFF/16GROFF-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 982, 'width': 1827, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16GROFF/16GROFF-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16GROFF/16GROFF-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/16GROFF/16GROFF-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Adam Johnson’s ‘Fortune Smiles’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knots of Anxiety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'valu