 fell 51 percent in the second quarter. Revamping may halt losses at the Motorola handset unit that Lenovo bought last year. But any return to growth depends on a demand pickup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Lenovo, Cost-Cutting Is Not Enough to Stem Losses', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lenovo Group', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T20:07:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robyn Mak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/284fac8b-b4db-5b54-a996-1a362e6bcfe8', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/284fac8b-b4db-5b54-a996-1a362e6bcfe8'}, {'abstract': 'Critics of the nuclear agreement think we can revert to sanctions. But doing so would be an economic disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/opinion/the-high-price-of-rejecting-the-iran-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Critics of the nuclear agreement think we can revert to sanctions. But doing so would be an economic disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — THE Iran nuclear deal offers a long-term solution to one of the most urgent threats of our time. Without this deal, Iran, the world’s leading state sponsor of terrorism, would be less than 90 days away from having enough fissile material to make a nuclear bomb. This deal greatly reduces the threat of Iran’s nuclear program, making Iran’s breakout time four times as long, securing unprecedented access to 