al tale involving normal tensions of adolescence and the need for independence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “One & Two,” an isolated family of four is about to go nuclear. Dad (Grant Bowler) runs a very tight ship on a very tidy homestead in a rural paradise, walled off from the outside world and apparently lacking any technology more recent than kerosene lamps. Mom (Elizabeth Reaser) pretty much goes along, except to try to soothe her husband when he rages about their teenagers, Zac (Timothée Chalamet) and Eva (Kiernan Shipka). They have powers, you see, that must be shunned.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ONETWO/ONETWO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ONETWO/ONETWO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ONETWO/ONETWO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ONETWO/ONETWO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ONETWO/ONETWO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ONETWO/ONETWO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ONETWO/ONETWO-thum