content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Devaluation That Could Escalate a Currency War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eavis, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renminbi (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T20:58:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/96920a00-9b5a-52b6-94ac-c455c0b5a4b2', 'word_count': 1327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96920a00-9b5a-52b6-94ac-c455c0b5a4b2'}, {'abstract': 'Aviva Kempner’s documentary offers a stirring portrait of a Sears executive whose Rosenwald Fund dispensed fellowships to black artists and academics including W. E. B. Du Bois and James Baldwin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/movies/review-rosenwald-on-a-philanthropist-who-created-schools-for-blacks-in-the-jim-crow-south.html', 'snippet': 'Aviva Kempner’s documentary offers a stirring portrait of a Sears executive whose Rosenwald Fund dispensed fellowships to black artists and academics including W. E. B. Du Bois and James Baldwin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the first half of the 20th century, Julius Rosenwald was not only a leading businessman — the chairman of Sears, Roebuck & Company, one of the country’s wealthiest men — but a leading philanthropist and civil rights advocate as well. With challenge grants, he spurred the building of Y.M.C.A.s that would accept blacks as residents; his Rosenwald Fund dispensed fellowships for a who’s who of black artists and academics, from W. E. B. Du Bois to James Baldwin.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ROSENWALD/14ROSENWALD-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ROSENWALD/14ROSENWALD-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 764}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ROSENWALD/14ROSENWALD-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ROSENWALD/14ROSENWALD-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1609, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ROSENWALD/14ROSENWALD-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ROSENWALD/14ROSENWALD-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14ROSENWALD/14ROSENWALD-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Rosenwald,’ on a Philanthropist Who Created Schools for Blacks in the Jim Crow South', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Review: ‘Rosenwald,’ on a Philanthropist Who Created Schools for Blacks in the Jim Crow South', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kempner, Aviva', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenwald, Julius', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rosenwald (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T20:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/47811e81-2bef-53c7-8bce-bd3c46e9853f', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47811e81-2bef-53c7-8bce-bd3c46e9853f'}, {'abstract': 'Experts said the unredacted audit was the first acknowledgment of how the Postal Service’s surveillance program for national security investigations is used.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/us/copy-of-postal-service-audit-shows-extent-of-mail-surveillance.html', 'snippet': 'Experts said the unredacted audit was the first acknowledgment of how the Postal Service’s surveillance program for national security investigations is used.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In what experts say is the first acknowledgment of how the United States Postal Service’s mail surveillance program for national security investigations is used, the service’s internal watchdog found that inspectors failed to follow key safeguards in the gathering and handling of classified information.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_pa