8-19718375d6d3'}, {'abstract': 'The musical, with music and lyrics by Benj Pasek and Justin Paul, will be staged Off Broadway, though its commercial producer didn’t rule out further life on Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/13/second-stage-adds-dear-evan-hansen-to-spring-season/', 'snippet': 'The musical, with music and lyrics by Benj Pasek and Justin Paul, will be staged Off Broadway, though its commercial producer didn’t rule out further life on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new musical about suicide, social media and a group of angsty high school students will be presented at Second Stage Theater next spring after a production at Arena Stage in Washington received strong reviews.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/13BLOGEVANHANSEN/13BLOGEVANHANSEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/13BLOGEVANHANSEN/13BLOGEVANHANSEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/13BLOGEVANHANSEN/13BLOGEVANHANSEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/13BLOGEVANHANSEN/13BLOGEVANHANSEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/13BLOGEVANHANSEN/13BLOGEVANHANSEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/13BLOGEVANHANSEN/13BLOGEVANHANSEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/13BLOGEVANHANSEN/13BLOGEVANHANSEN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Stage Adds ‘Dear Evan Hansen’ To Spring Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greif, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levenson, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pasek, Benj', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Justin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Platt, Ben (1993- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARENA STAGE', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Second Stage Theater', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T21:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Paulson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paulson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd7cabfc-11c9-5719-90b0-5ea45c6d54a0', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd7cabfc-11c9-5719-90b0-5ea45c6d54a0'}, {'abstract': 'This week, the company founded by the choreographer makes its New York debut.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/13/emery-lecrone-dance-joyce-theater/', 'snippet': 'This week, the company founded by the choreographer makes its New York debut.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You haven’t said anything yet,” the choreographer Emery LeCrone tells the dancers Shane Ohmer and Izabela Szylinska in rehearsal. They face each other, each with a hand on the other’s shoulder, and move closer. LeCrone pauses. “Now you have the conversation.” It’s the intensity of this movement — a silent yet intimate exchange between the dancers — that is emblematic of LeCrone’s choreographic style. While working within the classical vocabulary, LeCrone incorporates pedestrian movements — touching hands, hugging — that are strikingly tender. The steps look like ballet, but they’re less formal, more rugged and athletic — and her dancers are certainly not afraid of the floor. “When you go to a big theater and watch 20 dancers on a huge stage, it can feel very distant,” says LeCrone. “But ballet doesn’t have to be that way. It can be more approachable and emotional, less stark and refined.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emery LeCrone’s Intimate (and Often Emotional) Dance', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LeCrone, Emery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T21:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Madison Mainwaring', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Madison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mainwaring', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df193d3a-4885-53ed-8125-4860dceecb68', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df193d3a-4885-53ed-8125-4860dceecb68'}, {'abstract': 'In this sci-fi film set in an underground missile silo, the actions of two men could decide the fate of civilization.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/movies/review-in-air-norman-reedus-and-djimon-hounsou-keep-hope-and-themselves-alive.html', 'snippet': 'In this sci-fi film set in an underground missile silo, the actions of two men could decide the fate of civilization.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We can’t just decide who lives and who dies!” one character says in “Air.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14AIR/14AIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14AIR/14AIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14AIR/14AIR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14AIR/14AIR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14AIR/14AIR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14AIR/14AIR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14AIR/14AIR-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Air,’ Norman Reedus and Djimon Hounsou Keep Hope, and Themselves, Alive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Review: In ‘Air,’ Norman Reedus and Djimon Hounsou Keep Hope, and Themselves, Alive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Air (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantamessa, Christian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hounsou, Djimon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reedus, Norman', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pasetto, Chris (1971- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T21:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/60185980-5c21-5b5a-9217-871353b14dd0', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60185980-5c21-5b5a-9217-871353b14dd0'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Thorne plays a teenager with a dread of open spaces who must surmount her terror to save her mother and herself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/movies/review-in-big-sky-starring-bella-thorne-mortal-fears-collide.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Thorne plays a teenager with a dread of open spaces who must surmount her terror to save her mother and herself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actress Bella Thorne (“The Duff”; MTV’s “Scream”) dips her toes into grown-up desert noir with “Big Sky,” a lean exercise that leaves her over her head. Ms. Thorne plays Hazel, a teenager with acute agoraphobia and obsessive-compulsive disorder. Her lonely, mildly disheveled mother, Dee (Kyra Sedgwick), is accompanying her to a treatment center when the van carrying Hazel, Dee and four others is violently ambushed in a sandy wasteland. (The film was shot in New Mexico.) Their assailants are kidnappers (Aaron Tveit and Frank Grillo) who believe they have killed all the passengers save their quarry (Jodi Lynn Thomas), whom they stick in a car trunk. But Dee, though shot, is still alive, and Hazel, who has witnessed the carnage from a concealed spot, must surmount her fears to seek help in the wilderness.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14BIGSKY/14BIGSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14BIGSKY/14BIGSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14BIGSKY/14BIGSKY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14BIGSKY/14BIGSKY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14BIGSKY/14BIGSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14BIGSKY/14BIGSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14BIGSKY/14BIGSKY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'le