rah (Film Director)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renier, Jeremie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sugaipov, Surho (1985- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Idiev, Ramzan (2001- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T22:34:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f4d995a-791c-5da4-93f4-32076955a993', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f4d995a-791c-5da4-93f4-32076955a993'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Delphine Diaw Diallo’s “Highness” series originated as a collaboration with the hairstylist Joanne Petit Frere.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/13/delphine-diaw-diallo-photographs/', 'snippet': 'The photographer Delphine Diaw Diallo’s “Highness” series originated as a collaboration with the hairstylist Joanne Petit Frere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Delphine Diaw Diallo’s “Highness” series originated a few years ago as a collaboration with the hairstylist Joanne Petit Frere, who creates fantastical, sculptural styles with real hair. Frere asked Diallo, a graduate of the Academie Charpentier of Visual Arts in Paris, to photograph her work, and the two started working together\xa0on a series of increasingly revealing portraits. Diallo, who was born to a Senegalese father and a French mother in Paris, was attracted to the idea of women recreating themselves — and wanted to challenge traditional notions of femininity and eminence. “What kind of queen can I create?” she says. “How can I redefine what highness means to a woman’s experience?” To her, the true “highnesses” are warriors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos That Celebrate — and Challenge — Feminine Ideals', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T22:35:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Esin Ili Goknar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Esin', 'middlename': 'Ili', 'lastname': 'Goknar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df3f675e-3e8e-5eef-8704-50f5866414ce', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df3f675e-3e8e-5eef-8704-50f5866414ce'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/nyregion/things-to-do-in-new-jersey-aug-16-to-22-2015.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in New Jersey. Items for the calendar should be sent at least three weeks in advance to njtowns@nytimes.com.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16HINJ1/16HINJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16HINJ1/16HINJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 602}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16HINJ1/16HINJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1020, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy