article/3223613a-f6a1-58dd-965e-2aad1a511c22'}, {'abstract': 'This smart, fast-paced film, advertised as a screwball comedy, subverts this most buoyant of genres with a steady undertow of anxiety, dread and anger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/movies/review-mistress-america-a-noah-baumbach-comedy-on-getting-by-in-a-backbiting-world.html', 'snippet': 'This smart, fast-paced film, advertised as a screwball comedy, subverts this most buoyant of genres with a steady undertow of anxiety, dread and anger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Noah Baumbach’s “Mistress America” advertises itself as a screwball comedy. But this smart, fast-paced film is not really the zany, lighter-than-air divertissement that the term usually conjures. There are scattered sharp one-liners, but not enough to infuse the movie with a sustained bonhomie. It’s fair to say that “Mistress America” revises and subverts this most buoyant of genres with a steady undertow of anxiety, dread and anger. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14MISTRESS/14MISTRESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14MISTRESS/14MISTRESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14MISTRESS/14MISTRESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14MISTRESS/14MISTRESS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1032, 'width': 1909, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14MISTRESS/14MISTRESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14MISTRESS/14MISTRESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14MISTRESS/14MISTRESS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Mistress America,’ a Noah Baumbach Comedy on Getting By in a Backbiting World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Madcap New Yorker, Trying to Get Ahead in a Backbiting World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baumbach, Noah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gerwig, Greta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erbe, Kathryn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mistress America (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T23:02:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd5b5785-9bcd-5728-bdbd-bf04dc94f34c', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd5b5785-9bcd-5728-bdbd-bf04dc94f34c'}, {'abstract': 'Xavier Dolan directs and stars in this film about a bereaved lover who discovers that his boyfriend’s family had no idea that he had a gay companion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/movies/review-in-tom-at-the-farm-psychosexual-games-down-at-the-farm.html', 'snippet': 'Xavier Dolan directs and stars in this film about a bereaved lover who discovers that his boyfriend’s family had no idea that he had a gay companion.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Tom at the Farm,” the fourth film from the 26-year-old French Canadian wunderkind Xavier Dolan, is a teasing exercise in unfettered narcissism that sticks its out tongue out and goes, “Nyah, nyah, nyah” as if it were a 5-year-old running wild on a sugar high. I should add that the movie, completed in 2013 and just now being released, is wildly entertaining, sexy and beautifully shot in the Canadian heartland.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14TOMFARM/14TOMFARM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14TOMFARM/14TOMFARM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14TOMFARM/14TOMFARM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14TOMFARM/14TOMFARM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1440, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14TOMFARM/14TOMFARM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14TOMFARM/14TOMFARM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14TOMFARM/14TOMFARM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Tom at the Farm,’ Psychosexual Games Down at the Farm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Between the Chores Down at the Farm, Psychosexual Games', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, Xavier', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Tom at the Farm (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T23:04:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/93cdbda7-615d-593d-b1a7-0de4de9f02cc', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93cdbda7-615d-593d-b1a7-0de4de9f02cc'}, {'abstract': 'Playwrights and producers discuss whether having been in the 2014 New York International Fringe Festival was worth all the time, effort and money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/theater/last-years-fringe-festival-successes-look-back.html', 'snippet': 'Playwrights and producers discuss whether having been in the 2014 New York International Fringe Festival was worth all the time, effort and money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Fringe festival can be a real boon for theatergoers, offering the chance to binge on a variety of new plays, musicals and other performances. Best of all, in most cases you can gluttonously feed your theater addiction without spending a ton of money: Tickets for shows at the forthcoming New York International Fringe Festival, for example, are just $18.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGE01/14FRINGE01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGE01/14FRINGE01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGE01/14FRINGE01-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGE01/14FRINGE01-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGE01/14FRINGE01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGE01/14FRINGE01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGE01/14FRINGE01-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Year Later, Fringe Festival Shows Measure Their Success', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All That Work Just to Get on a Tiny Stage for a Few Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York International Fringe Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-13T23:14:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18464fec-4060-54f9-83ee-0cf20aea6465', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18464fec-4060-54f9-83ee-0cf20aea6465'}, {'abstract': '“Elaine Stritch: Still Here,” “Exact Change” and “Naked Hamilton” are among the shows in this year’s FringeNYC, which opens on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/theater/10-shows-to-watch-for-at-this-years-new-york-fringe-festival.html', 'snippet': '“Elaine Stritch: Still Here,” “Exact Change” and “Naked Hamilton” are among the shows in this year’s FringeNYC, which opens on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will participants in the 2015 New York International Fringe Festival be glad they performed, once this year’s frenzy is over? First they need audiences. Using methods mostly instinctual, editors and writers for The New York Times put their heads together for a list of 10 shows they’re anticipating among the 200 productions. (Dates, times and sites are at fringenyc.org.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGEsidebar/14FRINGEsidebar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGEsidebar/14FRINGEsidebar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/14/arts/14FRINGEsidebar/14FRINGEsidebar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 