-restaurant-joanina-in-huntington.html', 'snippet': 'A family deli business evolved into Restaurant Joanina, complete with a wine shop next door.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Was this downtown Huntington or a town in Tuscany? I counted nine restaurants with outdoor seating within a one-block radius. One of the most appealing spots was Restaurant Joanina. While most of the competition had sidewalk seating in front of a noisy street, Joanina faced a parking lot (a slight improvement) and its tables were separated from that lot by planters overflowing with flowers. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16DINELI1/16DINELI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16DINELI1/16DINELI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16DINELI1/16DINELI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16DINELI1/16DINELI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16DINELI1/16DINELI1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16DINELI1/16DINELI1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16DINELI1/16DINELI1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: A Classically Italian Menu at Restaurant Joanina in Huntington', 'kicker': 'Dining | Huntington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classically Italian, and Fueled by Family ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Huntington (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Restaurant Joanina (Huntington, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-14T00:02:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Starkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e39235cd-1af3-5691-88c7-15ecb0b65194', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e39235cd-1af3-5691-88c7-15ecb0b65194'}, {'abstract': 'The water just below a Colorado mine that poured three million gallons of toxic waste into nearby waterways has returned to pre-spill levels of toxicity, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/us/colorado-water-near-mine-at-pre-spill-toxicity.html', 'snippet': 'The water just below a Colorado mine that poured three million gallons of toxic waste into nearby waterways has returned to pre-spill levels of toxicity, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The water just below a Colorado mine that poured three million gallons of toxic waste into nearby waterways has returned to pre-spill levels of toxicity, officials said Thursday. The Environmental Protection Agency is still analyzing water farther along the spill’s path — in New Mexico, the Navajo Nation and Utah. Officials in Utah said waste from the mine had probably reached Lake Powell, a major water storage facility for the region. E.P.A. officials have said they will have to monitor the spill’s path for years to understand its full effect. The Gold King Mine, near Silverton, burst on Aug. 5 while workers contracted by the E.P.A. were conducting a field investigation of the mine, which had leaked for years. The agency has said it was responsible for the spill. Levels of metals including arsenic and lead jumped in local waterways as the contamination flowed down the Animas River and into the San Juan, angering many who use these rivers for drinking, irrigation and recreational activities. Colorado, New Mexico, Utah and the Navajo Nation declared states of emergency. The rivers remained closed Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colorado: Water Near Mine at Pre-Spill Toxicity ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Rockies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colorado: Water Near Mine at Pre-Spill Toxicity ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Animas River (Colo-NM)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-14T00:10:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Turkewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turkewitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa1367e5-aba6-53be-b62e-9e35e4b00713', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa1367e5-aba6-53be-b62e-9e35e4b00713'}, {'abstract': 'The death of a baby whose mother is accused of throwing him from a window has gripped the social service providers trying to address mental health problems of Bangladeshis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/nyregion/bangladeshi-women-isolated-in-new-york-city-need-more-support-advocates-say.html', 'snippet': 'The death of a baby whose mother is accused of throwing him from a window has gripped the social service providers trying to address mental health problems of Bangladeshis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 3-week-old baby ended up dead in the courtyard of an apartment building in Queens. The police arrested the mother, Rashida Chowdhury, a 21-year-old Bangladeshi immigrant, on charges of second-degree murder. They said she confessed to throwing the baby out the bathroom window of her fourth-floor apartment because she thought the child was possessed by an evil spirit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bangladeshi Women, Isolated in New York City, Need More Support, Advocates Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Death of Baby Grips Mental Health Advocates for Bangladeshi Women in City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chowdhury, Rashida (August 7, 2015 Murder)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmad, Rizwan (2015-15)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bangladeshi-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Richmond Hill (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-14T00:16:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f83742ab-b1a9-5135-b152-a30d7ff8ed98', 'word_count': 971, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f83742ab-b1a9-5135-b152-a30d7ff8ed98'}, {'abstract': 'Martha Nelson, a former editor in chief of Time Inc., will join Yahoo as its global editor in chief, overseeing its portfolio of digital magazines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/business/media/former-editor-of-time-inc-to-lead-yahoo-magazines.html', 'snippet': 'Martha Nelson, a former editor in chief of Time Inc., will join Yahoo as its global editor in chief, overseeing its portfolio of digital magazines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martha Nelson, a former editor in chief of Time Inc., will join Yahoo as its global editor in chief, the company said Thursday, overseeing its portfolio of digital magazines. Ms. Nelson, the founding editor of InStyle and a former editor of People magazine, had taken the top editorial job at Time Inc. in 2013. But she left later that year in a shake-up that eliminated her position and had editors of the company’s 21 magazines reporting to the business side. She will be based in New York when she starts her new job next week, Yahoo said, and will focus on developing Yahoo’s 13 domestic digital magazines and 30 international magazines. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Editor of Time Inc. to Lead Yahoo Magazines', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Editor of Time Inc. to Lead Yahoo 