h at a safe distance, somewhere out of reach but visible. Every day, inch it closer until you can hold the brush in your hand while you teach the gorilla to open its mouth. To do this, reward it with grapes, slices of apple, popcorn or juice (Crystal Light is an ape favorite). The first time an animal completes the desired behavior, ‘‘jackpot’’ it, offering 10 grapes instead of one. ‘‘Then they’re like, ‘Oh, whatever I just did I should do it again,’\u2009’’ Carrigan says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16tip/16mag-16tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16tip/16mag-16tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 597}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16tip/16mag-16tip-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1019, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16tip/16mag-16tip-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1900, 'width': 1910, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16tip/16mag-16tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16tip/16mag-16tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16tip/16mag-16tip-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Brush a Gorilla’s Teeth', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Brush a Gorilla’s Teeth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wollan, Malia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrigan, Jodi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zoo Atlanta', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-14T10:58:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e59be0f8-3baf-5ae7-9749-99ae1611f0bf', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e59be0f8-3baf-5ae7-9749-99ae1611f0bf'}, {'abstract': 'Selected by Natasha Trethewey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/magazine/more-than-once.html', 'snippet': 'Selected by Natasha Trethewey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So much depends on the precision of language. In this seemingly plain-spoken poem, ‘‘tears’’ suggests not only a literal image but also an abstract one. In that trick the eye plays on the mind, I see at once the rips in the fence and a glimpse at the emotion such a crossing — ‘‘a little dangerous’’ — can engender.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/magazine/16poem/16poem-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 208, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name