t the ultimate down-home event, the Iowa State Fair, in the state with the first nominating contest? Knowing what to eat is part of the challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every presidential election cycle, candidates face a big test at the Iowa State Fair: Can they fit in with the locals at the ultimate down-home event in the state with the first nominating contest? Knowing what to eat is part of the challenge: corn dogs, fried butter, and apple pie on a stick are just some of the cholesterol-filled favorites. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Draft Focus: It’s Heigh-Ho, Come to the (Iowa) Fair!', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State and County Fairs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-14T14:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21a9f69f-0264-5481-906a-919cee2c117d', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21a9f69f-0264-5481-906a-919cee2c117d'}, {'abstract': 'In this debut novel, a crime sets a woman’s life on an entirely new course.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/books/review/eileen-by-ottessa-moshfegh.html', 'snippet': 'In this debut novel, a crime sets a woman’s life on an entirely new course.', 'lead_paragraph': ' “I looked like a girl you’d expect to see on a city bus,” begins “Eileen,” Ottessa Moshfegh’s seductive novel, “reading some clothbound book from the library about plants or geography, perhaps wearing a net over my light brown hair.” This is the eponymous Eileen, and we quickly learn that any assumptions we might make about her from her appearance would be dead wrong. “I didn’t really read books about flowers or home economics,” she tells us a few pages later. “I liked books about awful things — murder, illness, death.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/0816-BKS-King/0816-BKS-King-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/0816-BKS-King/0816-BKS-King-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/0816-BKS-King/0816-BKS-King-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/0816-BKS-King/0816-BKS-King-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1303, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/0816-BKS-King/0816-BKS-King-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/0816-BKS-King/0816-BKS-King-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/books/review/0816-BKS-King/0816-BKS-King-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Eileen,’ by Ottessa Moshfegh', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where She Got the Gun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moshfegh, Ottessa (1981- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Eileen (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-14T14:47:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily King', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'King', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dfc31f5-026c-5e02-8f45-0ad8bf81e75b', 'word_count': 1362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dfc31f5-026c-5e02-8f45-0ad8bf81e75b'}, {'abstract': 'Fetal tissue is not only being used in potentially life-saving medical research, it has already saved countless lives.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/14/why-we-need-fetal-tissue-research/', 'snippet': 'Fetal tissue is not only being used in potentially life-saving medical research, it has already saved countless lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hidden-camera videos showing Planned Parenthood staffers discussing fetal tissue donations have led not just to efforts to defund the organization, but to calls for an end to the use of fetal tissue in research. In an article in The New England Journal of Medicine, the law and bioethics professor R. Alta Charo explains why these calls are misguided.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'