ect', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lingmerth, David (1987- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spieth, Jordan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PGA Championship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-14T19:05:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6801f0c9-1946-5384-af64-7cc8d9c1c5a3', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6801f0c9-1946-5384-af64-7cc8d9c1c5a3'}, {'abstract': 'John Hatfield, the executive director of Socrates Sculpture Park in Queens, has made a pre-emptive strike on empty-nest syndrome: He and his wife got a puppy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/nyregion/how-john-hatfield-executive-director-of-socrates-sculpture-park-spends-his-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'John Hatfield, the executive director of Socrates Sculpture Park in Queens, has made a pre-emptive strike on empty-nest syndrome: He and his wife got a puppy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the executive director of Socrates Sculpture Park, a public art space in Long Island City, Queens, John Hatfield keeps an eye on the weather: The clearer the skies and the warmer the temperature, the busier he is. “Late spring, summer, early fall — we have so many events,” Mr. Hatfield said. The schedule often keeps him away from his family’s TriBeCa apartment, so on Sundays, Mr. Hatfield, 51, focuses on spending time at home — taking in art with his wife, Amy Wolf, 57, an art dealer; catching up with their son, Otis, 18; and caring for the family’s new puppy, Babs Kramer.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mu