on was one of the many early vibrators prescribed to women as cure-alls for ailments like the always-vague “hysteria.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 15 years, the Museum of Sex, at 233 Fifth Avenue (an address, appropriately enough, near the former site of an early-20th-century red-light district known to vice enthusiasts as the Tenderloin), has been educating, by way of titillating, age-appropriate tourists and locals alike. While those who visit for a bit of blushing will no doubt find an array of X-rated artifacts capable of getting the job done, the true lessons to be learned from the one act with which every culture is consumed are many. And, oftentimes, a little gross.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16VAULT1/16VAULT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16VAULT1/16VAULT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16VAULT1/16VAULT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16VAULT1/16VAULT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16VAULT1/16VAULT1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16VAULT1/16VAULT1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 7