ect', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mylan Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Perrigo Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paulson & Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-14T21:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74c19b39-0c26-5540-a9fd-5c93aa93962c', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74c19b39-0c26-5540-a9fd-5c93aa93962c'}, {'abstract': 'The beachy peninsula in Queens seemed headed toward a taco-less summer. But Tacoway Beach has opened on the premises of the Rockaway Beach Surf Club, attracting a drinking crowd.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/nyregion/quenching-a-thirst-for-tacos-in-the-rockaways.html', 'snippet': 'The beachy peninsula in Queens seemed headed toward a taco-less summer. But Tacoway Beach has opened on the premises of the Rockaway Beach Surf Club, attracting a drinking crowd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It looked at one point that the Rockaways, the beachy peninsula in southern Queens, home to firefighters, midlevel Wall Street guys and armies of sun-seeking Brooklyn hipsters, was headed toward a taco-less summer. Late in March, the news slipped out that Andrew Field and David Selig, the co-owners of Rockaway Taco, had parted ways over business plans and that their ramshackle joint on Beach 96th Street would not return this season. But then, Mr. Selig decided to take a food-truck version of Rockaway Taco across the country, and Mr. Field made plans to move his own new venture, Tacoway Beach, onto the premises of the Rockaway Beach Surf Club on Beach 87th Street. Showing no sign of the hostilities, Tacoway Beach was booming recently, filled with a ruddy, beer-drinking crowd that included two newlywed (or newlywed-ish) couples.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16TABLE1/16TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16TABLE1/16TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16TABLE1/16TABLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16TABLE1/16TABLE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16TABLE1/16TABLE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16TABLE1/16TABLE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/nyregion/16TABLE1/16TABLE1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Quenching a Thirst for Tacos in the Rockaways', 'kicker': 'At the Table', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quenching Their Thirst ', 'name': N