 speaks in a British accent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/15/world/europe/russian-conspiracy-theorists-accidentally-give-reporter-from-kansas-british-accent-in-internet-hoax.html', 'snippet': 'In audio posted online this week by a Russian newspaper, a man identified as an American reporter working for the C.I.A. speaks in a British accent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the immediate aftermath of the downing of Malaysia Airlines Flight 17 over rebel-held, eastern Ukraine last year, Ukraine’s intelligence agency released what it said was audio from intercepted phone calls between separatist leaders and Russian military intelligence officers, in which the militants appeared to acknowledge shooting down a civilian plane by mistake.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Internet Hoax on Downing of Malaysian Jet Spreads in Russia', 'kicker': 'Open Source', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Internet Hoax on Downing of Malaysian Jet Spreads in Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaysia Airlines Flight 17', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Komsomolskaya Pravda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-14T23:34:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ba171a2-6873-5c97-8e