age opposition — and destroys his future in the process — in David Simon’s mini-series, based on a nonfiction book by Lisa Belkin, a former reporter for The New York Times. The cast includes Alfred Molina as a machine politician, Bob Balaban as the judge, and Terry Kinney, Clarke Peters and Catherine Keener. “What Mr. Simon and his ‘Wire’ collaborator William F. Zorzi have written, and Paul Haggis (‘Crash’) has directed, is many things: meticulously and cleverly assembled, wonderfully coherent, often moving and funny, painstaking in its evocation of a midsize, tired city in the late 1980s and early ’90s,” Mike Hale wrote in The New York Times. “In its later episodes, as the first black and Latino residents move into their new homes in formerly all-white neighborhoods of east Yonkers, it has a real (if modest) emotional punch. But, ultimately, it’s a show to be admired, not loved.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-16T16:11:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/97987c46-13e5-5478-8849-d30e935564d3', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97987c46-13e5-5478-8849-d30e935564d3'}, {'abstract': 'We finally see what it looks like when Hannibal turns vengeful.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/16/hannibal-recap-season-3-and-the-beast-from-sea/', 'snippet'