 Carlos Beltran lost in the sun paving the way for Toronto’s three-run third inning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/17/sports/baseball/yankees-fall-to-blue-jays-tightening-al-east-race-again.html', 'snippet': 'The game, like the first two in the series, turned on the finest of margins, with a fly ball that Carlos Beltran lost in the sun paving the way for Toronto’s three-run third inning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — Yankees General Manager Brian Cashman walked out on a ledge near the top of CN Tower late Saturday afternoon, tethered only by a harness, which was stronger than his nerves.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17YANKEES/17YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17YANKEES/17YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17YANKEES/17YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17YANKEES/17YANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17YANKEES/17YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17YANKEES/17YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17YANKEES/17YANKEES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Fall to Blue Jays, Tightening A.L. East Race Again', 'kicker': 'Blue Jays 3, Yankees 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beltran Loses a Ball in the Sun, and the Yankees Fail to Sweep ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltran, Carlos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bautista, Jose', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-16T20:46:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f516ed87-91a4-52b7-be56-8930dae83707', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f516ed87-91a4-52b7-be56-8930dae83707'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Vogt interpreted these composers and Cristian Macelaru conducted in a concert on Friday at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/17/arts/music/review-lars-vogt-presents-late-career-beethoven-and-schubert-at-mostly-mozart.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Vogt interpreted these composers and Cristian Macelaru conducted in a concert on Friday at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The word “muscular” often came to mind while listening to the German pianist Lars Vogt perform Beethoven’s Piano Concerto No. 4 at Avery Fisher Hall on Friday evening. Mr. Vogt balanced a powerful touch that stopped just short of harsh in forte passages, particularly in the piano’s upper register, with a limpid delicacy, control and poise that proved striking in intimate sections. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Lars Vogt Presents Late-Career Beethoven and Schubert at Mostly Mozart', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pianist Balances Power and Delicacy ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mostly Mozart Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macelaru, Cristian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vogt, Lars', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-16T20:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e25b5f3-950d-5d5c-bb64-6655aa622465', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e25b5f3-950d-5d5c-bb64-6655aa622465'}, {'abstract': 'This performance, part of the Battery Dance Festival in Lower Manhattan, included five genres of Indian dance from around that country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/17/arts/dance/review-erasing-borders-festival-of-indian-dance-a-showcase-of-dizzying-movement.html', 'snippet': 'This performance, part of the Battery Dance Festival in Lower Manhattan, included five genres of Indian dance from around that country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the weeklong Battery Dance Festival — an August perennial — has settled on a stage in Robert F. Wagner Jr. Park, it has the best backdrop in New York. The audience sees, behind the dancers, the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island. Sailboats, cruise boats and yachts pass. Airplanes pass silently above. The drawback is that audience members, at 6:30 p.m., have the early-evening sun in their eyes. Baseball caps or dark sunglasses are advised. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/arts/17INDIADANCE1/17INDIADANCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/17/arts/17INDIADANCE1/17INDIADANCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/arts/17INDIADANCE1/17INDIADANCE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/arts/17INDIADANCE1/17INDIADANCE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1336, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/arts/17INDIADANCE1/17INDIADANCE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/17/arts/17INDIADANCE1/17INDIADANCE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/arts