uated rail tunnels need a long-term solution and proper funding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The antiquated rail tunnels under the Hudson River between New York and New Jersey look older than their 105 years. In places, the cement walls next to the tracks are crumbling, exposing the electrical wiring that helps power and control the system. And even though Amtrak officials work every weekend to repair the two and a half-mile long tubes, they are alarmed by the rapid deterioration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/opinion/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/17/opinion/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/opinion/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/opinion/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/opinion/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/17/opinion/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV/20150817-Tunnel-SS-slide-LHSV-thumbStandard.jpg', 't