n-program.html', 'snippet': 'Hamstrung by financial difficulties, Parma F.C. endured an embarrassing season. Now the team, playing in a lesser league, has an altered name, a smaller staff and a revised concept of ownership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARMA, Italy — The fields are covered in burnt-out patches. The crossbar of one goal hangs limply, split straight down the middle. Most of the offices inside the spacious headquarters are dark and empty.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17PARMA1/17PARMA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17PARMA1/17PARMA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17PARMA1/17PARMA1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17PARMA1/17PARMA1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17PARMA1/17PARMA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17PARMA1/17PARMA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/17/sports/17PARMA1/17PARMA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Parma’s Rebirth Rests on a Ragged Pitch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rebirth Rests on a Ragged Pitch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borden, Sam (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Parma (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Serie A (Italian Soccer League)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parma Calcio 1913 (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-17T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c1cfdcc-d557-5856-81ec-a5fa715a9519', 'word_count': 1918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c1cfdcc-d557-5856-81ec-a5fa715a9519'}, {'abstract': 'A science journalist’s reading of medical history suggests that the “autism pandemic” is an optical illusion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/books/review/neurotribes-by-steve-silberman.html', 'snippet': 'A science journalist’s reading of medical history suggests that the “autism pandemic” is an optical illusion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The history of science is studded with stories of simultaneous discovery, in which two imaginative souls (or more!) turn out to have been digging tunnels to the same unspoiled destination. The most fabled example is calculus, developed independently in two different countries by Isaac Newton and Gottfried Wilhelm von Leibniz, but the list stretches back centuries and unfurls right into the present. One can add to it sunspots, evolution, platinum, chloroform .\u2008.\u2008. and now autism, as the science journalist Steve Silberman informs us, identified separately by Leo Kanner and Hans Asperger. The crucial difference is that Kanner had the fortune to publish his work in Baltimore, while Asperger had the misfortune to publish his in Nazi-controlled Vienna, and this accident of geopolitics lies at the tragic core of Silberman’s ambitious, meticulous and largehearted (if occasionally long-winded) history, “NeuroTribes: The Legacy of Autism and the Future of \xadNeurodiversity.” ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/0823-BKS-Senior/0823-BKS-Senior-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/0823-BKS-Senior/0823-BKS-Senior-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/0823-BKS-Senior/0823-BKS-Senior-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/0823-BKS-Senior/0823-BKS-Senior-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1427, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/0823-BKS-Senior/0823-BKS-Senior-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/