aoki-2/', 'snippet': 'Can you crack Japan’s latest puzzle sensation?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s challenge is an original\xa0suggested by\xa0Naoki Inaba, and is the second in a series by this ingenuous and remarkably prolific Japanese puzzle designer. (In case you missed it, check out Predator and Prey.) This week we take on\xa0Menseki Meiro, or\xa0“Area Maze,” referring to the labyrinthine process involved in finding the target\xa0— the area of a rectangle. Area Maze\xa0is\xa0already a hit in Japan. Will it have the same addictive potential\xa0in the\xa0United States as it does in\xa0Japan? Let’s give it a try. Here’s Mr. Inaba presenting five challenges in\xa0ascending difficulty:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Naoki Inaba’s Area Maze Puzzle', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inaba, Naoki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-17T16:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8b84637-c3b3-504f-a6ea-5f03b0146218', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8b84637-c3b3-504f-a6ea-5f03b0146218'}, {'abstract': 'A traveling exhibition will feature work by Scottish winners of the Turner Prize and nominees.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/17/gearing-up-for-turner-prize-art-exhibition-will-roam-scotland/', 'snippet': 'A traveling exhibition will feature work by Scottish winners of the Turner Prize and nominees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A roving art exhibition featuring 