6db3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f7e69100-be1c-53a9-9eb4-17af7a436db3'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The United States is furious at German conspirators in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/17/1915-u-s-angered-by-german-plots/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The United States is furious at German conspirators in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON\xa0— According to the New York correspondent of the ‘‘Daily Express,’’ the revelations concerning the great German plot in the United States have caused a nation-wide sensation, and the Government is considering whether formal action can be taken against the conspirators. The New York ‘‘World’’ to-day prints a memorandum on a project to obtain possession of all the liquid chlorine in America in order to prevent its exportation to the Allies for the manufacture of asphyxiating gases. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 18, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: U.S. Angered by German Plots', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sabotage (Crime)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-17T16:58:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/139cf774-15d0-56bd-9f9f-