8/19/dining/alcoholic-root-beer-generates-a-noticeable-buzz.html', 'snippet': 'Root beer with alcohol in stores; cups made of sugar; a pantry for Amy’s Bread; a new sriracha; new flavors of ice cream; a tandoori steakhouse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hard root beer is flying off the shelves. Not Your Father’s Root Beer, an ale fermented with spices, made by Small Town Brewery in Wauconda, Ill., landed in New York and elsewhere late last month. The taste, like soda fountain root beer with less sweetness, does not hide the gentle kick from 5.9 percent alcohol. Coney Island Brewing, which opened recently, also has a hard root beer. It is 5.8 percent alcohol and a tad sweeter and fizzier than the competition. The flavor is less earthy with more vanilla and coffee in the flavor notes. Coney Island’s main backer is Boston Beer, the parent company of Sam Adams. The root beer is being made at a Boston Beer plant, not in Brooklyn. Now you can turn that root beer float into a nightcap: Not Your Father’s Root Beer, $10.99 for a six-pack at Fairway markets; Coney Island Hard Root Beer, $2.50 a bottle at Malt & Mold, maltandmold.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/19/dining/19BURNER_ROOT/19BURNER_ROOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/19/dining/19BURNER_ROOT/19BURNER_ROOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 732}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/19/dining/19BURNER_ROOT/19BURNER_ROOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 840, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/19/dining/19BURNER_ROOT/19BURNER_ROOT-superJum