-bryan-tops-dr-dre-in-album-sales/', 'snippet': 'Dr. Dre’s first album in 16 years lands at No. 2, with Luke Bryan’s “Kill the Lights” taking the top spot on Billboard’s album chart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the music charts this week, the country star Luke Bryan beat Dr. Dre for the No. 1 album, as expected, while OMI’s “Cheerleader” returns as the top single.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Luke Bryan Tops Dr. Dre in Album Sales', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Luke Bryan Tops Chart With ‘Kill the Lights’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryan, Luke (1976- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dr Dre (1965- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-17T20:27:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce54f557-eb11-5496-8ea6-a1eaf072812f', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce54f557-eb11-5496-8ea6-a1eaf072812f'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said the attack, in which the assailant used his cousin to gain access before poisoning and shooting the officers, was the third of its kind in Helmand Province in less than two weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/18/world/asia/police-officers-are-killed-at-checkpoint-in-southern-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said the attack, in which the assailant used his cousin to gain access before poisoning and shooting the officers, was the third of its kind in Helmand Province in less than two weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANDAHAR, Afghanistan — At least five Afghan police officers were poisoned and t