 Steven Kaplan was head of investment banking at Goldman before leaving to teach at Harvard. He succeeds Richard Fisher. who left in March.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/18/business/former-goldman-executive-is-chosen-to-lead-dallas-fed.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Steven Kaplan was head of investment banking at Goldman before leaving to teach at Harvard. He succeeds Richard Fisher. who left in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas on Monday chose for its new president Robert Steven Kaplan, a former Goldman Sachs executive.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/business/18KAPLAN/18KAPLAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 483, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/business/18KAPLAN/18KAPLAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 483, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/business/18KAPLAN/18KAPLAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/18/business/18KAPLAN/18KAPLAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/business/18KAPLAN/18KAPLAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Goldman Executive Is Chosen to Lead Dallas Fed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Next President for Dallas Fed Is Named', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Robert S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appelbaum, Binyamin (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Richard W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-17T23:31:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecf2c330-d361-53f2-acba-7b9cdb9a42e6', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecf2c330-d361-53f2-acba-7b9cdb9a42e6'}, {'abstract': 'The group responsible for monitoring adherence to the global ban on chemical weapons said that it had contacted Iraq over reports of the possible use of such munitions there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/18/world/middleeast/iraq-monitoring-group-to-investigate-possible-chemical-weapons-use-by-isis.html', 'snippet': 'The group responsible for monitoring adherence to the global ban on chemical weapons said that it had contacted Iraq over reports of the possible use of such munitions there.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The group responsible for monitoring adherence to the global ban on chemical weapons said Monday that it had contacted Iraq over reports of the possible use of such munitions there. A statement by the group, the Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons, based in The Hague, came a few days after United States officials said Islamic State militants appeared to have used such munitions, possibly mustard gas, on Kurdish fighters in Iraq. If confirmed, it would be the first known use of the weapons by the Islamic State, which occupies parts of Syria and Iraq. The monitoring group called such reports “a matter of serious concern,” and its director, Ahmet Uzumcu, said it would “examine any substantive reports it receives including pertinent information that might be shared” by other signers of the chemical weapons ban, which appeared to be a reference to both Iraq and Syria. Iraq, where hundreds of old, corroded mustard artillery shells remained after the 2003 American invasion, signed the chemical weapons ban in 2009. Syria joined in 2013 after having promised to destroy its chemical stockpile, although the monitoring organization said this year that chlorine bombs had been used in the Syrian conflict. On Aug. 7, the United Nations Security Council passed a resolution authorizing an inquiry into who was responsible for the chlorine attacks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Monitoring Group to Investigate Possible Chemical Weapons Use by ISIS', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Iraq: Monitoring Group Will Investigate Possible Chemical Weapons Use by ISIS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-17T23:39:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfd5e65d-3c72-527d-b7ce-2a18983ef0aa', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfd5e65d-3c72-527d-b7ce-2a18983ef0aa'}, {'abstract': 'Bryan Mitchell was hit in the face with a line drive off the bat of Eduardo Nunez, who, in an odd twist, handed the Yankees a victory when he mishandled a bases-loaded grounder in the 10th.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/18/sports/baseball/yankees-pitcher-bryan-mitchell-hit-in-head-by-line-drive.html', 'snippet': 'Bryan Mitchell was hit in the face with a line drive off the bat of Eduardo Nunez, who, in an odd twist, handed the Yankees a victory when he mishandled a bases-loaded grounder in the 10th.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a frightening scene at Yankee Stadium on Monday night, Yankees starter Bryan Mitchell was hit in the face with a line drive off the bat of Eduardo Nunez, a right-handed hitter for the Minnesota Twins, in the second inning of an 8-7, 10-inning Yankees victory. In 2013, when Nunez was an infielder with the Yankees and on a rehab assignment with Class A Tampa, he and Mitchell were teammates for three games.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/sports/SUB-Y-YANKEES/SUB-Y-YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xl