major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-18T00:17:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Berkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1835cec-cfa9-593c-b8c0-e548c3963675', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1835cec-cfa9-593c-b8c0-e548c3963675'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration issued a final permit for Shell to start drilling for oil and gas in the Chukchi Sea off Alaska’s northwest coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/18/us/shell-wins-final-permission-for-arctic-oil-and-gas-drilling.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration issued a final permit for Shell to start drilling for oil and gas in the Chukchi Sea off Alaska’s northwest coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration on Monday issued a final permit for Shell to start drilling for oil and gas in the Arctic Ocean. The Interior Department gave conditional approval in May for the company’s long-delayed application to drill in the untouched waters of the Chukchi Sea off Alaska’s northwest coast. In July, the administration issued a permit that would allow Shell to start drilling at the top of the seabed but would not allow the drill to penetrate into the oil reserves until Shell had quick access to a “capping stack,” which is used to shut down wells in case of emergency spills. The ship carrying that capping stack arrived at the drilling site last week. Environmentalists have criticized Mr. Obama for moving forward with the drilling. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shell Wins Final Permission for Arctic Oil and Gas Drilling', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shell Wins Final Permission for Arctic Oil and Gas Drilling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Dutch Shell Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chukchi Sea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-18T00:25:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Coral Davenport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Coral', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davenport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5cd2e37-946b-5265-8bb4-a5ae96b21c8a', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5cd2e37-946b-5265-8bb4-a5ae96b21c8a'}, {'abstract': 'Only a relative handful of African-American lawyers persevere on the years-long path to joining a law firm’s lucrative leadership circle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/18/business/dealbook/many-black-lawyers-navigate-a-rocky-lonely-road-to-partner.html', 'snippet': 'Only a relative handful of African-American lawyers persevere on the years-long path to joining a law firm’s lucrative leadership circle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jimmie L. McMillian’s path to partnership in an Indianapolis law firm might seem unexceptional — except for a few telling details.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/business/13db-law-web/13db-law-web-articleLarge.