Ruth Madoff and Blanche DuBois, this shattered woman is “brilliantly brought to quivering life by Ms. Blanchett,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times, in Woody Allen’s “most sustained, satisfying and resonant film since ‘Match Point.’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-18T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/3022ecb2-0af4-59c4-b471-9c6f0fb95c3d', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3022ecb2-0af4-59c4-b471-9c6f0fb95c3d'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, August 18, 2015', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/18/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, August 18, 2015', 'lead_paragraph': '“Fifty-three. Where are all these girls?”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, August 18, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-18T05:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/71f404f8-2e66-53f1-acd