e test.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/19/arts/music/taking-the-starch-out-of-orchestra-attire.html', 'snippet': 'Some of the musicians who lament being all buttoned up, physically active and boiling under hot lights are putting new, flexible tuxedo shirts to the test.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mountaineers no longer wear the scratchy tweeds favored by their 19th-century forebears. Modern swimwear bears little resemblance to the flesh-covering woolen bathing costumes of summers long past. But orchestra musicians still tend to saw away at Beethoven and Mahler in hot, constricting formal attire that would be instantly recognizable to audiences of a century ago.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/arts/18PERFORMALWEB1/18PERFORMALWEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/18/arts/18PERFORMALWEB1/18PERFORMALWEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/arts/18PERFORMALWEB1/18PERFORMALWEB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/arts/18PERFORMALWEB1/18PERFORMALWEB1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/arts/18PERFORMALWEB1/18PERFORMALWEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/18/arts/18PERFORMALWEB1/18PERFORMALWEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/18/arts/18PERFORMALWEB1/18PERFORMALWEB1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Starch Out of Orchestra Attire    ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking the Starch, and Steam, Out of Orchestra Wear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yu, Kevin K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coregami Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-18T09:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a88e772-ef82-5be1-87d0-07a4c0b1e101', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a88e772-ef82-5be1-87d0-07a4c0b1e101'}, {'abstract': 'A fight is playing out in national forests from North Carolina to the Pacific Northwest between backpackers seeking solitude and gun owners out for target shooting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/19/us/a-culture-clash-over-guns-infiltrates-the-backcountry.html', 'snippet': 'A fight is playing out in national forests from North Carolina to the Pacific Northwest between backpackers seeking solitude and gun owners out for target shooting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SARATOGA SPRINGS, Utah — As a lover of ancient rock art, Steve Acerson usually roams Utah’s backcountry searching for images of hunters and rams carved on boulders and canyon walls. But one morning, on a hillside speckled with those prehistoric petroglyphs, he was also finding signs of a younger civilization: Shotgun shells. Bullets. Shredded juniper trees. Exploded cans of spray paint.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/us/14GUNSWEB1/14GUNSWEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/13/us/14GUNSWEB1/14GUNSWEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/us/14GUNSWEB1/14GUNSWEB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/us/14GUNSWEB1/14GUNSWEB1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/us/14GUNSWEB1/14GUNSWEB1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/13/us/14GUNSWEB1/14GUNSWEB1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/13/us/14GUNSWEB1/14GUNSWEB1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Quiet Woods, a Clamorous Gun Debate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Quiet Woods, a Clamorous Gun Debate ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Healy, Jack (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Lands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hikes and Hiking', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Land Management', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-18T09:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1dfa36a-c79c-5109-8f26-561811ac2756', 'word_count': 1295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1dfa36a-c79c-5109-8f26-561811ac2756'}, {'abstract': 'The “Blurred Lines” video star likes a Korean spa that doesn’t coddle her, and she doesn’t like facials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/fashion/emily-ratajkowski-on-her-beauty-regiment-and-why-she-doesnt-use-a-trainer.html', 'snippet': 'The “Blurred Lines” video star likes a Korean spa that doesn’t coddle her, and she doesn’t like facials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Emily Ratajkowski, 24, shot to fame as the playful and scandalously bare brunette in Robin Thicke’s “Blurred Lines” music video, but she has been earning her marks on the silver screen ever since. After supporting roles in “Gone Girl” and this summer’s “Entourage,” Ms. Ratajko