 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03d719de-2f00-50b5-ba8e-3e10ed1c39a8', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03d719de-2f00-50b5-ba8e-3e10ed1c39a8'}, {'abstract': 'Nevada, with its mix of rural and urban areas, a diverse population and lingering economic problems, is viewed as a good early-state indicator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/19/us/politics/hillary-clinton-turns-to-nevada-as-a-general-election-litmus-test.html', 'snippet': 'Nevada, with its mix of rural and urban areas, a diverse population and lingering economic problems, is viewed as a good early-state indicator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — On Tuesday, Hillary Rodham Clinton declared this city — with its flashy strip of casinos, rows of middle-class subdivisions and one of the highest unemployment rates in the nation — the perfect place to pitch her campaign message.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hillary Clinton Turns to Nevada as a General Election Litmus Test', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clinton Turns to a Rapidly Diversifying Nevada as a General Election Litmus Test', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chozick, Amy (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T00:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3690f54a-a349-59f4-b307-aac53a8ed583', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3690f54a-a349-59f4-b307-aac53a8ed583'}, {'abstract': 'A judge ordered an Albuquerque police officer and a retired detective to stand trial for the 2014 killing of a homeless man who they had accused of illegally camping.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/19/us/new-mexico-officers-to-be-tried-for-mans-killing.html', 'snippet': 'A judge ordered an Albuquerque police officer and a retired detective to stand trial for the 2014 killing of a homeless man who they had accused of illegally camping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge\xa0on Tuesday\xa0ordered an Albuquerque police officer and a retired detective to stand trial for the killing of a homeless man, James Boyd, last year during a long confrontation that started when the police accused Mr. Boyd of illegally camping on the foothills of the Sandia Mountains. The officer, Dominique Perez, and the retired detective, Keith Sandy, will face second-degree murder and manslaughter charges. A video of the shooting, captured by an officer’s lapel camera, set off protests in Albuquerque over the use of force by city police officers, who had fired at civilians at least 37 times in four years. These and other use-of-force incidents were the basis of a scathing report by the Justice Department, which entered into an agreement with the city last October to improve officers’ training, among other changes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Mexico: Officers to Be Tried for 