'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23onphotography1/23mag-23onphotography-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23onphotography1/23mag-23onphotography-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23onphotography1/23mag-23onphotography-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23onphotography1/23mag-23onphotography-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1335, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23onphotography1/23onphotography1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23onphotography1/23onphotography1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23onphotography1/23onphotography1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shadows in São Paulo', 'kicker': 'On Photography', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shadows in São Paulo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burri, Rene (1933-2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magnum Photos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teju Cole', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teju', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cole', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23833e4a-3ca5-534d-880b-5fa0927410ca', 'word_count': 1634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23833e4a-3ca5-534d-880b-5fa0927410ca'}, {'abstract': 'Its restrictions will be reviewed by the Supreme Court and are being copied by other states.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/upshot/how-texas-could-set-national-template-for-limiting-abortion-access.html', 'snippet': 'Its restrictions will be reviewed by the Supreme Court and are being copied by other states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Efforts to defund Planned Parenthood and calls for tighter abortion laws at the Republican presidential debate have moved abortion rights back into the national spotlight. But the real fight is at the state level. The next big Supreme Court case involving abortion is expected to come from Texas [Update: The Supreme Court is hearing the case], where a 2013 law led to the closing of many clinics and inspired abortion opponents around the country to propose similar restrictions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Texas Could Set National Template for Limiting Abortion Access', 'kicker': 'Debate That Divides', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas Could Be a Template for Reducing Abortion Access', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soffen, Kim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Soffen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soffen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66fb3738-a53c-5853-ad47-eb43d1b330c8', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66fb3738-a53c-5853-ad47-eb43d1b330c8'}, {'abstract': 'The ethicists consider how an employee should respond after learning that colleagues praised an anti-Semitic text.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/magazine/handling-a-racist-remark-in-the-workplace.html', 'snippet': 'The ethicists consider how an employee should respond after learning that colleagues praised an anti-Semitic text.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I represent a real-estate developer in Florida. Recently an employee of one of the developer’s commercial tenants confided to me that he overheard an administrator at his company tell another employee that she had just read a book called ‘‘The Protocols of the Elders of Zion’’ and thought it contained excellent points. The person with whom she was speaking, a department manager, responded that it was a great book and that it must be legitimate because it was endorsed by Henry Ford. I’m uncomfortable that this type of conversation might reflect a negative aspect of our tenant’s company culture. I’m tempted to raise this with the general counsel of the company, with whom I negotiated the lease — but for what purpose? I can’t betray the confidence, so what am I trying to accomplish? I can’t get over that employees working in a respected chain could really accept any premise in that anti-Semitic rant. I thought the reach of the book was limited to uneducated neo-Nazis, but these are educated people in positions of authority. Something just feels wrong here, and I would appreciate some guidance on where to go with this. NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23ethicists/23mag-23ethicists_two-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 562, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23ethicists/23mag-23ethicists_two-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 562}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23ethicists/23mag-23ethicists_two-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 959, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23ethicists/23mag-23ethicists_two-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1438, 'width': 1535, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23ethicists/23mag-23ethicists_two-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/23/magazine/23ethicists/23mag-23ethicists_two-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 7