nts crave it. And everything is against the law in the 1960s. But who wants to make arrests for crimes that aren’t really hurting anyone? Not Terry Muldoon, an officer with the New York Police Department’s public morals division. “So, then, what exactly do we do here?” asks Jimmy Shea, the handsome newcomer. “We do what has been done for the last hundred years: We manage it for the city,” Muldoon says. “Think of us as the landlords, and if you want to be in business, you got to pay your rent. Do you understand what I am telling you?” Shea does. “Now I’m only going to ask you this this one time,” Muldoon says. “Are you in?”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23GUIDE6/23GUIDE6-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23GUIDE6/23GUIDE6-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23GUIDE6/23GUIDE6-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23GUIDE6/23GUIDE6-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23GUIDE6/23GUIDE6-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23GUIDE6/23GUIDE6-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23GUIDE6/23GUIDE6-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In TNT’s ‘Public Morals,’ Ed Burns Is on the Vice Beat in ’60s New York', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Vice Beat in a Gritty City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Public Morals (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T15:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e4f6404-03df-56ec-b11c-c5e9b14520cb', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e4f6404-03df-56ec-b11c-c5e9b14520cb'}, {'abstract': 'Target bucked industry trends and beat Wall Street estimates after cutting jobs and closing stores.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/business/target-retail-earnings.html', 'snippet': 'Target bucked industry trends and beat Wall Street estimates after cutting jobs and closing stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a season dotted with notable earnings misses among retailers, Target bucked the industry trends by reporting strong earnings on Wednesday, its bottom line lifted by brisk sales of apparel and home goods as well as intensive cost-cutting.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/business/20target-web/20target-web-articleLarge.jpg'