bd-5398-bb86-31ba06f4281b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Obama will use the 10th anniversary of the disaster to tout his administration’s efforts to restore the economy and infrastructure of the region, according to the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/us/president-obama-hurricane-katrina-new-orleans.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Obama will use the 10th anniversary of the disaster to tout his administration’s efforts to restore the economy and infrastructure of the region, according to the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama will travel to New Orleans next week for the 10th anniversary of Hurricane Katrina, one of the costliest disasters in United States history.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/us/20OBAMAWEB/20OBAMAWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/20/us/20OBAMAWEB/20OBAMAWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/us/20OBAMAWEB/20OBAMAWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/us/20OBAMAWEB/20OBAMAWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/us/20OBAMAWEB/20OBAMAWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/20/us/20OBAMAWEB/20OBAMAWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/us/20OBAMAWEB/20OBAMAWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to Visit New Orleans for\xa0Hurricane Katrina Anniversary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama to Visit New Orleans for Storm Milestone ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Katrina (2005)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T15:40:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6185270b-6f2b-5df2-980e-182074c2a27f', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6185270b-6f2b-5df2-980e-182074c2a27f'}, {'abstract': 'An art critic remembers “Harlem on My Mind,” a 1969 show at the Metropolitan Museum of Art widely viewed within black cultural circles as an insult.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/arts/design/what-i-learned-from-a-disgraced-art-show-on-harlem.html', 'snippet': 'An art critic remembers “Harlem on My Mind,” a 1969 show at the Metropolitan Museum of Art widely viewed within black cultural circles as an insult.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some first-time art encounters are life-changers, and you know it instantly. They zap you, cast a spell, send you back out with your eyes and mind rewired. Other encounters are just as deep, but don’t seem to be, because you’re not ready for them. You don’t know what you’re looking at, though some day you will, and you’ll wish you could be back there again, equipped with all you’ve learned. “Harlem on My Mind” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art was that kind of show for me.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/design/20summer-cotter-illo/20summer-cotter-illo-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/design/20summer-cotter-illo/20summer-cotter-illo-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/design/20summer-cotter-illo/20summer-cotter-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/design/20summer-cotter-illo/20summer-cotter-illo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/design/20summer-cotter-illo/20summer-cotter-illo-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/design/20summer-cotter-illo/20summer-cotter-illo-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/design/20summer-cotter-illo/20summer-cotter-illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What I Learned From a Disgraced Art Show on Harlem', 'kicker': 'Virgin Eyes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lessons Learned From a Disgraced Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T15:43:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b719420b-a636-5d64-80c3-e5d35645f838', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b719420b-a636-5d64-80c3-e5d35645f838'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Japan’s prime minister is met with leftist protesters during a visit to Okinawa in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/19/1965-okinawa-visit-prompts-riot/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Japan’s prime minister is met with leftist protesters during a visit to Okinawa in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAHA, Okinawa — Nightlong leftist demonstrations tore this Pacific Island capital today and forced visiting Japanese Prime Minister Eisaku Sato to take refuge in a U.S. military camp. Mr. Sato came to emphasize Japanese ties with the Ryukyu Islands. Two thousand rioters fought with sticks and bottles against club-wielding, steel-helmeted police. Police said 17 demonstrators, mostly students and unionists, were hurt. The leftist mobs oppose Mr. Sato’s support of U.S. Vietnam policy, and his lukewarm position on reversion of Okinawa and the Ryukyu islands to Japan.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, August 20, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/19/blogs/19iht-old20-1965/19iht-old20-1965-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/19/blogs/19iht-old20-1965/19iht-old20-1965-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/19/blogs/19iht-old20-1965/19iht-old20-1965-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/19/blogs/19iht-old20-1965/19iht-old20-1965-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 809, 'width': 1137, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/19/blogs/19iht-old20-1965/19iht-old20-1965-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/19/blogs/19iht-old20-1965/19iht-old20-1965-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': No