s like “Sinister 2” and dramedies like “Me and Earl and the Dying Girl,” films-within-films are coming into their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Somewhere in an alternate universe, a multiplex is playing a curious slate of motion pictures: “The Dogwalker,” “Habeas Corpus,” “Mant!” and “Camp Bloodbath.” If you don’t recognize any of these titles, there’s a good reason: All of them are imaginary films that pop up in actual movies. We catch a glimpse of these fake flicks when characters watch them in “Trainwreck,” “The Player,” “Matinee” and “The Final Girls.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23MINI-FILM1/23MINI-FILM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 269, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23MINI-FILM1/23MINI-FILM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 269}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23MINI-FILM1/23MINI-FILM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23MINI-FILM1/23MINI-FILM1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1473, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23MINI-FILM1/23MINI-FILM1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23MINI-FILM1/23MINI-FILM1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url