on & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/2e534cc4-25f5-5913-a87f-171480c4bdcd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/2e534cc4-25f5-5913-a87f-171480c4bdcd'}, {'abstract': 'Keith McNally says his crowd-pleasing brasserie-style restaurant will have a new “look, menu and style of food.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/19/dining/pastis-plans-to-open-in-gansevoort-market-in-2017.html', 'snippet': 'Keith McNally says his crowd-pleasing brasserie-style restaurant will have a new “look, menu and style of food.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Keith McNally’s crowd-pleasing brasserie-style restaurant Pastis, which anchored the meatpacking district from 1999 and closed last year because of building construction, has found a new home in the Gansevoort Market, a collection of stands selling foods that opened about a year ago at 52 Gansevoort Street, near the new Whitney Museum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/dining/19pastis/19pastis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/20/dining/19pastis/19pastis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/dining/19pastis/19pastis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/dining/19pastis/19pastis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'super