sons', 'value': 'Murphy, Kathleen A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barker, Sara Elizabeth (d 2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T18:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c73de7-0d86-5614-a388-c96f95bfda88', 'word_count': 1160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c73de7-0d86-5614-a388-c96f95bfda88'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s largest city is a great place to walk — or bike or hike or sail. And then sample the locovore fare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/travel/what-to-do-in-36-hours-in-burlington-vermont.html', 'snippet': 'The state’s largest city is a great place to walk — or bike or hike or sail. And then sample the locovore fare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Burlington, home of the University of Vermont and the birthplace of Phish, Ben and Jerry’s and Seventh Generation, has long embodied the earthy progressivism and can-do independence that define the state’s spirit. Lately that ethos has taken on a sophisticated sheen, as chefs apply Vermont’s longtime obsession with local ingredients in exciting new directions. There are still plenty of Birkenstocks about; they’re just parked under tables spread with confit duck poutine, braised leek crepes and crisp, complex Vermont craft brews like Alchemist’s Heady Topper, a beer of near-mythic reputation among hops aficionados.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Burlington, Vermont', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours in Burlington, Vt.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Burlington (Vt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vermont', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T18:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a50931b3-68d3-5bf1-b66a-1f073882d230', 'word_count': 1572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a50931b3-68d3-5bf1-b66a-1f073882d230'}, {'abstract': 'The second day of testimony in the trial of Owen Labrie, who has pleaded not guilty, brought out both excruciating detail and intense emotion from the girl said to have been sexually assaulted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/us/in-st-pauls-rape-trial-girl-vividly-recounts-night-of-school-ritual.html', 'snippet': 'The second day of testimony in the trial of Owen Labrie, who has pleaded not guilty, brought out both excruciating detail and intense emotion from the girl said to have been sexually assaulted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CONCORD, N.H. — The 16-year-old girl sat on the witness stand, her hair pulled back. She tried to speak steadily as she told a jury about the night when a ritual at St. Paul’s — an elite boarding school here — turned into what she described as a shocking sexual assault.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/us/20STPAULSWEB/20STPAULSWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/