one, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jindal, Bobby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T19:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE ASSOCIATED PRESS', 'person': [], 'organization': 'THE ASSOCIATED PRESS'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/35b24a4e-d92a-5bac-82a8-b81a665157ae', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/35b24a4e-d92a-5bac-82a8-b81a665157ae'}, {'abstract': 'Earnings have disappointed as copper and coal have tumbled. And looking forward, both rivals’ behavior and Chinese demand remain unpredictable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/business/dealbook/glencore-tripped-up-by-faith-in-rational-markets.html', 'snippet': 'Earnings have disappointed as copper and coal have tumbled. And looking forward, both rivals’ behavior and Chinese demand remain unpredictable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Glencore’s shtick has long been that it is the master of the commodity markets. It knows when to take risks, it can shift supply to where it’s most wanted and it tweaks its own mines to maximise profit. Or at least it can do all that when everyone else behaves rationally. That thinking has come unstuck, and the British-Swiss commodities trader’s earnings have gone with it. They halved in the first six months of 2015.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glencore Tripped Up by Faith in Rational Markets', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glencore International AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xstrata', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T19:47:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Foley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Foley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/024b1163-2bd2-5c58-bbef-7f9fb50cf659', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/024b1163-2bd2-5c58-bbef-7f9fb50cf659'}, {'abstract': 'Why the Donald’s rise need not spell doom for Republican policy reform.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/19/how-trump-might-help-reform-conservatism/', 'snippet': 'Why the Donald’s rise need not spell doom for Republican policy reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We haven’t been talking very much about intra-conservative policy debates since the G.O.P. primary campaign, and especially the Trump boom, began in earnest. Over at Bloomberg Politics, Peter Gosselin has a piece up quoting some members of my own “reform conservative” tribe expressing dismay at this, and particularly at the way that Trump is killing off\xa0serious policy arguments and turning\xa0the G.O.P. primary into an exercise in substance-free showmanship. “To one degree or another,” Gosselin writes, “virtually everyone in [the reformocon] circle of mostly 30-something conservatives interviewed in recent days expressed apprehension that the Republican contest could degenerate into the negative, policy-light brawl of four years ago, something party officials and policy advocates had sought to avoid.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Trump Might Help Reform Conservatives', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jindal, Bobby', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-19T19:58:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00408f8e-d509-5336-8f35-c7ad2b167e49', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00408f8e-d509-5336-8f35-c7ad2b167e49'}, {'abstract': 'Sotheby’s is selling fine art and memorabilia from the collection of one of the most important creative forces behind the Simpsons, Sam Simon, who died in March.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/19/sothebys-to-auction-simpsons-memorabilia-from-sam-simon-collection/', 'snippet': 'Sotheby’s is selling fine art and memorabilia from the collection of one of the most important creative forces behind the Simpsons, Sam Simon, who died in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This fall ardent fans of “The Simpsons” can buy a Simpsons pinball machine at Sotheby’s. (Bart’s voice will berate you, “Hey, man, I’m an underachiever, too.” Homer’s taunts: “Don’t you know how to use the flippers?”)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/simpsons1/simpsons1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/simpsons1/simpsons1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 802}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/simpsons1/simpsons1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/simpsons1/simpsons1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2004, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/simpsons1/simpsons1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/simpsons1/simpsons1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/simpsons1/simpsons1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge',