ed, this blistering production from the New Group, which opened on Wednesday night at the Pershing Square Signature Center, doesn’t have the big-screen special effects associated with cinematic gore fests about the end of the world. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/20MERCURY/20MERCURY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/20MERCURY/20MERCURY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/20MERCURY/20MERCURY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/20MERCURY/20MERCURY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/20MERCURY/20MERCURY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/20MERCURY/20MERCURY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/arts/20MERCURY/20MERCURY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In Philip Ridley’s ‘Mercury Fur,’ It’s the World’s End, and the Party’s Here', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s the End of the World, and the Party’s All Here', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ridley, Philip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Group Theater Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elliott, Scott', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pershing Square Signature Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mercury Fur (Play)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-20T02:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5643b450-888f-5691-839c-db1405d9e672', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5643b450-888f-5691-839c-db1405d9e672'}, {'abstract': 'Getting pumped up with Jules Markey.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/19/gas-station-supply/', 'snippet': 'Getting pumped up with Jules Markey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY PUZZLE — This may sound odd, but I have nostalgic feelings for the COMPRESSED AIR machines at gas stations. For most, reinflating one’s tires is a mundane chore, but for me, it’s a symbol of personal growth. Stay with me on this one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gas Station Supply', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-20T02:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname