_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/42c7d20c-c11e-5538-8cf1-8b9dd5481503', 'word_count': 1053, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42c7d20c-c11e-5538-8cf1-8b9dd5481503'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 15 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/word-of-the-day-carping/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 15 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'carping • \\ˈkär-piN\\ • noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day + Quiz | carping', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-20T04:02:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4295f3f4-cea3-5c7a-89e7-facab91fdb9b', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4295f3f4-cea3-5c7a-89e7-facab91fdb9b'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:50 A.M. (Starz) MR. TURNER (2014) A growling, sputtering Timothy Spall, above, stars as J. M. W. Turner (1775-1851), the man the Victorian critic John Ruskin called “the greatest painter of all time.” Mike Leigh’s biographical masterpiece juxtaposes the vexing genius of Turner’s later years and his ramshackle personal life. Turner the painter divined luminously stormy seascapes and placid river scenes that inspired the praise of critics and the envy of colleagues — until his work fell out of fashion. Turner the man lived with his father (Paul Jesson), copulated with his longtime housekeeper (Dorothy Atkinson) and ignored his daughters by his semi-estranged wife (Ruth Sheen) while keeping company with a kindhearted widow (Marion Bailey) whose last name he adopts. “\xa0‘Mr. Turner’ is a mighty work of critical imagination, a loving, unsentimental portrait of a rare creative soul,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times of this Oscar nominee in cinematography, costume and production design, and original score. “But even as it celebrates a glorious painter and illuminates the sources of his pictures with startling clarity and insight, the movie patiently and thoroughly demolishes more than a century’s worth of mythology about what art is and how artists work.” He added, “It might be risking Ruskinesque folly to take ‘Mr. Turner’ as a self-portrait of its director, but Turner shares with Mr. Leigh an ability to travel the circuit between the sublime and the ordinary, to bring into view aspects of reality that had been somehow invisible in plain sight.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-20T04:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/aea9db34-de5f-532b-a155-863e07f2018b', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aea9db34-de5f-532b-a155-863e07f2018b'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Thursday, August 20, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/pageoneplus/c