ern civilization’s very own car wreck.” Roger Simon, writing for Politico, described it as Donald Trump mooning America while the “Republican clown car” careens around the country with no driver. And in The New York Times, Ross Douthat hoped the “antics” would produce more than just “crazy cable-news entertainment.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/upshot/21UP-Vavrick/21UP-Vavrick-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 481, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/21/upshot/21UP-Vavrick/21UP-Vavrick-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 481}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/upshot/21UP-Vavrick/21UP-Vavrick-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/upshot/21UP-Vavrick/21UP-Vavrick-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1640, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/upshot/21UP-Vavrick/21UP-Vavrick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/21/upshot/21UP-Vavrick/21UP-Vavrick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/upshot/21UP-Vavrick/21UP-Vavrick-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rise and Fall of Shooting-Star Candidates', 'kicker': 'Road to 2016', 'content_kic