-at-island-splendors.html', 'snippet': 'This show, opening soon at the de Young Museum in San Francisco, explores the iridescent wonders of feathered objects from centuries past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since at least the 15th century, collectors have competed for feathers sewn and glued onto fabrics, jewelry, fans and statues. New books and exhibitions have reunited widely scattered feathered objects made in Latin America and the Pacific islands, and growing archival evidence shows that the birds used for raw materials were treated relatively well — that is, plucked sustainably.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21ANTIQUES01/21ANTIQUES01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 262, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21ANTIQUES01/21ANTIQUES01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 262}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21ANTIQUES01/21ANTIQUES01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21ANTIQUES01/21ANTIQUES01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21ANTIQUES01/21ANTIQUES01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21ANTIQUES01/21ANTIQUES01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty