owing in breadth, depth and appeal, with Grace Jones, Lenny Kravitz, Raury, Danny Brown and Death Grips among the performers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eleven years in, Afropunk Fest, Brooklyn’s weekend-long blowout celebration of the diaspora of black music and culture, is more wide-ranging than ever. It’s now possible to imagine the skate kids and fashion bloggers who populate the scene coming with their parents to catch headliners including Grace Jones, Lenny Kravitz and Gary Clark Jr. Up-and-coming acts like Raury, rap stars (Danny Brown) and punkers (Death Grips) are also on the bill for the festival, with doors opening Saturday at noon at Commodore Barry Park in Fort Greene; expect food trucks, on-site mural painting, interactive art and a dance-friendly D.J. stage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AFROPUNK01/21AFROPUNK01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AFROPUNK01/21AFROPUNK01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AFROPUNK01/21AFROPUNK01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AFROPUNK01/21AFROPUNK01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AFROPUNK01/21AFROPUNK01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AFROPUNK01/21AFROPUNK01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AFROPUNK01/21AFROPUNK01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Afropunk Festival Brings Music, Dancing and Haute Street Fashion to Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hot and the Haute in Music and Fashion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-20T21:28:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10915bca-2c76-5627-b9da-797843609db8', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10915bca-2c76-5627-b9da-797843609db8'}, {'abstract': 'Touring after his first album was released this year, Kamasi Washington has recently taken part in musical projects beyond jazz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/arts/music/review-kamasi-washington-and-the-west-coast-get-down-are-blowing-through-town.html', 'snippet': 'Touring after his first album was released this year, Kamasi Washington has recently taken part in musical projects beyond jazz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WOODSTOCK, N.Y. — Kamasi Washington blew his tenor saxophone in heavy gusts — rangy and intemperate, or clipped and urgent — throughout the exultant sprawl of his concert at the Bearsville Theater here on Wednesday night. His sound assumed an almost tactile force in the room, an extension of his burly and stoic presence onstage. And yet that sound wasn’t the most impressive facet of the performance, which ran a little over two hours, with an intuitive, almost constant ebb and flow. What really drove the agenda was the smart, hurtling fury of Mr. Washington’s band, the West Coast Get Down, a Los Angeles demolition crew partway through its first tour. Among the remaining dates are two at the Blue Note in New York City, on Monday and Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21KAMASI/21KAMASI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21KAMASI/21KAMASI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21KAMASI/21KAMASI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21KAMASI/21KAMASI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21KAMASI/21KAMASI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21KAMASI/21KAMASI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21KAMASI/21KAMASI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Kamasi Washington and the West Coast Get Down Are Blowing Through Town', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blowing Through Town With Force and Fury', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Kamasi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'West Coast Get Down (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-20T21:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/099010da-4e23-5659-a671-53d72e5d0d80', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/099010da-4e23-5659-a671-53d72e5d0d80'}, {'abstract': 'Kristen Stewart and Mr. Eisenberg pair up again in this film, an action adventure with C.I.A. trouble and occasional laughs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/movies/review-in-american-ultra-jesse-eisenberg-is-a-stoner-and-a-target.html', 'snippet': 'Kristen Stewart and Mr. Eisenberg pair up again in this film, an action adventure with C.I.A. trouble and occasional laughs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of the many, many promotional spots for “American Ultra” make it seem like more of a comedy than it is. That’s not said as a criticism, just a warning. If you go, expect a diverting summer action adventure with occasional laughs, not a diverting stoner comedy with occasional action.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AMULTRA/21AMULTRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AMULTRA/21AMULTRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AMULTRA/21AMULTRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AMULTRA/21AMULTRA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1290, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AMULTRA/21AMULTRA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AMULTRA/21AMULTRA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/21AMULTRA/21AMULTRA-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘American Ultra,’ Jesse Eisenberg Is a Stoner and a Target', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Review: In ‘American Ultra,’ Jesse Eisenberg Is a Stoner and a Target', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nourizadeh, Nima', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenberg, Jesse', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Kristen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'American Ultra (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-20T21:33:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/40c1569d-abb5-5289-a1a2-8e9d96eef330', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40c1569d-abb5-5289-a1a2-8e9d96eef330'}, {'abstract': '“On Our Hands,” at Jacob Lewis Gallery, examines familiar themes, but with a considerably more complex process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/20/t-magazine/shepard-fairey-on-our-hands-jacob-lewis.html', 'snippet': '“On Our Hands,” at Jacob Lewis Gallery, examines familiar themes, but with a considerably more complex process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sept. 18, the street artist Shepard Fairey will open his first solo show in New York since 2010’s “Mayday” — the suitably colossal closing exhibition at the now-defunct Deitch Projects. Fairey’s latest offering, a series of new mixed-media paintings titled “On Our Hands,” will serve as his inaugural exhibition at Jacob Lewis Gallery, effectively consummating a 10-year friendship between the artist and Mr. Lewis, the gallery’s owner and the first director of the influential Pace Prints in Chelsea. “Jacob looks at every aspect of what the artist is doing, not just the genre, the price or how in fashion you are,” notes Fairey from his studio in Los Angeles, where he continues to finalize the collection. “If you look at the other artists he’s worked with, whether it’s Ryan McGinness or How and Nosm, they’re the only people doing what they do.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In His First New York Show in Five Years, Shepard Fairey Is Still Questioning Everything', 'kicker': 'Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fairey Returns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fairey, Shepard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-20T21:34:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kurt McVey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kurt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McVey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cebf1c5-ddf6-5ede-8d8b-1eba126f34c7', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cebf1c5-ddf6-5ede-8d8b-1eba126f34c7'}, {'abstract': 'The Times critic Neil Genzlinger reviews “American Ultra.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000003865775/movie-review-american-ultra.html', 'snippet': 'The Times critic Neil Genzlinger reviews “American Ultra.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times critic Neil Genzlinger reviews “American Ultra.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/20/multimedia/movies-ameu-08212015/movies-ameu-08212015-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/20/multimedia/movies-ameu-08212015/movies-ameu-08212