fbdbfd8312'}, {'abstract': 'The F.D.A. called for drug makers to conduct a clinical trial of testosterone products marketed to older men to combat diminished levels of the hormone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/us/trial-of-testosterone-supplements-sought.html', 'snippet': 'The F.D.A. called for drug makers to conduct a clinical trial of testosterone products marketed to older men to combat diminished levels of the hormone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration called on Thursday for drug makers to conduct a clinical trial of testosterone products marketed to older men to combat diminished levels of the hormone. While marketers call the often-normal decrease “low T”; the F.D.A. calls it “age-related hypogonadism” and describes it as controversial. In a commentary in The New England Journal of Medicine, agency officials cited concerns over cardiovascular risks of testosterone treatment and suggested that the benefits claimed in ads are unsupported by substantial evidence. The supplements are approved by the F.D.A. for treating classic hypogonadism, which includes well-recognized medical conditions like testicular damage. But most men prescribed testosterone do not appear to have this condition, agency officials wrote, calling the trend troubling. To date, no randomized, controlled trials have been designed to evaluate cardiovascular outcomes in men taking supplemental testosterone. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trial of Testosterone Supplements Sought', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trial of Testosterone Supplements Sought', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Testosterone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saint Louis, Catherine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3,