': 'nyt://article/a7ec6fb0-d24c-51bd-8557-1fe48c8abb5b'}, {'abstract': 'A 13-car crash at the beginning of the Belgian Grand Prix that year was just a foretaste of the most accident-marred, topsy-turvy race ever at Spa-Francorchamps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/22/sports/autoracing/the-great-pileup-of-1998.html', 'snippet': 'A 13-car crash at the beginning of the Belgian Grand Prix that year was just a foretaste of the most accident-marred, topsy-turvy race ever at Spa-Francorchamps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Considering that even in 1998 a Formula One car might have been an assemblage of at least a million dollars’ worth of parts, in the first few seconds of the Belgian Grand Prix that year at least $13 million washed away with the rainwater on the inundated track in the series’ biggest multiple-car crash, involving 13 cars at the first corner.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/sports/autoracing/22iht-srf1history22/22iht-srf1history22-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/22/sports/autoracing/22iht-srf1history22/22iht-srf1history22-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/sports/autoracing/22iht-srf1history22/22iht-srf1history22-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/sports/autoracing/22iht-srf1history22/22iht-srf1history22-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1189, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/sports/autoracing/22iht-srf1history22/22iht-srf1history22-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/22/sports/autoracing/22iht-srf1history22/22iht-srf1history22-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/sports/autoracing/22iht-srf1history22/22iht-srf1history22-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Pileup of 1998', 'kicker': 'Special Report: Belgian Grand Prix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recalling a Rainy Race in Which 22 Cars Started and Eight Finished', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T10:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Special Report', '_id': 'nyt://article/b575e63a-6760-55f1-8ce5-f32a874876e1', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b575e63a-6760-55f1-8ce5-f32a874876e1'}, {'abstract': 'While reminiscent of a diner, the food produced with first-rate ingredients in the hands of a well-regarded chef.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/travel/chile-las-cabras-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'While reminiscent of a diner, the food produced with first-rate ingredients in the hands of a well-regarded chef.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fuente de soda is Chile’s particular take on the soda fountain, a culinary institution along the lines of the American diner — friendly, familiar, old-fashioned. You go to one to tuck your tie into your shirt and wolf down a churrasco completo (imagine a comically large hamburger, but made with sliced meat, mashed avocado, tomatoes and mayonnaise). Throw back a freshly made juice or a beer and you’re ready to get back to work.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16BITES-SUB/16BITES-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16BITES-SUB/16BITES-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16BITES-SUB/16BITES-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16BITES-SUB/16BITES-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16BITES-SUB/16BITES-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/16/travel/16BITES-SUB/16BITES-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None,