ks and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T14:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed1d72d4-2710-5de9-83fb-3529cee52a39', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed1d72d4-2710-5de9-83fb-3529cee52a39'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a recent essay by Walter Isaacson and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/books/review/letters-new-orleans-10-years-later.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to a recent essay by Walter Isaacson and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: New Orleans, 10 Years Later', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T14:35:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/6652f5a9-0da2-566e-a1d9-3675f15e0b20', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6652f5a9-0da2-566e-a1d9-3675f15e0b20'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT IS VISIBLE, by Kimberly Elkins. (Twelve, $15.) As a young child in the 1830s, Laura Bridgman suffered a bout of scarlet fever that left her without sight, hearing, taste or smell. She rose to prominence after learning language, despite being both deaf and blind, at the institute that Annie Sullivan and Helen Keller would later attend. Her story is the basis of Elkins’s biographical novel, which imagines Bridgman’s inner life.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T14:36:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joumana Khatib', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joumana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khatib', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d3e471e-5d7e-5ba7-9041-a03edf7700f4', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d3e471e-5d7e-5ba7-9041-a03edf7700f4'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EILEEN, by Ottessa Moshfegh. (Penguin Press, $25.95.) Through her fascinatingly twisted heroine, Moshfegh explores a woman’s relationship to her body — the disconnection, the cultural claims, the male prerogative.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editors’ Choice | Recent Books of Particular Interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T14:36:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/003be93c-a06b-5b35-9d49-17b64c9d2d64', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/003be93c-a06b-5b35-9d49-17b64c9d2d64'}, {'abstract': 'A call to consider how far artificial intelligence technology should go in the quest to make life better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/books/review/machines-of-loving-grace-by-john-markoff.html', 'snippet': 'A call to consider how far artificial intelligence technology should go in the quest to make life better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Technologists rarely question technology in public. Yet last fall Tesla’s chief executive, Elon Musk, suggested we might need to regulate the development of artificial intelligence “just to make sure that we don’t do something very foolish.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23GRIER/23GRIER-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23GRIER/23GRIER-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23GRIER/23GRIER-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23GRIER/23GRIER-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum