ngers of head trauma in athletes and the psyche of football players.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Hit Count,’ by Chris Lynch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Helmet Heads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hit Count (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T15:06:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Volponi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Volponi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccd8f819-6704-51d7-9083-f0107378b9ec', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccd8f819-6704-51d7-9083-f0107378b9ec'}, {'abstract': 'New early readers feature an antic dancer, wiggy pigs and a girl whose dog hits it big. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/books/review/what-this-story-needs-is-a-pig-in-a-wig-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'New early readers feature an antic dancer, wiggy pigs and a girl whose dog hits it big. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'A children’s books editor once asked me what kind of books were needed most in libraries. My immediate response was, “Beginning readers!” Then I had a question: Why aren’t there more available? The editor’s reply was just as fast: “Because they’re too hard to write.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23SUBLUTZ1/0823-BKS-SUBLUTZ1-articleLarge.jp