': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Eleanor (Illustrator)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weing, Drew (1978- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ballet Cat: The Totally Secret Secret (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'What This Story Needs Is a Pig in a Wig (Book)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'In, Over and On! (the Farm) (Book)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Pig Is Big on Books (Book)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Flop to the Top! (Book)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T15:07:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Lutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bded15c9-87e3-587f-a2ea-aecdf37f6962', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bded15c9-87e3-587f-a2ea-aecdf37f6962'}, {'abstract': 'Four picture books show how immigrant children settle into a changed environment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/books/review/mamas-nightingale-by-edwidge-danticat-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Four picture books show how immigrant children settle into a changed environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Picture books have long been concerned with helping children transition to an unfamiliar place. A child’s first day in a new school or a family’s move to a different neighborhood are by now classic subjects. But since the dawn of the 21st century, with the number of immigrants in the United States continuing to increase markedly, children’s authors and publishers have begun to take on a far more challenging task — helping immigrant children settle into a new cultural environment, one that even their parents may find inexplicable. Since the principal obstacle to understanding a culture is, of course, the language that expresses it, language can loom large in these books; and a language divide is a concept difficult to express pictorially. Given all this, a child’s experience of immigration is a subject matter that requires some inventive tactics, as four new books ably demonstrate.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23KIDSYELCHINREV/23KIDSYELCHINREV-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23KIDSYELCHINREV/23KIDSYELCHINREV-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23KIDSYELCHINREV/23KIDSYELCHINREV-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23KIDSYELCHINREV/23KIDSYELCHINREV-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23KIDSYELCHINREV/23KIDSYELCHINREV-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/23/books/review/23KIDSYELCHINREV/23KIDSYELCHINREV-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/