': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/21NYFFWEB/21NYFFWEB-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/21NYFFWEB/21NYFFWEB-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/21NYFFWEB/21NYFFWEB-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/21NYFFWEB/21NYFFWEB-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1088, 'width': 1956, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/21NYFFWEB/21NYFFWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/21NYFFWEB/21NYFFWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/21NYFFWEB/21NYFFWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reunion Screening of ‘O Brother, Where Art Thou?’ and More at the New York Film Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'u2018O Brotheru2019 Screening at New York Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, LAURIE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, PAUL THOMAS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Palma, Brian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenwood, Jonny', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Comment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T16:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99f0e251-2ba6-559b-8dd9-fc1159865f4a', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99f0e251-2ba6-559b-8dd9-fc1159865f4a'}, {'abstract': 'Cate Blanchett is known for playing women who are just barely holding it together. In life, she’s firmly in control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/t-magazine/cate-blanchett-interview-carol-movie.html', 'snippet': 'Cate Blanchett is known for playing women who are just barely holding it together. In life, she’s firmly in control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was Cate Blanchett’s second time climbing the Sydney Harbour Bridge. She couldn’t really say why she wanted to do it, or what it is about heights that appeals to her. She has no interest in skydiving or bungee jumping or parachuting. She’s not especially sporty or athletic. It’s not thrills she likes; it’s control. She once drove her children to the edge of Mount Yasur, an active volcano on the island of Tanna.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '226', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/t-magazine/23womens-well-cate1/23tmag-08well_cate2-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'art