analysis from the research firm CB Insights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It used to be a rare thing when start-ups were valued at $1 billion or more by their investors. Now it’s become so common that there are at least 131 start-ups boasting such valuations and a term — “unicorns” — to refer to the companies. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Companies That May Be the Next 50 Start-Up Unicorns', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delivery Services', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Health Records', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T17:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aa6b964-ded2-5fdc-8df0-8d12d96c37f0', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aa6b964-ded2-5fdc-8df0-8d12d96c37f0'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Wall Street stocks tumble out of sight in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/1890-panic-on-wall-street/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Wall Street stocks tumble out of sight in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This has been the most exciting day Wall Street has seen since the assassination of President Garfield. The stringency in the money market reached such a degree that it precipitated a panic among borrowers and carried the rate of call loans to nearly 190 per cent, the highest rate on record since the chaos resulting from the tragedy of ’81. The demand for funds at this anomalous rate of per cent per day, in addition to the regular rate of interest, cannot honestly be attributed to mere bear manipulation. The eagerness with which long stock was thrown on the market fully attested to the general need for money that prevails in Wall Street. While Wall Street was howling, stocks were tumbling out of sight. The threatened state of affairs on the Vanderbilt railroad system did not improve matters. Heavy liquidation in the entire group was one of the first conspicuous features of the session. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 22, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/blogs/22iht-oldaug22-wallstreet/22iht-oldaug22-wallstreet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 482, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/blogs/22iht-oldaug22-wallstreet/22iht-oldaug22-wallstreet-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 482, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/blogs/22iht-oldaug22-wallstreet/22iht-oldaug22-wallstreet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/22/blogs/22iht-oldaug22-wallstreet/22iht-oldaug22-wallstreet-thumbStandar