ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/793594ab-c144-58c1-9ecc-1ba04d7e0f2e', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/793594ab-c144-58c1-9ecc-1ba04d7e0f2e'}, {'abstract': '“Enduring Images,” which includes works by Andy Warhol and Yonia Fain, seeks to “showcase the artist’s role as a witness or participant in capturing moments of great turmoil,” the museum’s executive director said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/nyregion/a-hofstra-museum-exhibition-offers-views-of-the-past-through-a-softer-light.html', 'snippet': '“Enduring Images,” which includes works by Andy Warhol and Yonia Fain, seeks to “showcase the artist’s role as a witness or participant in capturing moments of great turmoil,” the museum’s executive director said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even though all the art works in “Enduring Images,” an exhibition at Hofstra University in Hempstead, address themes like war, genocide, oppression and natural disasters, several of the paintings, prints and drawings use pastels or bright colors to illuminate the dark subject matter. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI1/23ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI1/23ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI1/23ARTSLI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI1/23ARTSLI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1348, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI1/23ARTSLI1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI1/23ARTSLI1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI1/23ARTSLI1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hofstra Museum Exhibition Offers Views of the Past Through a Softer Light', 'kicker': 'Arts | Hempstead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Views of the Past Through a Softer Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobson, Aileen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hofstra University Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hempstead (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T17:40:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aileen Jacobson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aileen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13eb745d-0758-5344-b72d-419c9311c0d2', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13eb745d-0758-5344-b72d-419c9311c0d2'}, {'abstract': 'A look at a few sequences, from “Caddyshack,” “Ferris Bueller’s Day Off” and other movies, that have helped make cultural milestones of hot-weather fare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/movies/the-other-sounds-of-summer-musical-scenes-that-make-movies-sizzle.html', 'snippet': 'A look at a few sequences, from “Caddyshack,” “Ferris Bueller’s Day Off” and other movies, that have helped make cultural milestones of hot-weather fare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Savvy filmmakers know that when their releases are scheduled during the summer, it helps to include a musical sequence or set piece. This year, “Trainwreck” took appropriate precautions, with a cheerleader-dance finale set to a medley that included 2 Unlimited’s “Get Ready for This” (known for its appearance in “Space Jam”) and Billy Joel’s resilient “Uptown Girl.” It’s part of a long tradition — “Are you ready for the summer?” a chorus of excited children once inquired in Ivan Reitman’s sunbaked 1979 masterpiece, “Meatballs.” Here are a few highlights that have helped make hits and cultural milestones of hot-weather fare through the years.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23SUMMERFILM1/23SUMMERFILM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 247, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23SUMMERFILM1/23SUMMERFILM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 247}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23SUMMERFILM1/23SUMMERFILM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23SUMMERFILM1/23SUMMERFILM1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 845, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23SUMMERFILM1/23SUMMERFILM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23SUMMERFILM1/23SUMMERFILM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/arts/23SUMMERFILM1/23SUMMERFILM1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The (Other) Sounds of Summer: Musical Scenes That Make Movies Sizzle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The (Other) Sounds of Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T17:47:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Spitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/968c292e-db71-56f4-83bf-5f3c25757949', 'word_count': 1531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/968c292e-db71-56f4-83bf-5f3c25757949'}, {'abstract': 'Her implication that kids might be getting vaccines for noncommunicable diseases doesn’t hold water, according to FactCheck.org.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/fact-checking-carly-fiorinas-vaccine-claims/', 'snippet': 'Her implication that kids might be getting vaccines for noncommunicable diseases doesn’t hold water, according to FactCheck.org.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Carly Fiorina said that school districts should be able to deny admission to children who haven’t been vaccinated against “highly communicable diseases.” But, she added, “when we’re talking about some of these more esoteric immunizations, then I think absolutely a parent should have a choice and a school district shouldn’t be able to say, ‘sorry, your kid can’t come to school’ for a disease that’s not communicable, that’s not contagious, and where there really isn’t any proof that they’re necessary at this point.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts & Figures: Carly Fiorina on Vaccines', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tetanus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whooping Cough', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fiorina, Carleton S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FactCheck.org', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T17:47:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be9836e8-6d15-5faa-a33e-b650eda39bbe', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be9836e8-6d15-5faa-a33e-b650eda39bbe'}, {'abstract': 'Removing the application for federal aid would encourage more qualified low-income students to apply to college.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/upshot/fafsa-follies-to-gain-a-student-eliminate-a-form.html', 'snippet': 'Removing the application for federal aid would encourage more qualified low-income students to apply to college.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many smart students forgo college in the mistaken belief that they cannot afford it. The financial aid system, which is intended to increase opportunities for low-income students, is largely to blame.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/upshot/22UP-Sub-VIEW/22UP-Sub-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/22/upshot/22UP-Sub-VIEW/22UP-Sub-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/upshot/22UP-Sub-VIEW/22UP-Sub-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/upshot/22UP-Sub-VIEW/22UP-Sub-VIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1108, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/upshot/22UP-Sub-VIEW/22UP-Sub-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/22/upshot/22UP-Sub-VIEW/22UP-Sub-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/upshot/22UP-Sub-VIEW/22UP-Sub-VIEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fafsa Follies: To Gain a Student, Eliminate a Form', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Gain a College Student, Eliminate a Form', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dynarski, Susan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Aid (Education)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALEXANDER, LAMAR', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennet, Michael Farrand', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T17:54:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Dynarski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dynarski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89f003b3-f368-5be9-82d7-dbfbf5862662', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89f003b3-f368-5be9-82d7-dbfbf5862662'}, {'abstract': 'In Abi Morgan’s “Splendour” at the Donmar Warehouse, Sinead Cusack plays a dictator’s wife who drinks shots with her guests at the palace in a revolution-torn city.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/london-journal-inside-vodka-and-stilettos-outside-the-revolution/', 'snippet': 'In Abi Morgan’s “Splendour” at the Donmar Warehouse, Sinead Cusack plays a dictator’s wife who drinks shots with her guests at the palace in a revolution-torn city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Is it possible to achieve a contact high from alcohol? If so, I should be reeling. Strong drink is flowing freely – and damagingly – on this city’s stages. The night after I saw the Almeida Theater’s wine-soaked production of Euripides’ “Bakkhai,” I spent an evening at the Donmar Warehouse with four mutually contemptuous women who kept filling shot glasses with undiluted vodka.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/Splendour/Splendour-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/Splendour/Splendour-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/Splendour/Splendour-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/Splendour/Splendour-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/Splendour/Splendour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/Splendour/Splendour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/arts/Splendour/Splendour-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: Inside, Vodka and Stilettos; Outside, the Revolution', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cusack, Sinead', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Abi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Donmar Warehouse Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T17:56:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d2c2535-cdad-512f-b546-ba8d2c1d0146', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d2c2535-cdad-512f-b546-ba8d2c1d0146'}, {'abstract': 'Visitors to the Aldrich museum in Ridgefield can explore sloth and other iniquities in recline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/nyregion/a-deadly-sin-at-the-aldrich-from-the-comfort-of-an-armchair.html', 'snippet': 'Visitors to the Aldrich museum in Ridgefield can explore sloth and other iniquities in recline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Strollers along Main Street in Ridgefield, Conn., will encounter a curious signpost planted in front of the Aldrich Contemporary Art Museum. Each of its prongs is inscribed with one of the seven deadly sins followed by mileage information. Six aim westward: Lust, Gluttony, Greed, Wrath, Envy and Pride. The other points east, directly at the museum. It reads “Sloth 0.01 miles.”', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/nyregion/23ARTSWE1/23ARTSWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/nyregion/23ARTSWE1/23ARTSWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 791}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo