bs-india-and-pakistan-seem-on-verge-of-canceling-talks.html', 'snippet': 'The escalation of tensions comes as the foreign ministries on both sides issued tough statements over Pakistan’s plans to meet with Kashmiri separatist leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Talks between India and Pakistan, scheduled for next week in New Delhi, appeared on the brink of collapse Friday after the foreign ministries on both sides traded tough statements over Pakistan’s plans to meet with Kashmiri separatist leaders while in India.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trading Barbs, India and Pakistan Seem on Verge of Canceling Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Briefing | Asia; India: Talks With Pakistan Falter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Najar, Nida', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T19:25:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nida Najar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Najar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fe375f2-1bb0-51df-913e-c8cc80df2476', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fe375f2-1bb0-51df-913e-c8cc80df2476'}, {'abstract': 'Have your recession early!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/carter-reagan-and-machiavelli/', 'snippet': 'Have your recession early!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rex Nutting has a very nice article about the reality of Jimmy Carter’s presidency, which has been distorted out of recognition by the myth of Saint Reagan. As he points out, Carter presided over faster average job growth and lower unemployment than Reagan; unfortunately for Carter, his timing was bad, with vigorous growth for most of his presidency but a recession at the end.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carter, Reagan, and Machiavelli', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T19:28:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94f29df0-96d1-5697-a59c-dcea8ce35227', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94f29df0-96d1-5697-a59c-dcea8ce35227'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Silberman talks about “NeuroTribes: The Legacy of Autism and the Future of Neurodiversity,” and Elisabeth Egan discusses her debut novel, “A Window Opens.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/inside-the-new-york-times-book-review-the-history-of-autism/', 'snippet': 'Steve Silberman talks about “NeuroTribes: The Legacy of Autism and the Future of Neurodiversity,” and Elisabeth Egan discusses her debut novel, “A Window Opens.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In The New York Times Book Review, Jennifer Senior reviews Steve Silberman’s “NeuroTribes: The Legacy of Autism and the Future of Neurodiversity.” Ms. Senior writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima