active/6f939d7b-4e4b-5c5c-9dc1-9bed3ee99b5c'}, {'abstract': 'Home is where the “aw” is.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/21/friday-not-music-talking-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Home is where the “aw” is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Somehow not feeling musical this week. But I recently took a relative to the wonderful Tenement Museum, where we listened among other things to a recording of someone who lived in the building just before it was condemned; it was fascinating, but what got my companion going was the accent, which she found hilarious and I found comforting. After all these years, it’s the sound of home:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Not Music: Talking New York', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-21T21:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43feaa7c-92a0-5390-8170-772f659bfb28', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43feaa7c-92a0-5390-8170-772f659bfb28'}, {'abstract': 'These two new albums feature performances from Arturo O’Farrill and the Afro-Latin Jazz Alliance and Wynton Marsalis and the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/22/arts/music/cuba-the-conversation-continues-and-live-in-cuba-expand-a-musical-dialogue.html', 'snippet': 'These two new albums feature performances from Arturo O’Farrill and the Afro-Latin Jazz Alliance and Wynton Marsalis and the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the American flag was raised over the United States Embassy in Cuba last Friday, the pianist and composer