ds-opposition-to-nuclear-deal.html', 'snippet': 'A military base in Iran has become a symbol of whether international inspectors are interested in digging into the past, or will just be checking boxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the most strident opponents of President Obama’s nuclear deal with Iran, the suspicious behavior at a military base about 12 miles southeast of Tehran has become a rallying call to defeat the accord, especially as it now appears that Iranian officials may be allowed to take their own environmental samples at the site and turn them over to inspectors.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prospect of Self-Inspections by Iran Feeds Opposition to Nuclear Deal', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Critics of Deal Find Fuel in Iran Self-Inspections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Atomic Energy Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amano, Yukiya', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-22T01:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5a4ed90-73a3-5cdc-a2cb-203bd6c27fc2', 'word_count': 1212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5a4ed90-73a3-5cdc-a2cb-203bd6c27fc2'}, {'abstract': 'The lives and deaths of Tom Zbyszewski, Richard Wheeler and Andrew Zajac offer a window into the close-knit world of wildland firefighting in the West.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/22/us/three-killed-in-washington-wildfire-are-mourned.html', 'snippet': 'The lives and deaths of Tom Zbyszewski, Richard Wheeler and Andrew Zajac offer a window into the close-knit world of wildland firefighting in the West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHELAN, Wash. — Tom Zbyszewski, 20, won a poetry-reciting competition but was studying physics at Whitman College, the small liberal arts school in southeastern Washington where he was about to enter his junior year. He also studied Mandarin Chinese and dabbled in theater, and got into firefighting to help pay for school.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/us/22WILDFIRE/22WILDFIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/22/us/22WILDFIRE/22WILDFIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/us/22WILDFIRE/22WILDFIRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/us/22WILDFIRE/22WILDFIRE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1348, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/us/22WILDFIRE/22WILDFIRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/22/us/22WILDFIRE/22WILDFIRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/22/us/22WILDFIRE/22WILDFIRE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Killed in Washington Wildfire Are Mourned', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Killed in Washington Wildfire Are Mourned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Kirk', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeler, Richard (1984-2015)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zajac, Andrew (1988-2015)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zbyszewski, Tom (1994-2015)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-22T01:46:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson and Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7681104a-964d-5afd-be7c-dd2e1fbe68b4', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7681104a-964d-5afd-be7c-dd2e1fbe68b4'}, {'abstract': 'Many supporters of the Labour Party were shocked to find themselves accused of being saboteurs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/22/world/europe/britains-labour-party-accused-of-purging-members.html', 'snippet': 'Many supporters of the Labour Party were shocked to find themselves accused of being saboteurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until this week, Grace Coles, a 24-year-old student in Wales, had never heard of Ken Loach, the great English filmmaker born five decades before her, whose social-realist dramas about the struggles of the British working class are more acclaimed at Cannes these days than in the multiplexes of Cardiff.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For @UKLabour, RT = Endorsement, Apparently', 'kicker': 'Open Source', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For @UKLabour, RT = Endorsement, Apparently', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbyn, Jeremy (1949- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loach, Ken', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-22T01:50:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae06977c-9e79-5abd-8942-1fff1b407859', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae06977c-9e79-5abd-8942-1fff1b407859'}, {'abstract