'value': 'Border Patrol (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citizenship and Immigration Services (US)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-23T12:29:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32179f2b-e036-5cf4-811e-7da8b2f413ca', 'word_count': 1899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32179f2b-e036-5cf4-811e-7da8b2f413ca'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Vichy government in France limits drinking of aperitifs to four days a week in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/1940-vichy-curbs-aperitif-drinking-in-law-against-drunkenness/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Vichy government in France limits drinking of aperitifs to four days a week in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VICHY — Drastic measures to suppress alcoholism and drunkenness in France are embodied in a law which will be published in the ‘‘Journal Officiel’’ tomorrow [Aug. 24]. According to the terms of this law, consumption of aperitifs (drinks before meals) containing more than 16 per cent alcohol will henceforth be prohibited. Furthermore, drinking of aperitifs will be limited to four days a week, namely Mondays, Wednesdays, Fridays and Sundays. The sale of these drinks is also forbidden to minors under twenty years of age. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Vichy Curbs Aperitif Drinking In Law Against Drunkenness', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major':