 party, U Shwe Maung attended dinners with the president and made speeches from the floor of Parliament. But this weekend, the country’s election commission ruled that despite more than four years in office, he was not a citizen and thus was ineligible to run for re-election in landmark voting in November.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Myanmar Striking Rohingya From Voter Rolls, Activists Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar Lawmaker Is Barred From Re-election', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rohingya (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shwe Maung', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-23T16:35:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/629fd737-39d8-53cc-aa33-46dd94f3dfa5', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/629fd737-39d8-53cc-aa33-46dd94f3dfa5'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Bubble-gum art appears on the New York art scene in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/1965-bubble-gum-blows-into-art-world/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Bubble-gum art appears on the New York art scene in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — For those who feel the Theater of the Absurd has had it, there’s a whole new world of absurdities coming up strong in the field of art. Bubble-gum art, for example. Only a few weeks ago, an elaborate announcement extolled its possibilities. Attached to the announcement — and wrapped in hygienic cellophane — were six gaily colored pellets of bubble-gum, not to be chewed and loudly popped, but to be chewed, gingerly removed from the mouth and stuck on a blank canvas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Bubble Gum Blows Into Art World', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Candy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chewing Gum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-23T16:46:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd0d9eb0-e502-56f9-812f-68c2d3c70ad2', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd0d9eb0-e502-56f9-812f-68c2d3c70ad2'}, {'abstract': 'The film, about the rap group N.W.A., which counted Dr. Dre as a founding member, collected an estimated $26.8 million over the weekend, for a two-week total of $111.5 million, according to Rentrak, which compiles box office data.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/23/compton-spends-second-week-at-top-of-box-office/', 'snippet': 'The film, about the rap group N.W.A., which counted Dr. Dre as a founding member, collected an estimated $26.8 million over the weekend, for a two-week total of $111.5 million, according to Rentrak, which compiles box office data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Despite growing dismay that “Straight Outta Compton” glosses over Dr. Dre’s history of physical abuse toward women, that Universal Pictures drama was again the No. 1 movie in North America, easily defeating three R-rated newcomers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Compton’ Spends Second Week at Top of Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Compton’ Tops Box Office For a Second Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dr Dre (1965- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Kristen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'N W A (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twentieth Century Fox', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Universal Pictures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-23T16:48:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4597c8de-5b07-5d88-8cab-695d491ca338', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4597c8de-5b07-5d88-8cab-695d491ca338'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of protesters streamed into downtown Beirut for a second day on Sunday to demand that the government resign over its inability to remove enormous heaps of garbage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/world/middleeast/lebanese-protest-as-trash-piles-up-in-beirut.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of protesters streamed into downtown Beirut for a second day on Sunday to demand that the government resign over its inability to remove enormous heaps of garbage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Thousands of protesters streamed into downtown Beirut for a second day on Sunday to demand that the government resign over its inability to remove enormous heaps of garbage from the city’s streets. The demonstrations led to clashes with the police, who turned fire hoses and tear gas guns on the crowds.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clashes Break Out During Protests Over Trash Crisis in Lebanon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clashes Break Out During Protests Over Trash Crisis in Lebanon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beirut (Lebanon)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salam, Tammam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN RED CROSS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-23T17:19:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hwaida Saad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hwaida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3520b82a-e857-589a-a7a8-393d60cb14b2', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3520b82a-e857-589a-a7a8-393d60cb14b2'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Walker, Chris Christie and Carly Fiorina each took shots at Mr. Trump on the Sunday morning news shows over his immigration proposals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/08/23/as-rivals-snipe-trump-dodges-questions-on-details-of-immigration-plan/', 'snippet': 'Scott Walker, Chris Christie and Carly Fiorina each took shots at Mr. Trump on the Sunday morning news shows over his immigration proposals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald J. Trump repeatedly side-stepped questions on Sunday about how he would pay for his new plan to deport undocumented immigrants, and he also faced criticism from several rivals for the Republican presidential nomination about his call to end so-called birthright citizenship for children of those immigrants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/us/23trump-firstdraft/23trump-firstdraft-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/23/us/23trump-firstdraft/23trump-firstdraft-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/us/23trump-firstdraft/23trump-firstdraft-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/us/23trump-firstdraft/23trump-firstdraft-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/23/us/23trump-firstdraft/23trump-firstdraft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/