a451', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/618bc3b2-e06f-52cf-ad77-6b5a748fa451'}, {'abstract': 'New rules to speed up play have been in effect for more than three months and are beginning to shave several minutes off games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/sports/baseball/baseball-on-the-clock.html', 'snippet': 'New rules to speed up play have been in effect for more than three months and are beginning to shave several minutes off games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRENTON — On the first day that minor league baseball’s new rules to speed up the game went into full effect this season, a home-plate umpire ejected the manager of the Class AA Trenton Thunder for arguing.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Baseball, the Times Are Changing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changing Times in Baseball ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casey, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkman, Seth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T02:41:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Casey and Seth Berkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dfd3cdb-ce8e-550d-bee6-84e67076a44c', 'word_count': 2394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dfd3cdb-ce8e-550d-bee6-84e67076a44c'}, {'abstract': 'Hunter-Reay won the crash-filled IndyCar race which left Justin Wilson in a coma and critical condition when he was hit in the head by a piece of debris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/sports/ryan-hunter-reay-wins-at-pocono.html', 'snippet': 'Hunter-Reay won the crash-filled IndyCar race which left Justin Wilson in a coma and critical condition when he was hit in the head by a piece of debris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the Belgian Grand Prix in Spa-Francorchamps on Sunday, expectations of chaos were high because of a new rule designed to liven up the track action by giving full technical responsibility over clutch settings to the drivers at the start of the race, instead of having them take precise instructions from their team engineers over the radio. But the start went off practically without a hitch, and the explosive action came in the penultimate lap of the race, when the right rear tire of Sebastian Vettel’s Ferrari blew out while he was in third place. That handed Romain Grosjean and his Lotus team their first podium finish since the 2013 United States Grand Prix. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Hunter-Reay Wins at Pocono', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sports Briefing | Auto Racing; Podium Finish for Grosjean', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grosjean, Romain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indy Racing League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pocono Raceway', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter-Reay, Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '201