lead_paragraph': 'conception • \\kən-ˈsep-shən\\ • noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day + Quiz | conception', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T04:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ebd7179-d008-568c-a3a4-332de1b317ef', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ebd7179-d008-568c-a3a4-332de1b317ef'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Cinemax) MAPS TO THE STARS (2015) Havana Segrand (Julianne Moore, above), an actress on the verge of unraveling at any moment, has seen the apparition of her mother — a more famous actress, who died in a fire when she was young — and seeks therapy from a self-help guru (John Cusack). He happens to be the father of Benjie Weiss (Evan Bird), an obnoxious young star, and his older sister, Agatha (Mia Wasikowska), who was banished from the family after setting a fire that may have been intended to kill her brother, and which badly burned her. Eventually Agatha befriends a limo driver (Robert Pattinson) and turns an Internet acquaintanceship with Carrie Fisher into a job as Havana’s personal assistant. “Suavely directed by David Cronenberg from an elegantly waspish script by Bruce Wagner, it belongs to the venerable tradition of movieland self-loathing,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “It takes a perverse effort of will to love ‘Maps to the Stars.’ It’s a little too chilly, and in some places too easy. But you may find yourself drawn back to it, and retracing its route from the familiar to the uncanny, from entertainment to revulsion, from dream to nightmare.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T04:05:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c7b59f5-8e7d-59dd-81c6-c17ff0314b69', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c7b59f5-8e7d-59dd-81c6-c17ff0314b69'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, August 24, 2015', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-monday-august-24-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, August 24, 2015', 'lead_paragraph': '“He seemed like he was ready to fight to the end, and so were we.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, August 24, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T05:24:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/21a225ea-6960-52e4-99af-6c4c0cda97ae', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21a225ea-6960-52e4-99af-6c4c0cda97ae'}, {'abstract': 'As the tensions between Russian and Ukraine have continued, Pavel Volkov has explored the lives of young Russian conscripts with mixed reactions to the conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/a-russian-solider-story/', 'snippet': 'As the tensions between Russian and Ukraine have continued, Pavel Volkov has explored the lives of young Russian conscripts with mixed reactions to the conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Ukrainian revolution and Russia’s annexation of Crimea, Pavel Volkov wondered how young Russian Army conscripts felt about becoming part of the turmoil they — and the rest of the world — saw play out on television and in newspapers. Mr. Volkov traveled for eight months around military bases in Russia, taking photographs and asking questions. The resulting body of work is a portrait of Russian youth with mixed feelings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Russian Soldier Story', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Volkov, Pavel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crimea (Ukraine)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T07:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Boryga', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boryga', 'qualifier': Non