nyt://article/096b14a5-179b-5f29-9a35-4f5198c3f7af'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A cholera epidemic hit Spain in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/1890-cholera-epidemic-hits-spain/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A cholera epidemic hit Spain in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — Reports received to-day from the cholera-infected districts show a heavy increase of the epidemic in Toledo, where there are fifty-one new cases in the city and twenty-seven in the suburbs and in Valencia. In the other provinces the epidemic is stationary. The official record for the 22nd was seventy-one new cases and fifty-one deaths and for the 23rd it was 139 new cases and sixty-six deaths. The total figures for the whole of Spain since the commencement of the epidemic are: Number of cases 2,393, number of deaths 1,203. The fumigation to which travelers arriving at Seville are subjected is so severe that many have been made seriously ill. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 25, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1890: Cholera Epidemic Hits Spain', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T12:55:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f649faec-3604-50a0-a76a-0fdf87074