ect', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scarves', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sewing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Ellen J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T16:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79462136-9c45-547d-9d41-7bf856b52de1', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79462136-9c45-547d-9d41-7bf856b52de1'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A British squadron attacked the Belgian coast in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/1915-britain-shells-belgian-coast/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A British squadron attacked the Belgian coast in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROTTERDAM — This morning a British squadron of considerable strength carried out a great bombardment of the German positions on the Belgian coast. The attack was the most important in the number of ships engaged and the fierceness of the fire since the enemy’s occupation of the littoral. It is reported that great damage was done, principally to the military works at Zeebrugge. The thunder of the fleet’s guns was heard all over Zeeland, where the windows of houses at places miles inland rattled. The sound carried distinctly to Flushing. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 25, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/24/blogs/24iht-oldaug24-puck/2