 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T16:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7cdc632a-99e3-541c-8290-167d5081820a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7cdc632a-99e3-541c-8290-167d5081820a'}, {'abstract': 'When one parent is planning to leave a marriage, how can both spouses prepare a preschooler for the change?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/how-do-you-talk-to-a-3-year-old-about-a-divorce-you-dont-want/', 'snippet': 'When one parent is planning to leave a marriage, how can both spouses prepare a preschooler for the change?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our occasional parenting Quandaries, we pull from the comments, the weekly open thread or email a question that we know (or at least suspect) plagues more than one parent. You — the readers — provide the advice. Today’s question comes from a commenter many will recognize as a long-time member of the community—Ramona, from Toronto. If you have advice, and particularly if you’ve been where she is and come through it, please help. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Talk to a 3-Year-Old About a Divorce You Don’t Want?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T16:14:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f740c66e-a700-5eb5-ac6c-ede720df3eb4', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f740c66e-a700-5eb5-ac6c-ede720df3eb4'}, {'abstract': 'Raising healthy twins is a unique problem for the zoo’s mother panda: Only two mother bears have successfully done so in captivity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/science/two-panda-cubs-at-the-national-zoo-present-special-problems.html', 'snippet': 'Raising healthy twins is a unique problem for the zoo’s mother panda: Only two mother bears have successfully done so in captivity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two tiny giant panda cubs, each weighing about as much as a stick of butter, are the focus at the National Zoo in Washington of an intense, round-the-clock effort to keep them alive, but the odds are against them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Panda Cubs at the National Zoo Present Special Problems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pandas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian National Zoological Park', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neiffer, Donald Leroy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T16:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Rogers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rogers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f3d8cfd-a5b6-5a3e-9077-8a45df310670', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f3d8cfd-a5b6-5a3e-9077-8a45df310670'}, {'abstract': 'New food companies are giving the established names a run for the money as consumers seek out novel products and better ingredients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/26/dining/start-up-food-business