', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Small Food Brands, Big Successes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Small Brands, Big Hits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strom, Stephanie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kensington & Sons LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CircleUp Network Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whole Foods Market Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zevia LLC', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T16:36:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0207720e-6e2c-598c-8f24-4ef542faebc1', 'word_count': 1612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0207720e-6e2c-598c-8f24-4ef542faebc1'}, {'abstract': 'Reporter Ian Austen provides insight into his reporting on Canadian maple syrup and the disquiet in that country’s sugar camps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/insider/inside-the-maple-syrup-beat-reporters-notebook.html', 'snippet': 'Reporter Ian Austen provides insight into his reporting on Canadian maple syrup and the disquiet in that country’s sugar camps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While reporting from the Tour de France in July, I encountered a rare reminder of Canada one morning. In the hotel’s breakfast room there was a bottle of Maple Joe Absolutely Pure Maple Syrup. Just as prominent on the label was the English phrase “Produce of Canada” and, presumably to drive home that point, a drawing of broad-shouldered Joe, who has an improbable beard and wears a plaid shirt and red hunter’s cap. It was a vivid reminder of the article I wrote about Quebec maple syrup, a barrel of which is worth more today than a barrel of crude oil.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/24/insider/24-Insider-Maple/24-Insider-Maple-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/24/insider/24-Insider-Maple/24-Insider-Maple-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/24/insider/24-Insider-Maple/24-Insider-Maple-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/24/insider/24-Insider-Maple/24-Insider-Maple-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/24/insider/24-Insider-Maple/24-Insider-Maple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/24/insider/24-Insider-Maple/24-Insider-Maple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/24/insider/24-Insider-Maple/24-Inside