unt': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/639814a6-ec18-5317-adf3-553227c48dc4'}, {'abstract': 'On a chaotic path through the Balkans, tens of thousands of migrants are pushing to reach northern Serbia before Hungary seals the border.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/world/europe/migrants-push-toward-hungary-as-a-border-fence-rises.html', 'snippet': 'On a chaotic path through the Balkans, tens of thousands of migrants are pushing to reach northern Serbia before Hungary seals the border.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TISZASZIGET, Hungary — Roiling everything in its path, a wave of tens of thousands of migrants and refugees — many fleeing wars in Iraq, Syria and Afghanistan — has worked its way up the length of the Balkans in recent days.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/world/25MIGRANTS-1/25MIGRANTS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/25/world/25MIGRANTS-1/25MIGRANTS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/world/25MIGRANTS-1/25MIGRANTS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/world/25MIGRANTS-1/25MIGRANTS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/world/25MIGRANTS-1/25MIGRANTS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/25/world/25MIGRANTS-1/25MIGRANTS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/world/25MIGRANTS-1/25MIGRANTS-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Migrants Race North as Hungary Builds a Border Fence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Migrants Race North as Hungary Builds a Fence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Border Barriers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Balkan States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T18:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c48cf9b-4592-56d5-90d9-05236716e020', 'word_count': 1551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c48cf9b-4592-56d5-90d9-05236716e020'}, {'abstract': 'The designers Andrew Paulson and Sean Dougall live and work in a renovated space filled with art, objects and looms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/24/t-magazine/dougall-paulson-home-studio-los-angeles.html', 'snippet': 'The designers Andrew Paulson and Sean Dougall live and work in a renovated space filled with art, objects and looms.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We’re making the sprawl work to our favor,” says Andrew Paulson, a self-taught weaver and one half of the Los Angeles-based design duo Dougall Paulson. Paulson and his partner in life and work, the ceramist Sean Dougall, live in Watts, a neighborhood that’s recently begun to show signs of a renaissance 50 years after the 1965 riots, thanks to chefs like Roy Choi and Daniel Patterson, who are opening a new restaurant there later this year, and Frank Gehry, who is set to collaborate on a local community center for the Children’s Institute Inc. “People ask us, ‘Is that the new neighborhood?’” says Dougall, noting the 75 blocks that separate Watts from downtown’s flourishing arts district. “We’re not feeding off of an existing art scene. We’re trying to build our own visual language, on an island.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Watts, Turning an Old Light Bulb Factory Into a Home', 'kicker': 'Home and Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T18:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dda8e644-4d4b-5e2b-b091-7c57d0641025', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dda8e644-4d4b-5e2b-b091-7c57d0641025'}, {'abstract'