unt': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/733007fb-269d-5af5-bda0-6802918e4868'}, {'abstract': 'The festival’s final installment, on Sunday night in Tompkins Square Park, included the saxophonists Joe Lovano and Rudresh Mahanthappa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/arts/music/review-charlie-parker-jazz-festival-subtly-recalls-its-inspiration.html', 'snippet': 'The festival’s final installment, on Sunday night in Tompkins Square Park, included the saxophonists Joe Lovano and Rudresh Mahanthappa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Charlie Parker Jazz Festival comes by its name with a blissfully casual reverence. The festival, whose 22nd edition ran over the weekend, involves free outdoor concerts in Harlem and the East Village, neighborhoods where Parker, the pioneering alto saxophonist and bebop lodestar, once lived. It always falls near his birthday. (Born on Aug. 29, he would have turned 95 this year. He died at 34.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25PARKER1/25PARKER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25PARKER1/25PARKER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25PARKER1/25PARKER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25PARKER1/25PARKER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1313, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25PARKER1/25PARKER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25PARKER1/25PARKER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25PARKER1/25PARKER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Charlie Parker Jazz Festival Subtly Recalls Its Inspiration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honoring a Master by Recalling, Not Echoing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parker, Charlie, Jazz Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tompkins Square Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovano, Joe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spalding, Esperanza', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahanthappa, Rudresh', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Parks Foundation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T22:06:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0d81e23-cbe2-5489-b410-c2d44c52d12d', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0d81e23-cbe2-5489-b410-c2d44c52d12d'}, {'abstract': 'A four-day festival, Journey to the Son, will explore the music of Son House, whose Rochester years will also be commemorated with a Mississippi Blues Trail marker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/arts/music/son-house-inspires-a-rochester-blues-festival.html', 'snippet': 'A four-day festival, Journey to the Son, will explore the music of Son House, whose Rochester years will also be commemorated with a Mississippi Blues Trail marker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROCHESTER — A sign about eight miles east of this city’s storied Corn Hill neighborhood points out a historical landmark, the rail yard where the blues musician Son House worked as a porter in the 1940s. The vowel in House’s nickname (he was born Eddie) is an odd size, rising about a half inch above the letters on either side. An explanation of sorts can be seen in the abrupt curvature at the top of the first O: The original sign misspelled his name as “SUN,” and the U was rounded off after the fact.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25SONHOUSE/25SONHOUSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25SONHOUSE/25SONHOUSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 764}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25SONHOUSE/25SONHOUSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25SONHOUSE/25SONHOUSE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1610, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25SONHOUSE/25SONHOUSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25SONHOUSE/25SONHOUSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/25/arts/25SONHOUSE/25SONHOUSE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Son House Inspires a Rochester Blues Festival', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Man From Rochester, by Way of Mississippi ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grode, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rochester (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geva Theater Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blues Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'House, Son (1902-88)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T22:09:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Grode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4829e32-e9e0-5df4-8109-e7e64bd76022', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4829e32-e9e0-5df4-8109-e7e64bd76022'}, {'abstract': 'Local rebels and an international aid group accused the militant group of using mustard gas against civilian and rival insurgents in northern Syria last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/world/middleeast/isis-suspected-of-chemical-attack-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Local rebels and an international aid group accused the militant group of using mustard gas against civilian and rival insurgents in northern Syria last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — The Islamic State may have used chemical agents in an attack against civilians and rival insurgents in northern Syria late last week, according to local rebels and an international aid group.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Report of ISIS Using Poison Gas in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Report of Islamic State Using Poison Gas in Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shoumali, Karam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yeginsu, Ceylan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syrian Army', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T22:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karam Shoumali and Ceylan Yeginsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shoumali', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank'