f the genre’s politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year’s Hugo Awards, given to the best in science fiction, turned into a referendum on the genre’s politics. Two blocks of conservative authors and fans, calling themselves the Sad Puppies and the Rabid Puppies, have argued that the Hugos have become a litmus test of political correctness, valuing the racial and sexual identities of authors over their storytelling skills. This year, the groups used their leverage to fill categories with their own preferred nominees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Puppies’ Unrewarded at Sci-Fi Book Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalzi, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-24T23:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9db9175-8134-5ad6-82fc-033819254974', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9db9175-8134-5ad6-82fc-033819254974'}, {'abstract': 'David Hurn’s celebrity photos helped shape popular memories of the 1960s. But he was more drawn to the stuff of daily life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/08/24/blogs/20150824-lens-hurn.html', 'snippet': 'David Hurn’s celebrity photos helped shape popular memories of the 1960s. But he was more drawn to the stuff of daily life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Hurn’s celebrity photos helped shape popular memories of the 1960s. But he was more drawn to the stuff of daily life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, '