'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0e70966-8ded-5011-adf9-e77e5ee6f33c', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0e70966-8ded-5011-adf9-e77e5ee6f33c'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis of market share of insurance companies offering private Medicare plans found that nearly all American markets were already “highly concentrated.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/business/with-mergers-concerns-grow-about-private-medicare.html', 'snippet': 'An analysis of market share of insurance companies offering private Medicare plans found that nearly all American markets were already “highly concentrated.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As some of the nation’s largest health insurers plan to merge, a new report raises fresh concern over the lack of competition in the private Medicare market. The analysis, released on Tuesday, concludes “there is little competition anywhere in the nation.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Mergers, Concerns Grow About Private Medicare', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Mergers, Concerns Grow About Private Medicare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abelson, Reed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commonwealth Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-25T04:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea95f549-8696-55f0-9e3e-1a2de1c27f78', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea95f549-8696-55f0-9e3e-1a2de1c27f78'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (Cinemax) DALLAS BUYERS CLUB (2013) A fiercely gaunt Matthew McConaughey, in an Oscar-winning role, portrays Ron Woodroof, a Texas electrician and rodeo rider who, after learning in 1985 that he is H.I.V.-positive, decides to treat himself by hunting down medication that is not then legal in the United States. He eventually begins a subscription service, selling contraband medicine for a monthly fee. Jared Leto, in another Oscar-winning performance, plays Rayon, a transgender woman who becomes Ron’s business partner. And Jennifer Garner is the doctor who turns into an ally. What is largely missing from this drama, directed by Jean-Marc Vallée and inspired by real events, “is the sense that Ron’s efforts are part of a larger movement,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “Ron’s bravery and determination are entirely credible, thanks to Mr. McConaughey’s disciplined, high-spirited performance and the filmmakers’ interest in the complexity of the character. But his actions unfold in something of a vacuum.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], '