 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Longo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a02eeea3-22cb-5d2d-9773-16e371a268e5', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a02eeea3-22cb-5d2d-9773-16e371a268e5'}, {'abstract': '“Leadership is most important of all” when it comes to solutions to the violence against incarcerated people, a Human Rights Watch senior adviser says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/opinion/prisons-mental-illness-and-excessive-force.html', 'snippet': '“Leadership is most important of all” when it comes to solutions to the violence against incarcerated people, a Human Rights Watch senior adviser says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prisons, Mental Illness and Excessive Force', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prison and Mental Illness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Guards and Corrections Officers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-25T07:21:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ab84fab-4a8d-5ef9-8e6a-262020d431d9', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ab84fab-4a8d-5ef9-8e6a-262020d431d9'}, {'abstract': 'The most important decisions in life should be based not on what we think we want, but on what or whom we admire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/opinion/david-brooks-the-big-decisions.html', 'snippet': 'The most important decisions in life should be based not on what we think we want, but on what or whom we admire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s say you had the chance to become a vampire. With one magical bite you would gain immortality, superhuman strength and a life of glamorous intensity. Your friends who have undergone the transformation say the experience is incredible. They drink animal blood, not human blood, and say everything about their new existence provides them with fun, companionship and meaning.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1003, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1891, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Decisions', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Big Decisions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Laurie Ann (1966- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Transformative Experience (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-25T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0402d834-cb73-5325-87ea-a21aeb6decd8', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0402d834-cb73-5325-87ea-a21aeb6decd8'}, {'abstract': 'It’s frustrating that his lasting accomplishments have gone unrecognized.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/opinion/jimmy-carters-unheralded-legacy.html', 'snippet': 'It’s frustrating that his lasting accomplishments have gone unrecognized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — AS Jimmy Carter moves into the twilight of his life, it is enormously frustrating for those of us who worked closely with him in the White House to witness h