uri': 'nyt://article/587a58be-3d16-520d-83b0-4dac9a4275e0'}, {'abstract': 'What do you predict will happen to global stock markets in the coming days and weeks?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/news-qs-stock-markets-tumble-as-upheaval-continues/', 'snippet': 'What do you predict will happen to global stock markets in the coming days and weeks?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Note: We’ve updated 6 Q’s About the News for the new school year. Let us know what you think.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Q’s | Stock Markets Tumble as Upheaval Continues', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-08-25T08:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab1a4b62-c558-5ac4-a808-ba7fbca28f42', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab1a4b62-c558-5ac4-a808-ba7fbca28f42'}, {'abstract': 'A narrative history of the continuing efforts to weaken the Voting Rights Act of 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/30/books/review/give-us-the-ballot-by-ari-berman.html', 'snippet': 'A narrative history of the continuing efforts to weaken the Voting Rights Act of 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty years ago, when President Lyndon B. Johnson signed the Voting Rights Act on Aug. 6, 1965, he felt, his daughter Luci said, “a great sense of victory on one side and a great sense of fear on the other.” According to Ari Berman, a political correspondent for The Nation, he knew the law would transform American politics and democracy more than any other civil rights bill in the 20th century, but he also feared that it would deliver the South to the Republican Party for years to come. Both predictions proved to be accurate. “The revolution of 1965 spawned an equally committed group of counterrevolutionaries,” Berman writes in “Give Us the Ballot.” “Since the V.R.A.’s passage, they have waged a decades-long campaign to restrict voting rights.” Berman argues that these counterrevolutionaries have “in recent years, controlled a majority on the Supreme Court” and “have set their sights on undoing the accomplishments of the 1960s civil rights movement.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30ROSEN/30Rosen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 914, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30ROSEN/30Rosen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 914}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30ROSEN/30Rosen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 673, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30ROSEN/30Rosen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1345, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30ROSEN/30ROSEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30ROSEN/30ROSEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image