'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NIKE Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uniforms', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sporting Goods and Equipment', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knight, Phil', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Maryland', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Oregon', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-25T20:55:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fd3ebcb-d88e-50f0-8fba-69b6a7721e6f', 'word_count': 1737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fd3ebcb-d88e-50f0-8fba-69b6a7721e6f'}, {'abstract': 'In this book, Gilbert M. Gaul examines how a small percentage of teams generate big revenue, often leaving others to sustain losses while trying to keep pace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/26/books/review-billion-dollar-ball-explores-the-economics-of-college-footballs-top-programs.html', 'snippet': 'In this book, Gilbert M. Gaul examines how a small percentage of teams generate big revenue, often leaving others to sustain losses while trying to keep pace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it is reported that the University of Alabama pays its head coach an annual salary of $6.5 million a year, or that the University of Oregon erected a $42 million academic support center for it players, or that the University of Texas assesses its fans as much as $20,000 in the form of “seat donations” for preferred locations, it is clear that college football is no longer just a game.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/arts/26BOOKGILBERT1/26BOOKGILBERT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/26/arts/26BOOKGILBERT1/26BOOKGILBERT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/arts/26BOOKGILBERT1/26BOOKGILBERT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/arts/26BOOKGILBERT1/26BOOKGILBERT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1434, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/arts/26BOOKGILBERT1/26BOOKGILBERT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/26/arts/26BOOKGILBERT1/26BOOKGILBERT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/arts/26BOOKGILBERT1/26BOOKGILBERT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Billion-Dollar Ball’ Explores the Economics of College Football’s Top Programs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Sport&#8217;s Most Alluring Statistic Is Found on the Balance Sheet ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub'