ton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After months of speculation, the Sydney Theater Company has appointed a new artistic director to succeed Andrew Upton, who announced his exit from the position in February.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/25CHURCHWEB/25CHURCHWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/25CHURCHWEB/25CHURCHWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/25CHURCHWEB/25CHURCHWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/25CHURCHWEB/25CHURCHWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/25CHURCHWEB/25CHURCHWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/25CHURCHWEB/25CHURCHWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/25CHURCHWEB/25CHURCHWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sydney Theater Company Names New Artistic Director', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sydney Theater Company  Names Artistic Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-25T21:10:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Wolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03d2dbfe-d027-52c6-9fc8-b933a28e083e', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03d2dbfe-d027-52c6-9fc8-b933a28e083e'}, {'abstract': 'Pete Sampras, Andre Agassi, Serena Williams and more played tennis in the street in front of fans last night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/t-magazine/tennis-players-serena-williams-pete-sampras-andre-agassi-photos.html', 'snippet': 'Pete Sampras, Andre Agassi, Serena Williams and more played tennis in the street in front of fans last night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1995, Andre Agassi and Pete Sampras appeared together in a commercial for Nike. In the ad, a taxi pulls up to a bustling New York intersection; the players run onto the street, unfurl a net and begin a game of pick-up tennis. Last night, in honor of its 20th anniversary — and to mark the 2015 U.S. Open, which begins next week — Sampras and Agassi reconvened to restage the ad, taxi and all, in another made-for-TV (and now, publicist-orchestrated) moment: They played a quick round of tennis in front of fans on a pop-up tennis court in the Meatpacking District. They were joined by Serena Williams, Maria Sharapova, Rafael Nadal and Roger Federer — and many more. Photographer Dina Litovsky was on hand to capture the scene.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tennis Greats Convene for a U.S.-Open-Themed Spectacle', 'kicker': 'The Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'