nal accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caroline Kennedy, the United States ambassador to Japan, and several other senior American diplomats there have used personal email accounts to conduct State Department business, the inspector general for the department said in a report released Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caroline Kennedy Used Personal Email for State Department Business, Report Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Caroline Kennedy Used Personal Email for State Department Business, Report Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Michael S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Caroline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Linick, Steve A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inspectors General', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-25T23:27:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89ac8fec-7e62-59f6-ad4b-cc33b59bd436', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89ac8fec-7e62-59f6-ad4b-cc33b59bd436'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Rosenkrantz discusses her recently reissued 1968 book, which is made up of candid conversations about psychoanalysis, sex and art.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/among-friends-linda-rosenkrantz-on-talk/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Rosenkrantz discusses her recently reissued 1968 book, which is made up of candid conversations about psychoanalysis, sex and art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Linda Rosenkrantz spent the summer of 1965 in East Hampton recording conversations between herself and two close friends. The resulting book, “Talk,” is formatted like a play, with the three characters discussing their ambitions in the buzzing 1960s New York City art world and cultural sea changes in psychoanalysis and sexual politics. (“How does a ménage à trois work?” someone asks. “Doesn’t it make you feel competitive?”) When it was published in 1968, the book was called fiction. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Among Friends: Linda Rosenkrantz on ‘Talk’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tape Recorder and a Summer in the Hamptons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-25T23:28:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb57d96-dd49-508c-b847-ae4f1c624d12', 'word_count': 1338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb57d96-dd49-508c-b847-ae4f1c624d12'}, {'abstract': 'Notably absent on the list of underwriters for what would be one of the biggest market debuts of the year is JPMorgan Chase, which recently settled a hiring dispute with First Data.', 'web_url': 'h