-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/blogs/20150830JOINTss-slide-8FLD/20150830JOINTss-slide-8FLD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seafood With a Popular Touch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Seafood Restaurant and Fish Market (Center Moriches, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Dennis F (1958- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-26T03:25:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/986f0bec-9feb-52a4-b955-874a84b34a13', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/986f0bec-9feb-52a4-b955-874a84b34a13'}, {'abstract': 'A court in China’s western region of Xinjiang tried two brothers of an American reporter on charges of endangering state security and leaking secrets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/26/world/asia/china-legal-ordeals-for-brothers-of-a-journalist.html', 'snippet': 'A court in China’s western region of Xinjiang tried two brothers of an American reporter on charges of endangering state security and leaking secrets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A court in China’s western region of Xinjiang tried two brothers of an American reporter on charges of endangering state security and leaking secrets, according to a spokesman for Radio Free Asia, the journalist’s employer. No verdict has yet been announced in the trials of Shawket Hoshur on Tuesday and his younger brother Rexim Hoshur, which took place on Aug. 19, Rohit Mahajan, a spokesman for the United States government-funded R.F.A., said in an interview. Their brother, Shohret Hoshur, is a United States citizen whose reports on the Chinese government’s crackdown on Xinjiang’s Uighur ethnic group have been criticized by Beijing. The plight of Shohret Hoshur’s brothers — a third brother, Tudaxun, was convicted of endangering state security last year and sentenced to five years in prison — has become an issue between the two countries before President Xi Jinping’s summit meeting with President Obama in Washington next month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Legal Ordeals for Brothers of a Journalist', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asia; China: Legal Ordeals for Brothers of a Journalist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forsythe, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoshur, Shohret (1965- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio Free Asia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-26T03:26:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Forsythe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Forsythe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/448acbf0-43f7-548d-ba81-c1495c6e642b', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/448acbf0-43f7-548d-ba81-c1495c6e642b'}, {'abstract': 'As one expectant mother discovered, many Chinese seeking to give birth in the United States are encountering new obstacles, as the government cracks down on abuses.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/25/closer-scrutiny-as-chinese-seek-to-give-birth-in-the-united-states/', 'snippet': 'As one expectant mother discovered, many Chinese seeking to give birth in the United States are encountering new obstacles, as the government cracks down on abuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Ma Yi, 36, a senior manager from Shanghai, landed at Los Angeles International Airport on June 5, she had her own version of the American dream. She was entering her eighth month of pregnancy and intended to give birth to an American baby.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Closer Scrutiny as Chinese Seek to Give Birth in the United States', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Customs and Border Protection (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles International Airport', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-26