rd_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3676138a-d76c-5cb3-bcba-5f15b065781c'}, {'abstract': 'A picture book captures the bittersweet mood of the end of summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/26/books/review/the-specific-ocean-review.html', 'snippet': 'A picture book captures the bittersweet mood of the end of summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the possible drawbacks of a family vacation is that it requires leaving somewhere, then arriving somewhere, twice over. With certain children, that is far more challenging than it sounds. The narrator of “The Specific Ocean” is this kind of child – sensitive, internal, averse to change. She’s reluctant to leave her home and friends in the city for a trip to the beach far away. We see her curled up on her bed, wearing her backpack, as her father tries to lure her out the door. Even arriving at their breathtaking destination — “a boxy house on the Pacific Ocean” — does not impress her. There is “dull, droning, dreary water” all around. The next day she stays in the house while her mother and brother go down to the beach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/books/review/26childrens/26childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/26/books/review/26childrens/26childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/books/review/26childrens/26childrens-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/books/review/26childrens/26childrens-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name':