great strength of Dale Russakoff’s heartbreaking and disheartening book, “The Prize: Who’s in Charge of America’s Schools,” (Houghton Mifflin Harcourt, 2015) is its steadfast insistence on avoiding generalities and explaining realities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/business/db-bookentry-web1/db-bookentry-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/27/business/db-bookentry-web1/db-bookentry-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/business/db-bookentry-web1/db-bookentry-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/business/db-bookentry-web1/db-bookentry-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/business/db-bookentry-web1/db-bookentry-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/27/business/db-bookentry-web1/db-bookentry-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/business/db-bookentry-web1/db-bookentry-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Melting of Mark Zuckerberg’s Donation to Newark Schools', 'kicker': 'Book Entry', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pact to Save Newark’s Schools Goes Awry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russakoff, Dale', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-26T18:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan A. Knee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Knee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9e8bc38-1563-5516-ab0a-1c9fd5936e48', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9e8bc38-1563-5516-ab0a-1c9fd5936e48'}, {'abstract': 'The less-harried Asian side of Istanbul is a greener, cleaner swath of the city that offers its own multicultural mix of Ottoman palaces, intriguing cuisine and hipster nightlife.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/30/travel/what-to-do-in-36-hours-in-istanbul.html', 'snippet': 'The less-harried Asian side of Istanbul is a greener, cleaner swath of the city that offers its own multicultural mix of Ottoman palaces, intriguing cuisine and hipster nightlife.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lines to enter major sites on the European side of Istanbul, Turkey’s cultural capital, can stretch for hours. But just across the Bosporus lies the less-harried Asian side, a greener, cleaner and often more conservative swath of the city that offers its own multicultural mix of Ottoman palaces, artsy hotels, tasty cuisine and hipster night life. Here, at the gateway to Anatolia, hilly pine-forest trails in former fishing villages offer opportunities to burn off the baklava, while shady tea gardens abound for those who prefer relaxing with a water view. Wealthy Turks live in villas to the north, while miles to the south, party-friendly Kadikoy is bursting with vegetable and fish markets and bookstores, and is home to a street devoted to bars.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Istanbul, Asian Side', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours in Istanbul, Asian Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fowler, Susanne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosporus (Turkey)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-26T18:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Fowler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fowler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5b9db9c-8735-5300-89e3-a88b773cb23f', 'word_count': 1644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5b9db9c-8735-5300-89e3-a88b773cb23f'}, {'abstract': 'The $47 billion merger required aggressive assumptions and carried risks. Syngenta’s management now needs to prove its reluctance to a deal was worth it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/27/business/dealbook/questions-for-syngenta-as-monsanto-walks-away.html', 'snippet': 'The $47 billion merger required aggressive assumptions and carried risks. Syngenta’s management now needs to prove its reluctance to a deal was worth it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monsanto, the world’s largest seed maker, has abandon