ame': None, 'lastname': 'Joffe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/082ccc87-2ef3-51e5-adf7-28c7b013b3a8', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/082ccc87-2ef3-51e5-adf7-28c7b013b3a8'}, {'abstract': 'The bad guys are no match for a bullied woman in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/30/books/review/girl-waits-with-gun-by-amy-stewart.html', 'snippet': 'The bad guys are no match for a bullied woman in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amy Stewart’s first novel, “Girl Waits With Gun,” follows her award-\xadwinning nonfiction — “The Drunken Botanist,” itself a dram of good cheer after her previous, excellently informative \xaddoses of bad news in the shape of rampant earthworms (“The Earth Moved”), poisonous bouquets (“Flower Confidential”), toxic vegetation (“Wicked Plants”) and lethal insects (“Wicked Bugs”). ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/0830-BKS-Powers/0830-BKS-Powers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 848, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/0830-BKS-Powers/0830-BKS-Powers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 848}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/0830-BKS-Powers/0830-BKS-Powers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/0830-BKS-Powers/0830-BKS-Powers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1449, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '