e final volume of Amitav Ghosh’s trilogy all have something to hide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To read Amitav Ghosh’s “Flood of Fire” is to enter a world of sepoys, sahibs and rajahs, traveling with them from Assam to Calcutta to Canton, all the while learning about their pasts and dreading or hoping for their futures. It is a fictional journey both physical and temporal and, like real journeys, best appreciated when one is willing to accept detours and adventures.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30Lalami/30Lalami-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30Lalami/30Lalami-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30Lalami/30Lalami-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30Lalami/30Lalami-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1267, 'width': 1887, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30Lalami/30Lalami-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30Lalami/30Lalami-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/books/review/30Lalami/30Lalami-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height'