anies', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pritzker, Penny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Club for Growth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-26T21:15:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86b755f9-6104-55dc-952a-98be7c65dc0b', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86b755f9-6104-55dc-952a-98be7c65dc0b'}, {'abstract': 'The Weeknd is a slightly nicer, and much more firmly structured, songwriter on his new album which has echoes of Michael Jackson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/27/arts/music/review-the-weeknd-makes-a-bid-for-pop-outreach-on-a-new-album.html', 'snippet': 'The Weeknd is a slightly nicer, and much more firmly structured, songwriter on his new album which has echoes of Michael Jackson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abel Tesfaye, the Canadian songwriter who calls himself the Weeknd, used to be pop’s bleakest, creepiest Don Juan. The come-ons he sang in his high, sweet tenor — and in the scratchy moan that sometimes replaced it — were more like warning labels. They detailed how loveless, drugged-out, callous, self-destructive and self-absorbed he could be. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/27WEEKEND/27WEEKEND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 498, 'width': 498, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/27WEEKEND/27WEEKEND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 498, 'width': 498, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/27WEEKEND/27WEEKEND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/27WEEKEND/27WEEKEND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/27WEEKEND/27WEEKEND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: The Weeknd Makes a Bid for Pop Outreach on ‘Beauty Behind the Madness’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prince of Pain Moves Toward King of Pop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tesfaye, Abel (Weeknd)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-26T21:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizatio