nal': 'By Sridhar Pappu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sridhar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pappu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/535315d5-7a39-50c8-b23a-440e4b673d13', 'word_count': 1897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/535315d5-7a39-50c8-b23a-440e4b673d13'}, {'abstract': 'Agathe Snow, a darling of the downtown New York art scene, resurrected a fête from 10 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/27/fashion/the-24-hour-party-at-the-guggenheim.html', 'snippet': 'Agathe Snow, a darling of the downtown New York art scene, resurrected a fête from 10 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years ago, Agathe Snow, a darling of the downtown New York art scene, gave a 24-hour party. More than 300 artists and creative types gathered to dance in a grimy loft on Ann Street in Lower Manhattan that was still tinged by the Sept. 11 attack. Ms. Snow filmed the entire affair.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 24-Hour Party at the Guggenheim', 'kicker': 'Scene City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Their Night/Day at the Museum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Katie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snow, Agathe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-26T22:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Rogers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rogers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a5bcb2f-c5d1-58ab-b5af-e2e6af854d03', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a5bcb2f-c5d1-58ab-b5af-e2e6af854d03'}, {'abstract': 'Lacoste is offering clothes and tennis lessons; the debut Gabriela Hearst collection is available; a Billy Reid sample sale; and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/27/fashion/shopping-events-and-sales-happening-this-week-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Lacoste is offering clothes and tennis lessons; the debut Gabriela Hearst collection is available; a Billy Reid sample sale; and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lacoste has a store event at 541 Broadway on Thursday from 6 to 8 p.m. where you can meet the tennis player John Isner and shop for gear like a polo with zippered collar in striped ultradry pique ($90) and a pleated tennis skirt ($90) in support of the City Parks Foundation. On Sunday, it will host a clinic from noon to 2 p.m. with free tennis instruction by the Lacoste player Murphy Jensen, snacks and prizes; Central Park Tennis Courts, Central Park West and 96th Street.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/fashion/27SCOUT1/27SCOUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/27/fashion/27SCOUT1/27SCOUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/fashion/27SCOUT1/27SCOUT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url