with an Eighth Symphony with the London Symphony Orchestra.) You would hope that the new performances and recordings would automatically supersede the old ones, but this first disc does not necessarily bear that out. Abravanel’s 1974 First Symphony, as remembered, relies perhaps a bit too much on sheer nervous energy, but it is also more respectful of the subtleties of Mahler’s score. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/MAHLER/MAHLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/MAHLER/MAHLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 875}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/MAHLER/MAHLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 703, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/MAHLER/MAHLER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1713, 'width': 1175, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/MAHLER/MAHLER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/MAHLER/MAHLER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/arts/MAHLER/MAHLER-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Playlist: Mahler and Killer Tuba Songs', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_