d backpacks, swing into Engine 1 and hurtle out the door in almost a single motion, a blast of red lights and caterwauling sirens. More often than not, there is no fire.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/us/21sanfranciscoweb1/21sanfranciscoweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/21/us/21sanfranciscoweb1/21sanfranciscoweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/us/21sanfranciscoweb1/21sanfranciscoweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/us/21sanfranciscoweb1/21sanfranciscoweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/us/21sanfranciscoweb1/21sanfranciscoweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/21/us/21sanfranciscoweb1/21sanfranciscoweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/21/us/21sanfranciscoweb1/21sanfranciscoweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'San Francisco Firefighters Become Unintended Safety Net for the Homeless', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Responding to Homelessness More Than Fires', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nir, Sarah Maslin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-27T00:40:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34be2ddf-981d-5e16-848c-603774ef9ab7', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34be2ddf-981d-5e16-848c-603774ef9ab7'}, {'abstract': 'The other cub appears to be healthy and officials are optimistic it will survive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/27/us/smaller-of-panda-cub-twins-dies-at-the-national-zoo.html', 'snippet': 'The other cub appears to be healthy and officials are optimistic it will survive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The smaller of twin giant panda cubs, who faced long odds for survival after it was born at the National Zoo in Washington on Saturday, died on Wednesday despite round-the-clock efforts to help the mother with the difficult task of balancing two babies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/us/26WATCHING-panda/26WATCHING-panda-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/26/us/26WATCHING-panda/26WATCHING-panda-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/us/26WATCHING-panda/26WATCHING-panda-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/us/26WATCHING-panda/26WATCHING-panda-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1542, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/us/26WATCHING-panda/26WATCHING-panda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/26/us/26WATCHING-panda/26WATCHING-panda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/26/us/26WATCHING-panda/26WATCHING-panda-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Smaller of Panda Cub Twins Dies at the National Zoo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smaller Panda Cub Dies; Twin Is Doing Well', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pandas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian National Zoological Park', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-27T00:47:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Victor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Victor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a0c125b-ab45-501d-b1dc-c80a351ee0d6', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a0c125b-ab45-501d-b1dc-c80a351ee0d6'}, {'abstract': 'King Salman will visit the White House next week for the first time since ascending to the throne, Saudi officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/27/world/middleeast/saudi-arabia-king-plans-to-visit-us.html', 'snippet': 'King Salman will visit the White House next week for the first time since ascending to the throne, Saudi officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' King Salman will visit the White House next week for the first time since ascending to the throne, Saudi officials said, as part of a trip intended to patch over differences with President Obama over the Iran nuclear agreement. While White House officials refused to confirm the Sept. 4 visit, John Kirby, a State Department spokesman, said Wednesday that he would not contradict an announcement on the trip by the Saudi authorities. “If the Saudi government announced it, I’m certainly not in any position to characterize it any other way,” Mr. Kirby said. King Salman, who became king in January, pulled out of a summit meeting with Persian Gulf leaders at Camp David in May. The Saudis have been concerned about the Iran accord but endorsed it three weeks ago, along with other Gulf states, after receiving assurances from American officials. Prem G. Kumar, a Middle East expert at the Albright Stonebridge Group, said the Saudis’ biggest concern was “how the U.S. will counter Iran’s destabilizing behavior in the Middle East.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saudi Arabia: King Plans to Visit U.S.', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Saudi Arabia: King Plans to Visit U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salman, King of Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirby, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-27T00:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa7d5ea9-ecfb-59e2-8e38-d6a3f8f008b7', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa7d5ea9-ecfb-59e2-8e38-d6a3f8f008b7'}, {'abstract': 'An effort by Chinese officials to limit the influence of religion has raised concerns about encroachment on the city’s autonomy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/27/world/asia/hong-kong-christian-groups-feel-new-scrutiny-from-mainland.html', 'snippet': 'An effort by Chinese officials to limit the influence of religion has raised concerns about encroachment on the city’s autonomy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — For years, the Rev. Philip Woo, the feisty leader of a small Protestant church here, has delighted in testing the limits of China’s restrictive laws on religion. From his perch in Hong Kong, he has delivered fiery sermons on human rights, led seminars