7a-8b00-b9178520bcfd'}, {'abstract': 'This Netflix series tells the story of the ruthless Medellín cartel, which ruled the international cocaine trade in the 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/28/arts/television/review-narcos-follows-the-rise-and-reign-of-pablo-escobar.html', 'snippet': 'This Netflix series tells the story of the ruthless Medellín cartel, which ruled the international cocaine trade in the 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The small screen offers plenty of post-Vietnam, pre-Sept. 11 nostalgia these days, but don’t expect a warm and fuzzy feeling from “Narcos,” an irresistible drama that begins streaming Friday on Netflix. Expect instead a reminder of a time when a few lawless men did a lot of societal damage by spreading cocaine far and wide.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28NARCOS1/28NARCOS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28NARCOS1/28NARCOS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28NARCOS1/28NARCOS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28NARCOS1/28NARCOS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28NARCOS1/28NARCOS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28NARCOS1/28NARCOS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28NARCOS1/28NARCOS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Narcos’ Follows the Rise and Reign of Pablo Escobar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cocaine Kingpin’s Iron Fist and Multiple Ambitions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moura, Wagner', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Escobar, Pablo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Padilha, Jose', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Narcos (TV Program)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-27T12:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/20c5a0c2-6c0f-50d1-b45f-280ca9af95fe', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20c5a0c2-6c0f-50d1-b45f-280ca9af95fe'}, {'abstract': '“Bend It Like Beckham: The Musical,” with its focus of dreams of the future, has many parallels to “Billy Elliot: The Musical.” Then, also in London, there is the Hitler-era “Grand Hotel.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/27/london-theater-journal-make-em-dream/', 'snippet': '“Bend It Like Beckham: The Musical,” with its focus of dreams of the future, has many parallels to “Billy Elliot: The Musical.” Then, also in London, there is the Hitler-era “Grand Hotel.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — When a show talks about dreaming as much as “Bend It Like Beckham: The Musical” does, a theatergoer can start to feel drowsy. This family-friendly hit, which opened at the Phoenix Theater in June, begins with an open-faced young woman named Jess (Natalie Dew) in a soccer jersey looking, well, dreamy as she croons about how people “say that I’m a dreamer” and “that wishing for the moon will never get me anywhere.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/theater/27bend/27bend-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/27/theater/27bend/27bend-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/theater/27bend/27bend-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/theater/27bend/27bend-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/theater/27bend/27bend-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/27/theater/27bend/27bend-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'captio