 Rudolph Schindler’s 1939 Mackey Apartments, where the artists are housed for six months, is a 0.65:1 scale replica of the famous Loos Bar in Vienna.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-artlos/26tmag-artlos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-artlos/26tmag-artlos-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-artlos/26tmag-artlos-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-artlos/26tmag-artlos-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-artlos/26tmag-artlos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-artlos/26tmag-artlos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-artlos/26tmag-artlos-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In L.A., a Cheaply Constructed Pop-Up Bar That’s a Work of Art', 'kicker': 'Drinks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Bar (Los Angeles, Calif, Bar)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-27T13:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marissa Gluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0845100f-4958-5a65-ac98-548b2ca8d613', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0845100f-4958-5a65-ac98-548b2ca8d613'}, {'abstract': 'This ambitious contemporary music program offers nine works in either world or New York premieres.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/30/arts/music/bargemusics-here-and-now-labor-day-festival.html', 'snippet': 'This ambitious contemporary music program offers nine works in either world or New York premieres.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The week leading up to Labor Day is typically the least-scheduled stretch in New York’s classical music season. But the intrepid Bargemusic, Brooklyn’s floating recital hall, always steps into the brink with a gala program. It does so this week with “Here and Now Labor Day Festival,” an ambitious contemporary music program, repeated four times, offering nine works in either world or New York premieres. There are premieres of two pieces by Dalit Warshaw; a solo cello Soliloquy by Andrew Rudin; David Del Tredici’s Duo for Violin and Cello (“To Be Sung on the Water”); Richard Sussman’s Trio for Violin, Piano and Laptop; and David Taylor’s Concertino for Bass Trombone and Trio. Works by Morton Subotnick, John Zorn and Gordon Beeferman receive New York premieres. Among the enticing roster of 11 performers are the pianist Kathleen Supové, the violinist Jennifer Choi and the bassoonist Peter Kolkay. (8 p.m., Wednesday, Friday and Saturday, with a final performance next Sunday at 4 p.m., bargemusic.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/30GUIDE1/30GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/30GUIDE1/30GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/30GUIDE1/30GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/30GUIDE1/30GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/30GUIDE1/30GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/30GUIDE1/30GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/arts/30GUIDE1/30GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bargemusic’s ‘Here and Now Labor Day Festival’', 'kicker': 'Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Premieres for Summer’s End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'ran