anchise-in-a-single-bound.html', 'snippet': 'How directors of independent films make the franchise leap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Independent film for decades has been seen as a way for directors to hold the greatest creative control over their projects. They work with meager means to create something close to their hearts, without the crushing pressure for it to be a global financial success. But having little or no cash to make art can be difficult, so many directors see indies as a steppingstone to the mainstream, a calling card to show studios how their intimate ideas could translate to big-budget projects. That may mean making a number of small films, then a climb up the studio ladder.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/30first-films-image/07TREVORROWJP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/30first-films-image/07TREVORROWJP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/30first-films-image/07TREVORROWJP2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 559, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/30first-films-image/07TREVORROWJP2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1118, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/30first-films-image/30first-films-image-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/