n.html', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn restaurant offers Caribbean cuisine that will have you believing that food is a matter urgent for the soul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cross-shape sign says, “Jesus Saves,” or almost: The first S has fallen away. All along this stretch of Rogers Avenue in Crown Heights, Brooklyn, battered-looking storefronts speak of miracles and end times. So the Food Sermon, standing on a corner with its windows shining and its name in letters as yellow as the noon sun, may be mistaken at first for a sleeker, more modern place of worship.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Food Sermon, Keeping the Faith in Crown Heights', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping the Faith in Crown Heights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crown Heights (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food Sermon (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-27T15:20:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/429949a3-6595-5e20-94f4-cf70fb05f9f7', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/429949a3-6595-5e20-94f4-cf70fb05f9f7'}, {'abstract': 'The rapper Tyler, the Creator has been barred from the United Kingdom, which claimed that his music potentially “encourages violence and intolerance of homosexuality.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/27/tyler-the-c