', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE ASSOCIATED PRESS', 'person': [], 'organization': 'THE ASSOCIATED PRESS'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c4f0bade-b111-5514-9292-f71db0c302f1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c4f0bade-b111-5514-9292-f71db0c302f1'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday, during a speech in Greenville, S.C., he deployed a new prop: a copy of The New York Times, from which he read, on and off, for about eight minutes — alternately praising and mocking a front-page story about him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/08/27/donald-trumps-latest-target-the-new-york-times/', 'snippet': 'On Thursday, during a speech in Greenville, S.C., he deployed a new prop: a copy of The New York Times, from which he read, on and off, for about eight minutes — alternately praising and mocking a front-page story about him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theatricality is a staple of Donald J. Trump’s campaign events. On Thursday, during a speech in Greenville, S.C., he deployed a new prop: a copy of The New York Times, from which he read, on and off, for about eight minutes — alternately praising and mocking a front-page article about him. When he was done, Mr. Trump dramatically flung the newspaper into the air, allowing it to slowly descend over the audience. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump’s Latest Target: The New York Times', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-27T18:47:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad6830ac-e319-5549-88f5-13cdc0f1341b', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad6830ac-e319-5549-88f5-13cdc0f1341b'}, {'abstract': 'Donald J. Trump brought his free-association presidential campaign to Greenville, S.C., even inviting a woman in the crowd to pull on his hair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/08/27/pull-on-my-hair-donald-trump-says-i-dont-wear-a-toupee/', 'snippet': 'Donald J. Trump brought his free-association presidential campaign to Greenville, S.C., even inviting a woman in the crowd to pull on his hair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald J. Trump brought his free-association presidential campaign to Greenville, S.C., on Thursday, following up a cavalier reference to the “silent majority” that supports him with an annotated reading of a New York Times front-page article about him and then with an invitation to a woman in the crowd to yank his hair (“I don’t wear a toupee — it’s my hair”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/us/politics/27firstdraft-trump-sub/27firstdraft-trump-sub-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/27/us/politics/27firstdraft-trump-sub/27firstdraft-trump-sub-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/us/politics/27firstdraft-trump-sub/27firstdraft-trump-sub-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 1024, 'subType'