ng on a different Mexican regional cuisine. The fifth, Tacombi West Village, opens on the corner of Bleecker and Cornelia streets in September. Wolos and his chef, Jason DeBriere — who honed his kitchen chops at restaurants Washington Park, Barbuto and Peels — traveled throughout the Yucatán, stopping at roadside stands and markets in search of dishes and flavors they could bring back to New York. “We wanted to focus and bring these flavors from the Yucatán, because there wasn’t a lot of representation,” DeBriere says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-tacombi/27tmag-tacombi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-tacombi/27tmag-tacombi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-tacombi/27tmag-tacombi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-tacombi/27tmag-tacombi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-tacombi/27tmag-tacombi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-tacombi/27tmag-tacombi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/27/t-magazine/27tmag-tacombi/27tmag-tacombi-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Mexican Restaurant That Doesn’t Skimp on the Spice', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New, Yucatán-Focused Outpost From Tacombi’s Dario Wolos and Jason DeBriere', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tacombi West Village (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-27T21:53:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Binlot', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Binlot', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15aeca57-3a92-5ffc-a4a7-a89d159efbd9', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15aeca57-3a92-5ffc-a4a7-a89d159efbd9'}, {'abstract': 'This exhibition at the Metropolitan Museum of Art presents 40 works that form a freewheeling introduction to staged photography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/28/arts/design/review-grand-illusions-showcases-deceptive-photography.html', 'snippet': 'This exhibition at the Metropolitan Museum of Art presents 40 works that form a freewheeling introduction to staged photography.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Grand Illusions: Staged Photography From the Met Collection” is a small, choice, concentrated exhibition. Ensconced in modest galleries at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, its 40 works are drawn entirely from that museum’s collection and form a freewheeling introduction to staged photography. This tactic — arranging objects or people for the camera — began with photography’s invention; figured prominently in portraiture, commercial and Surrealist lines of work; and entered mainstream art full throttle in the 1980s, with the arrival of the Pictures Generation and postmodernism. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28ILLUSIONS1/28ILLUSIONS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28ILLUSIONS1/28ILLUSIONS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28ILLUSIONS1/28ILLUSIONS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28ILLUSIONS1/28ILLUSIONS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28ILLUSIONS1/28ILLUSIONS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28ILLUSIONS1/28ILLUSIONS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/arts/28ILLUSIONS1/28ILLUSIONS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Grand Illusions’ Showcases Deceptive Photography', 'kicker': 