a-c69aac48410c'}, {'abstract': 'A conversation with Matthias C. Hühne, the author of “Airline Visual Identity, 1945-1975,” a collection of hundreds of vivid and colorful posters from the golden age of flying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/30/travel/american-airlines-posters.html', 'snippet': 'A conversation with Matthias C. Hühne, the author of “Airline Visual Identity, 1945-1975,” a collection of hundreds of vivid and colorful posters from the golden age of flying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In more ways than one, “Airline Visual Identity, 1945-1975” (Callisto Publishing) is a hefty piece of work, landing at 430 pages, weighing 14 pounds and selling for $400. But the true size of its ambition is how it reveals the optimism of the Jet Age through nearly 400 posters and images from airlines like Pan Am, TWA, and United, evoking a time now seen as the golden age of flying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Airlines Looked Cool and Showed It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Posters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trans World Airlines (TWA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pan American World Airways', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-27T22:10:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization':