le/d2d6ff7a-3d06-5fab-8980-f0de29ee6131'}, {'abstract': 'High-stakes testing isn’t the only problem, and it’s time for schools to change their approach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/28/opinion/how-common-core-can-help-in-the-battle-of-skills-vs-knowledge.html', 'snippet': 'High-stakes testing isn’t the only problem, and it’s time for schools to change their approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington — STANDARDIZED tests are commonly blamed for narrowing the school curriculum to reading and math. That’s one reason Congress is considering changes in the law that could lead states to put less emphasis on test scores. But even if we abolished standardized tests tomorrow, a majority of elementary schools would continue to pay scant attention to subjects like history and science.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/opinion/28Wexler/28Wexler-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/28/opinion/28Wexler/28Wexler-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/opinion/28Wexler/28Wexler-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/opinion/28Wexler/28Wexler-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1138, 'width': 1626, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/opinion/28Wexler/28Wexler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail