pg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/sports/29FISH1/29FISH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/sports/29FISH1/29FISH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/28/sports/29FISH1/29FISH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/sports/29FISH1/29FISH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Saying Farewell at U.S. Open, Mardy Fish Intends to Stay for a While', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Last Stop: Flushing Meadows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Mardy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McEnroe, Patrick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-28T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Robson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04a0b5ff-d2db-5594-ba25-b010d4655959', 'word_count': 1298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04a0b5ff-d2db-5594-ba25-b010d4655959'}, {'abstract': 'Selected by Natasha Trethewey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/30/magazine/mirror-memory.html', 'snippet': 'Selected by Natasha Trethewey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cultural memory often involves a good measure of willed forgetting, an overlooking of some parts of experience in favor of a dominant narrative. In this poem, the precise imagery of faces reflected in a kettle — “misted and revealed” — hints at how these subjects are at once obscured and plainly seen. Here, the memory of people who are often left out of history is set against the imagery of the painting, connected by the single long sentence from which the poem is made.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/magazine/30poem/30mag-30poem-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 265, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/30/magazine/30poem/30mag-30poem-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 265}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/magazine/30poem/30mag-30poem-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/magazine/30poem/30mag-30poem-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 904, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/magazine/30poem/30mag-30poem-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/30/magazine/30poem/30mag-30poem-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/magazine/30poem/30mag-30poem-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Mirror. Memory’', 'kicker': 'Poem', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mirror. Memory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trethewey, Natasha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boland, Eavan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-28T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eavan Boland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eavan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65e11559-28e0-5322-9155-88fad322d4f2', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65e11559-28e0-5322-9155-88fad322d4f2'}, {'abstract': 'An alliance of newspaper and magazine publishers has taken an increasingly active role in fighting the growing dominance of the tech giant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/29/technology/european-publishers-play-lobbying-role-against-google.html', 'snippet': 'An alliance of newspaper and magazine publishers has taken an increasingly active role in fighting the growing dominance of the tech giant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — In private sessions this summer, giant publishers and media companies from Germany, France and elsewhere have met with European officials about proposals to regulate Europe’s digital economy. The discussions have covered a broad range of contentious issues, according to public disclosures and several people who attended or were briefed on the meetings. Central to almost all of them has been limiting the reach of a single American company: Google.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/business/28eupublishers-web1/28eupublishers-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/28/business/28eupublishers-web1/28eupublishers-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/business/28eupublishers-web1/28eupublishers-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/business/28eupublishers-web1/28eupublishers-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/business/28eupublishers-web1/28eupublishers-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/28/business/28eupublishers-web1/28eupublishers-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/28/business/28eupublishers-web1/28eupublishers-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'European Publishers Play Lobbying Role Against Google', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aiming to Bring Google to Heel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-28T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott and Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7105c960-c00e-5a3c-837c-b5355b7c46a3', 'word_count': 1676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7105c960-c00e-5a3c-837c-b5355b7c46a3'}, {'abstract': 'The Albanian capital’s brightly colored buildings and palpable energy are indicative of the long way the capital has come since the fall of its Communist regime in 1991.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/30/travel/tirana-restaurants-bars.html', 'snippet': 'The Albanian capital’s brightly colored buildings and palpable energy are indicative of the long way the capital has come since the fall of its Communist regime in 1991.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You begin to understand Tirana, the capital of Albania, the first time you try to cross the city’s main road, which locals simply refer to as Boulevard. There are zebra-striped crosswalks, and cars stop if they must, but the feat is something akin to stage diving into a free-form automotive ballet. Confidence is the operative word here — coupled with an understanding that Albanians live by a rhythmic, improvisational code: Fill space when it’s free.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/travel/30ALBANIA5/30ALBANIA5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/30/travel/30ALBANIA5/30ALBANIA5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/travel/30ALBANIA5/30ALBANIA5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/travel/30ALBANIA5/30ALBANIA5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/travel/30ALBANIA5/30ALBANIA5-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/30/travel/30ALBANIA5/30ALBANIA5-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/30/travel/30ALBANIA5/30ALBANIA5-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tirana, Breaking Free From Communist Past, Is a City Transformed', 'kicker': 'Next Stop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In