 would not render existing television sets obsolete, Mr. Kesten said. The receiver used in the demonstration was of standard type, adjusted to a minor extent and equipped with a simple attachment which can be produced at comparatively small costs, while other tests proved that standard sets without any adjustment would receive black and white images broadcast by the new method. — New York Herald Tribune, August 30, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/29/blogs/29iht-oldaug29-tv/29iht-oldaug29-tv-jumbo.png', 'height': 551, 'width': 427, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/29/blogs/29iht-oldaug29-tv/29iht-oldaug29-tv-superJumbo.png', 'height': 551, 'width': 427, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/29/blogs/29iht-oldaug29-tv/29iht-oldaug29-tv-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/29/blogs/29iht-oldaug29-tv/29iht-oldaug29-tv-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/29/blogs/29iht-oldaug29-tv/29iht-oldaug29-tv-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Color Television to Start Jan. 1', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major'