Portraits of a majority-female South African anti-poaching squad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/28/magazine/on-patrol-with-the-black-mambas.html', 'snippet': 'Portraits of a majority-female South African anti-poaching squad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past two years, the majority-female Black Mamba Anti-Poaching Unit has patrolled the Balule Nature Reserve, a private wildlife reserve in northern South Africa. The Balule has an open border with Kruger National Park, an Israel-size reserve that has in recent years been besieged by poachers in pursuit of the park’s famed wildlife — particularly its rhinoceroses, whose horns are now worth hundreds of thousands of dollars on the international black market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Patrol With the Black Mambas', 'kicker': 'Look', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kruger National Park (South Africa)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-28T19:04:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Photographs by Julia Gunther', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Photographs', 'middlename': 'Julia', 'lastname': 'Gunther', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59567044-7112-58c5-abff-e0e53d1b8512', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59567044-7112-58c5-abff-e0e53d1b8512'}, {'abstract': 'The Sweeney Building, once home to the W.H. Sweeney Manufacturing Company in the Dumbo section of Brooklyn, is now a residential property.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/30/nyregion/the-history-of-the-sweeney-building-in-bro