 overseas, and she’s the subject of a documentary planned by the director Wong Kar-wai.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — When “The Legend of the White Snake” opens Wednesday at the David H. Koch Theater at Lincoln Center, an American audience will get its first glimpse of Zhang Huoding, one of China’s biggest Peking Opera stars, as she makes her United States debut.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31ZHANG/31ZHANG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 558, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31ZHANG/31ZHANG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 558}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31ZHANG/31ZHANG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 952, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31ZHANG/31ZHANG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1487, 'width': 1599, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31ZHANG/31ZHANG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31ZHANG/31ZHANG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31ZHANG/31ZHANG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Zhang Huoding of Peking Opera Takes a Turn in the United States', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chinese Opera Star Takes a Turn in the U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barboza, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Huoding', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peking Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-30T21:32:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95c47c10-1cb8-54ed-a461-fe965975618a', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95c47c10-1cb8-54ed-a461-fe965975618a'}, {'abstract': 'A large and youthful crowd gathered for two song cycles performed by a company that has built a following with its roving, intimate productions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/31/arts/music/review-loftopera-brings-mischief-and-a-crowd-to-berlioz-and-mahler.html', 'snippet': 'A large and youthful crowd gathered for two song cycles performed by a company that has built a following with its roving, intimate productions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ll admit, with a certain degree of shame, that my predominant feeling on Friday night when I entered the Muse, a warehouse deep in Bushwick, Brooklyn, usually used as a circus school, was surprise, even shock. I hadn’t trusted that 10 love songs by Berlioz and Mahler had much power to draw a crowd; after all, lieder has long been opera’s poor relation, and even opera, some say, today struggles to find an audience.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31LOFTOPERA/31LOFTOPERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31LOFTOPERA/31LOFTOPERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31LOFTOPERA/31LOFTOPERA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31LOFTOPERA/31LOFTOPERA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31LOFTOPERA/31LOFTOPERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31LOFTOPERA/31LOFTOPERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/arts/31LOFTOPERA/31LOFTOPERA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: LoftOpera Brings Mischief, and a Crowd, to Berlioz and Mahler', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bringing Some Mischief, and a Crowd, to Unlikely Song Cycles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LoftOpera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 