rating his 2008 album, “808s & Heartbreak,” at the Hollywood Bowl next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/31/arts/music/kanye-west-to-perform-an-808s-concert.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. West will perform a one-off concert celebrating his 2008 album, “808s & Heartbreak,” at the Hollywood Bowl next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kanye West will perform a one-off concert celebrating his 2008 album, “808s & Heartbreak,” at the Hollywood Bowl next month. That album, which featured heavy use of auto-tune and synthesizers, did not receive universal acclaim upon release but now is regarded as a pivotal influence on current hip-hop and R&B stars, including Drake, the Weeknd and Future. “\xa0 ‘808s & Heartbreak’ sounds like none of his other albums, nor any rap album of note,” Jon Caramanica wrote in his review for The Times. “At best, it is a rough sketch for a great album.” Mr. West later described it as “the first black new wave album” in an interview with Mr. Caramanica. The concert will take place on Sept. 25. Tickets go on sale Friday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kanye West to Perform an ‘808s’ Concert', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kanye West to Perform an ‘808s’ Concert', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-30T22:23:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Andrew R. Chow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Chow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief',