he lengthy preparation destroys, rather than enhances, academic ability. Student enthusiasm and curiosity are crushed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking the Grip of the Gaokao, China’s SAT', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SAT (College Admission Test)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-31T16:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36672888-ce82-56f9-85c7-0a2a08038986', 'word_count': 2104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36672888-ce82-56f9-85c7-0a2a08038986'}, {'abstract': 'The German chancellor warned that the Continent’s open-border policy was at risk unless all European countries showed an equal willingness to help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/09/01/world/europe/germany-migrants-merkel.html', 'snippet': 'The German chancellor warned that the Continent’s open-border policy was at risk unless all European countries showed an equal willingness to help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Faced with a humanitarian crisis that shows no signs of letting up, Chancellor Angela Merkel gave her fellow Germans and other Europeans a pep talk on Monday, praising those assisting the thousands seeking asylum here but warning that the Continent’s open-border policy was at risk unless all European countries showed an equal willingness to help.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/world/01germany-web/01germany-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/09/01/world/01germany-web/01germany-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/world/01germany-web/01germany-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/world/01germany-web/01germany-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/world/01germany-web/01germany-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/09/01/world/01germany-web/01germany-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/world/01germany-web/01germany-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Angela Merkel Calls for European Unity to Address Migrant Influx', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-31T16:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f49aa279-b7b0-5f0f-9644-552100bdad54', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f49aa279-b7b0-5f0f-9644-552100bdad54'}, {'abstract': 'The tea specialist says her four tiles of highly prized pu-erh tea are too precious to drink.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/09/02/dining/pu-erh-tea-kathy-y-l-chan.html', 'snippet': 'The tea specialist says her four tiles of highly prized pu-erh tea are too precious to drink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, a member of a private tea society in Shanghai presented Kathy YL Chan with a small box as slender as a cigarette case. Inside were four tiles of highly prized pu-erh tea, conjoined like a chocolate bar and almost black, twined with green and ocher.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mu