 nightlife entrepreneur Jayma Cardoso has been involved in a handful of high-profile Manhattan projects: SoHo’s GoldBar, Lavo in Midtown. But none is unmistakably hers as the Surf Lodge, the Montauk mainstay now wrapping up its sold-out eighth season: like the hotel, Cardoso is unfussy and welcoming, with an accent left over from her native Brazil and a throaty laugh she deploys often.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Montauk Home Where the Windows Are Always Open', 'kicker': 'Home and Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montauk (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cardoso, Jayma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-31T16:19:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandria Symonds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Symonds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d08cbe0-4297-52cb-b1dc-9763c9b5c4b9', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d08cbe0-4297-52cb-b1dc-9763c9b5c4b9'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Rob Portman called the renaming “another example of the President going around Congress,” but he hasn’t always felt that Congress should concern itself with names.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/31/denalis-name-change-upsets-a-senator/', 'snippet': 'Senator Rob Portman called the renaming “another example of the President going around Congress,” but he hasn’t always felt that Congress should concern itself with names.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I know it’s a tricky thing to expect consistency from politicians, but I was struck by Senator Rob Portman’s indignation at President Obama’s decision to change the name of Mount McKinley in Alaska back to Denali, which is the name that local Native Americans gave it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/opinion/31rosenthalWEB/31rosenthalWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/31/opinion/31rosenthalWEB/31rosenthalWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/opinion/31rosenthalWEB/31rosenthalWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/opinion/31rosenthalWEB/31rosenthalWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/opinion/31rosenthalWEB/31rosenthalWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/31/opinion/31rosenthalWEB/31rosenthalWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/31/opinion/31rosenthalWEB/31rosenthalWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Denali’s Name Change Upsets a Senator', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Geographical', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKinley, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portman, Rob', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mount McKinley (Alaska)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-31T16:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4016e5ce-af3b-5b69-9e5b-8a3e493198ac', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4016e5ce-af3b-5b69-9e5b-8a3e493198ac'}, {'abstract': 'Miley Cyrus talks drugs, Caitlyn Jenner and being in love with an astronaut.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/08/31/the-long-winding-interview-with-miley-cyrus/', 'snippet': 'Miley Cyrus talks drugs, Caitlyn Jenner and being in love with an astronaut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last night, after hosting the MTV Video Music Awards in a typical polarizing performance, Miley Cyrus surprise-released a free, 23-track new album, “Miley Cyrus & Her Dead Petz,” written and recorded largely at her home with members of the Flaming Lips. In a five-hour interview the previous weekend, Ms. Cyrus, 22, discussed the experimental project, which you can read about here. But along the way, she also touched on her budding friendship with Caitlyn Jenner, learning about herself through drugs, and how she’s learned to handle the media. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/music/01artsbeat-miley/01artsbeat-miley-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 856, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/music/01artsbeat-miley/01artsbeat-miley-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 856}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/music/01artsbeat-miley/01artsbeat-miley-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 718, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/music/01artsbeat-miley/01artsbeat-miley-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1436, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/music/01artsbeat-miley/01artsbeat-miley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/music/01artsbeat-miley/01artsbeat-miley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im