': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The Soviet Union dismisses an American proposal on non-proliferation in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA\xa0— The Soviet Union formally rejected today [Aug. 31] the American-proposed disarmament treaty which was designed to try to halt the spread of nuclear weapons. Soviet delegate Semyon K. Tsarapkin told the 17-nation disarmament conference the U.S. treaty draft presented Aug. 17 was unacceptable even as a basis for discussion. He described the draft as a cynical Western attempt to admit West Germany to the nuclear club by the back door. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, September 1, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Russia Rejects U.S. Proposal', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMS CONTROL AND LIMITATION AND DISARMAMENT', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-31T16:52:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db0db905-f224-5b32-bdd3-95b5312ed51a', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db0db905-f224-5b32-bdd3-95b5312ed51a'}, {'abstract': 'What was striking about Dr. Sacks was his capacity for enthusiasm about whatever idea or object had caught his attention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/09/01/science/oliver-sacks-diverse-elements-in-harmony.html', 'snippet': 'What was striking about Dr. Sacks was his capacity for enthusiasm about whatever idea or object had caught his attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2001, shortly after his book, “Uncle Tungsten: Memories of a Chemical Boyhood,” was published, I asked Dr. Oliver Sacks which of the chemical elements he had written about was his favorite.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/science/01SACKS/01SACKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/09/01/science/01SACKS/01SACKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/science/01SACKS/01SACKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/science/01SACKS/01SACKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1302, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/science/01SACKS/01SACKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/09/01/science/01SACKS/01SACKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/science/01SACKS/01SACKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oliver Sacks: Diverse Elements in Harmony', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diverse Elements in Harmony', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sacks, Oliver', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Awakenings (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-31T16:54:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9960fb7d-a57a-58ce-beb2-2ead7407a832', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9960fb7d-a57a-58ce-beb2-2ead7407a832'}, {'abstract': 'Plus: Lithuanian honey liqueur, Moroccan sauces and a Puerto Rican food festival bring a range of flavors, and a Vermont inn is ready to serve you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/09/02/dining/challah-and-brisket-rethought-for-rosh-hashana.html', 'snippet': 'Plus: Lithuanian honey liqueur, Moroccan sauces and a Puerto Rican food festival bring a range of flavors, and a Vermont inn is ready to serve you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most challah is made from wheat flour. But rye, barley, spelt and oats may also be used according to Jewish law. This year, in time for Rosh Hashana, Breads Bakery is using a mixture of spelt and wheat to make a handsome and tasty round loaf. It is not kosher. The gluten- and dairy-free By the Way Bakery is making challah primarily from oat flour, under rabbinical supervision, so it’s kosher and pareve. It is baked in a ring shape and is dense and thickly studded with raisins for a bread that’s earthy and sweet: Spelt challah, $8.50, beginning Friday at Breads Bakery, 18 East 16th Street, and Breads Bakery kiosk in Bryant Park, breadsbakery.com; oat challah, $12, Sept. 11, 13, 18, 21 and 22 from By the Way Bakery, 2442 Broadway (90th Street); 574 Warburton Avenue, Hastings-on-Hudson, N.Y., BTWBakery.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/02/dining/02BURNER9/02BURNER9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/09/02/dining/02BURNER9/02BURNER9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/02/dining/02BURNER9/02BURNER9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/02/dining/02BURNER9/02BURNER9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1481, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/02/dining/02BURNER9/02BURNER9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/09/02/dining/02BURNER9/02BURNER9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/02/dining/02BURNER9/02BURNER9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Challah and Brisket, R