11', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb3e9606-8153-57d5-80e5-d9526bcd7411'}, {'abstract': 'A hotel housed in a 19th-century building toes the line between classic and modern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/31/t-magazine/casa-bonay-hotel-barcelona.html', 'snippet': 'A hotel housed in a 19th-century building toes the line between classic and modern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite not being particularly known for its contemporary art scene or flashy architectural projects, Barcelona is one of those rare cities that somehow always feels up to date. The same, however, can’t be said for its hotels, which are either Old World-stodgy or genera-minimalist. But the affordable new Casa Bonay, located in a stately, sun-washed 1869 building in the city’s central, semi-industrial Dreta de l’Eixample neighborhood, is changing that. The co-owner Inés Miró-Sans, who worked with the Brooklyn-based design firm Studio Tack to restore the space without destroying its 19th-century charms, preserved as many details as she could, from old fireplaces to the mosaic floors, while keeping the feeling super simple.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '98', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-bonay-t-1/13tmag-09look_bonay-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-bonay-t-1/13tmag-09look_bonay-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-bonay-t-1/13tmag-09look_bonay-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20