ysics, the other with a look at her parents’ divorce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/09/01/arts/dance/review-atomic-orbital-and-midway-avenue-examining-electrons-and-memories.html', 'snippet': 'Laura Peterson and Nichole Canuso share a bill at Here, one with a dance nodding to quantum physics, the other with a look at her parents’ divorce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Choreography may not be quite as perplexing as quantum mechanics, but it is a mysterious art. “Atomic Orbital,” Laura Peterson’s contribution to a shared program at Here this past weekend, is an abstract dance whose clean lines, attention to detail and complex sense of stage space recall the work of Merce Cunningham. And yet something is missing, the something that makes such abstraction dramatically absorbing. It’s hard to say exactly what that something is. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/01ATOMIC1/01ATOMIC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/01ATOMIC1/01ATOMIC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/01ATOMIC1/01ATOMIC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/01ATOMIC1/01ATOMIC1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/01/arts/01ATOMIC1/01ATOMIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thum