 [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-08-31T22:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7531b18-ec29-5f60-8bb6-c19cd5c014f4', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7531b18-ec29-5f60-8bb6-c19cd5c014f4'}, {'abstract': 'When Oliver Sacks, the neurologist and author, died of a cancer, Times readers took to the online comments section of his obituary to share what he meant to them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/31/insider/an-outpouring-of-reader-reflection-after-the-death-of-oliver-sacks.html', 'snippet': 'When Oliver Sacks, the neurologist and author, died of a cancer, Times readers took to the online comments section of his obituary to share what he meant to them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Oliver Sacks died at age 82 on Sunday, readers flocked to his obituary to pay their respects. Many wrote of their connections to the neurologist as patients, mentees and, largely, as readers. In his essay last February “My Own Life,” Dr. Sacks acknowledged the impact his readers had had on his life, writing, “I have had an intercourse with the world, the special intercourse of writers and readers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/19/arts/19sacks-1-obit/19sacks-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/19/arts/19sacks-1-obit/19sacks-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight':